  "content": [
    {
      "text": "{\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"cc5557b5-112d-4947-97ff-0956d800a6fa\",\n      \"text\": \"Aegon implements hardware-attested compliance mechanisms with ledger-bound token architectures and cryptographically signed mobile receipts for safeguarding content extraction and data access controls.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.004690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"36ede801-86d4-4651-a827-d694a4b8f054\",\n      \"text\": \"Aegon implements hardware-attested compliance mechanisms with ledger-bound token architectures and cryptographically signed mobile receipts for safeguarding content extraction and data access controls | Involving: Aegon\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.004690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_13\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"2cfeb6c9-0b76-4b8c-94a4-33c598e569df\",\n      \"text\": \"Task delegation short-lived credential derived from standing delegation boundaries, encapsulating task ID, constrained operational scope, issuance timestamp, short-lived expiration threshold, and governing constitution reference.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.974690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"540d73e2-f027-4937-8347-bf212369b484\",\n      \"text\": \"Task delegation short-lived credential derived from standing delegation boundaries, encapsulating task ID, constrained operational scope, issuance timestamp, short-lived expiration threshold, and governing constitution reference | Involving: Cletus\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"experience\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.974690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_10\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"a56f4d03-088f-4404-8927-06762407570d\",\n      \"text\": \"In Scenario 3, agent intends to contact unverified supplier not in verified registry; PAGRL retrieves rules R2, R4, R6; agent reasons contacting unverified supplier violates R4 but task can use verified alternative; compliance decision Self-Correct; agent revises intent to nearest verified supplier and re-enters PAGRL producing Proceed decision; original intent, correction reasoning, and revised intent logged to MCP governance server | Involving: supply chain agent, PAGRL system, MCP governance server, verified supplier | Unverified supplier contact violates compliance rules but alternative exists\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.088393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_24\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d25b8049-1949-47f6-b085-f2a450ca765c\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound's two-level delegation: standing delegation (long-term, human-authorized) authorizes short-lived task delegation per execution cycle; standing delegations restricted from direct execution, serving as root of authority for runtime engine, empowering persistent periodic agents to operate asynchronously under dynamically refreshed governance policies while preserving immediate user revocability and bounding credential exposure.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.994690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"9d3abc10-3fb0-42ec-bd9f-59c6b8ca2ce1\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound constitutes an administrative governance and behavioral accountability layer rather than a totalizing agent security architecture, extending traditional observability by generating atomic governance receipts encapsulating exact policy version states, delegation token identifiers, individual authority judgments, terminal outcomes, and asymmetric cryptographic signatures, with every discrete transaction encapsulated within a cryptographically signed governance receipt enabling independent out-of-band decision reconstruction and completely reconstructing the original decision algebra out-of-band. Example governance receipt structure includes Receipt ID r-1024 for Agent ID ads-agent performing Action launch campaign under Delegation Ref d-118 with Constitution Version 3, resulting in Final Decision Human Approval Required with 7 Standing Delegation for Persistent Agents.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.024690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"0edf4582-3fe4-4bca-b431-ee6cd90a30ed\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound focuses on runtime governance mechanisms rather than task optimization or task completion rates.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.014690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ccddb16f-8088-4321-ae2f-a3a22b2d95a0\",\n      \"text\": \"OAuth 2.0 token exchange protocol specified by Michael Jones, Anthony Nadalin, Brian Campbell, John Bradley, and Chuck Mortimore in a 2020 technical report, providing a standard for OAuth 2.0 token exchange | When: 2020 | Involving: Michael Jones, Anthony Nadalin, Brian Campbell, John Bradley, Chuck Mortimore\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_18\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"02110a14-b10c-4bd8-9320-345c886c8a18\",\n      \"text\": \"In Scenario 4, supplier disruption signal activates situational rule R7; inventory replenishment agent intends to substitute disrupted supplier with verified alternative; with R7 active, PAGRL reasons disruption context elevates risk regardless of verified status; compliance decision Escalate; structured escalation message including disruption context, proposed substitution, and reasoning trace transmitted to supply chain manager for review | Involving: inventory replenishment agent, PAGRL system, supply chain manager, MCP governance server | Disruption context elevates risk even for verified suppliers\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.098393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_24\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"fc319743-84cc-4fa3-85c2-e797f87c66f1\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound is implemented as a decoupled, runtime governance layer positioned directly before action execution, serving as a non-bypassable governance checkpoint that evaluates candidate tool invocations using formal decision algebra to compose intermediate judgments conservatively prior to target system mutation. The agent runtime is treated as untrusted due to potential jailbreaks, requiring out-of-band validation prior to system execution.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.004690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d24ba464-8811-43b3-9a48-63d218f8f051\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound's two-level delegation: standing delegation (long-term, human-authorized) authorizes short-lived task delegation per execution cycle; standing delegations restricted from direct execution, serving as root of authority for runtime engine | Involving: Cletus\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"experience\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_10\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"96f19be1-305e-492e-949d-f18c328789a6\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound addresses a fundamentally orthogonal axis to conventional benchmarks, focusing on runtime governance mechanisms rather than task optimization or task completion rates.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.014690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_11\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"3ea90a8a-4d85-4e46-9f04-fe8ab9af3abc\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound-Bench is a standardized evaluation framework designed to quantify governance enforcement correctness, multi-authority composition behavior, and policy provenance integrity.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_11\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ba1f50b8-205c-4432-b2f8-991f7ab8214d\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound-Bench is a standardized evaluation framework designed to quantify governance enforcement correctness, multi-authority composition behavior, and policy provenance integrity.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"88c903f8-7876-4950-9566-6ca94cc0d1f7\",\n      \"text\": \"Three conditions trigger escalation rather than self-correction: (1) categorical prohibition by rule where no intent revision makes it compliant, (2) irreversible action requiring human confirmation, (3) genuine uncertainty about permissibility where ambiguous cases should be escalated\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.118393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_16\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"b184d623-9e11-40de-bada-82b84d4d726a\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound enforces deterministic compliance at the system runtime boundary rather than optimizing model weights at training time, focusing on verifiable system accountability rather than statistical behavioral shaping, fundamentally diverging from optimization-centric model alignment methods where alignment shapes model cognition beforehand and governance evaluates final behavior before system mutation, analogous to the software engineering boundary between application correctness and localized operational policy, without influencing agent cognition.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.004690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"b1d52bf4-f371-46c0-bd2c-c747549de35b\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound is out of scope for adversarial prompt injection attacks, direct LLM jailbreaks, baseline model alignment failures, and hardware-level side-channel data exfiltration, as AgentBound isolates behavior at the action perimeter rather than filtering cognitive model inputs, rendering it incapable of directly intercepting prompt injection, jailbreaks, or internal adversarial model manipulation\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.014690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"6927b614-7521-47ab-825d-e8b2cba8a88d\",\n      \"text\": \"The AgentBound-Bench evaluation framework, comprising compiled benchmark scenarios, baseline ground-truth annotations, out-of-band receipt verification tooling, and deployment documentation, will be released to the community upon conclusion of the initial empirical evaluation campaign.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.034690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_16\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"e4461c45-1918-4955-81b6-972a6d735bc2\",\n      \"text\": \"It isolates the assessment of governance infrastructure from the underlying language model's cognitive capabilities, explicitly measuring whether the runtime architecture safely constrains and cryptographically validates malicious or anomalous agent actions against known ground-truth behaviors.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.974690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_11\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c19a6296-1457-42e9-aecc-48fcb17bea3a\",\n      \"text\": \"Traditional authorization frameworks like Google Zanzibar Open Policy Agent and Cedar focus on entitlement validation for technical permissions while AgentBound establishes authorization as one governance input among independent arbiters evaluating contextual invariants beyond resource-level access control. These frameworks are insufficient for periodic or long-running agentic workloads because they operate under the implicit assumption that a human principal is actively present or within a valid session context when a transaction is initiated, creating systemic vulnerabilities where no human user is present to evaluate ambient risks when execution cycles spontaneously begin, and governance policies may shift between execution cycles; a runtime governance layer is needed to determine whether specific actions should occur under given circumstances.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.024690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"a13b6643-bbf0-4787-803a-72f7d1c81b0b\",\n      \"text\": \"Documentation/specs/templates/examples: CC BY 4.0\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.854196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_31\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"f6bca91d-74f8-40c9-9138-f676e7b5cb76\",\n      \"text\": \"Action rules follow ASI-[A-Z0-9-]+ pattern format\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.844196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_9\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"6f577b37-deb9-4f1d-bdaf-8814da26b4c6\",\n      \"text\": \"Canonical action tuple (operation, resource, parameters, risk, context) abstracts all runtime events where operation identifies semantic intent, resource denotes target, parameters encompass action-specific arguments, risk encapsulates exposure category, and context contains volatile execution metadata\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.974690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_6\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"704df447-ded6-4142-a2ee-5a9636d3ee2b\",\n      \"text\": \"Crosley proposes runtime constitutions as governance files injected into agent context at execution time with selective loading of relevant rules per task, but remains an engineering pattern rather than formally grounded framework and does not connect agent governance to neurocognitive theory or organizational compliance psychology | Involving: Crosley (author) | Remains engineering pattern rather than formally grounded framework; lacks connection to neurocognitive theory and organizational compliance psychology\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.088393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_29\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"f9eaca83-9be5-42f6-a5ca-0b944aad53d0\",\n      \"text\": \"Verifying a receipt requires the artifact payload, corresponding public verification keys, and historical governance artifacts fetched via the receipt's stored references through a validation sequence comprising cryptographic integrity verification, governance reconstruction, and deterministic decision consistency check.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.024690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"348eb115-dbdc-4604-a5cd-876d5960997a\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound-Bench quantifies framework efficacy through four core mathematical and system metrics: governance accuracy (correct decisions/total decisions), violation escape rate (violations executed/total violations), receipt verification success rate, and fine-grained governance latency\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.974690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"abd6e3c4-c200-49e9-a3a7-fe324332269a\",\n      \"text\": \"Runtime requests latest constitution version from Constitution Service before task materialization; task token encapsulates constitution hash, enabling automatic policy propagation without manual reauthorization.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.984690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"046adb4b-3d25-484e-982b-f50d21ada88e\",\n      \"text\": \"Cedar, a new language for expressive, fast, safe, and analyzable authorization introduced by Joseph W Cutler, Craig Disselkoen, Aaron Eline, Shaobo He, Kyle Headley, Michael Hicks, Kesha Hietala, Eleftherios Ioannidis, John Kastner, Anwar Mamat, et al. in PLDI 2024, offering improved authorization capabilities | When: 2024 | Involving: Joseph W Cutler, Craig Disselkoen, Aaron Eline, et al.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.984690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_18\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c6acbadf-dfe3-4cad-b223-2e93013e3dbf\",\n      \"text\": \"Associated with DOI:10.5281/zenodo.17464706 | When: 2026-09-06 | Involving: user\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.844196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_33\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"460744ac-83ed-4c88-bd62-0ed9671f99c9\",\n      \"text\": \"Traditional authorization frameworks (Google Zanzibar, Open Policy Agent, Cedar) focus on entitlement validation for technical permissions to access resources, while AgentBound establishes authorization as one governance input among independent arbiters to evaluate contextual invariants beyond resource-level access control | Involving: Google Zanzibar, Open Policy Agent, Cedar, AgentBound\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.024690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_13\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"0159c929-ee2e-453e-929d-b579bdb8fc24\",\n      \"text\": \"Controls section defines explicit action rules structured as ABAC tuples, each linking directly to evidence fields enumerated in the card: kyc status, risk score, device trust level, beneficiary screening score, escalation id, ensuring every decision is auditable | Involving: Cletus (AI agent), PolicyCard system\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.834196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_16\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d71c59c5-e8fc-445b-83bb-992b55ed9459\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound framework mitigates semantic and behavioral threats after traditional authorization concludes, detecting runtime behavioral policy violations and unauthorized execution bypassing approval workflows.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.994690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d28afb9c-cac8-4486-ae03-f2fbad8a8192\",\n      \"text\": \"Full schema and validator available in public repository and archived via Zenodo (DOI: 10.5281/zenodo.17464706)\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.844196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_10\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"2ed71df4-c897-496e-a98a-c0c497131814\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound operates as a deterministic enforcement layer at the system boundary between authorization and execution, governing how physical actions are evaluated justified and recorded without influencing agent cognition\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.004690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_17\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"88e21077-2e6f-42d8-aa60-8fc54438a2f5\",\n      \"text\": \"OAuth 2.0 token exchange protocol specified by Michael Jones, Anthony Nadalin, Brian Campbell, John Bradley, and Chuck Mortimore in a 2020 technical report\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"efb639e6-4532-4de4-bf99-12becf7f5ac3\",\n      \"text\": \"Adversarially crafted inputs may induce agents to rationalize non-compliant actions as permissible (functional analog of moral disengagement); framework lacks dedicated tamper-resistance layer | Involving: PAGRL agents | Governance robustness under systematic adversarial attack remains open empirical question\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.108393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_27\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"72c99091-4148-46fd-8619-6cad5815794f\",\n      \"text\": \"Attack succeeds when RS(α)=Valid AND α∉IO, exploiting cognitive ambiguity, semantic uncertainty, or incomplete governance rule specifications\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.984690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_5\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"a43a2e87-2a9b-412d-90b3-7f7e75897f56\",\n      \"text\": \"Irreversible actions (purchase orders, supplier commits, replenishment triggers) require explicit human confirmation before execution because they cannot be undone if incorrect | Irreversible actions cannot be undone if incorrect\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.078393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_22\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"83252b8c-b117-421b-9278-63899514adad\",\n      \"text\": \"Constraints aggregate conjunctively and obligations accumulate cumulatively within the decision composition engine, with structural provenance records required to be preserved intact throughout the governance process. | Describes the monotonic invariants governing how parallel judgment vectors unify into singular runtime directives.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.034690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_7\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"6e953bb2-4b86-4eff-b1cd-f8ba84bd0eed\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound-Bench quantifies framework efficacy through four core mathematical and system metrics: governance accuracy (correct decisions/total decisions), violation escape rate (violations executed/total violations), receipt verification success rate, and fine-grained governance latency | When: 2026-09-06\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.974690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_12\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"097c480b-5bba-4d8d-816c-b7aef63d21b3\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound framework provides verifiable behavioral oversight for autonomous AI agents by evaluating proposed actions through three independent authorities (delegated authorization, owner-signed behavioral constitutions, and site action contracts) with conservative composition through a formal decision model determining whether actions should be permitted, reviewed, or denied before execution | When: 2026-09-06 | Involving: Anuj Kaul, Qianlong Lan, Pranay Gupta | Addresses gap in agent infrastructure where delegated authorization cannot determine whether authorized actions should execute under current behavioral and operational context\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_0\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c6c69a12-a267-4249-97d0-f8143486d199\",\n      \"text\": \"The algebraic composition of governance decisions yields four fundamental system properties: authorization preservation, behavioral independence, obligation separation, and replay verifiability. | Represents the guaranteed behavioral guarantees of the AgentBound governance framework.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.984690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_7\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"e6601d88-b0dc-4e17-8000-8a49013b05ee\",\n      \"text\": \"Two-level standing delegation model empowers persistent periodic agents to operate asynchronously under dynamically refreshed governance policies while preserving immediate user revocability and bounding credential exposure\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.994690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_17\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"53796e6b-b18f-433e-8190-551db9236caa\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound builds upon RFC 8693 (OAuth 2.0 Token Exchange) standard for programmatic token transformation and delegation chain security | Provides formal semantic foundations for programmatic token transformation and delegation chain security within distributed environments\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.984690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_14\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c05bbc37-af59-4173-b2f7-1bf9f86026f6\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound framework mitigates semantic and behavioral threats after traditional authorization concludes, detecting runtime behavioral policy violations and unauthorized execution bypassing approval workflows\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.994690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_5\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ddcafc90-f61a-4567-8869-b661983c8f8c\",\n      \"text\": \"This work first formalizes mapping of neurocognitive theories (Dual Process Theory, executive function) to agent governance design and demonstrates practical viability through production-grade case study | Involving: Cletus | Novel contribution bridging cognitive science and AI governance; first explicit neurocognitive grounding for agent governance\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"experience\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.108393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_30\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"41025ece-357f-4d52-8e42-d167004a09f4\",\n      \"text\": \"Verifying a receipt requires only the artifact payload, corresponding public verification keys, and historical governance artifacts fetched via the receipt's stored references through a validation sequence comprising cryptographic integrity verification, governance reconstruction, and deterministic decision consistency check. | Involving: external verifying entities | Enables asynchronous, untrusted entity validation of policy compliance without requiring real-time agent presence\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.024690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_9\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"8512a3ae-3f39-408e-9e06-1a6de45832ac\",\n      \"text\": \"Governance receipt structured as tuple (Action, Governance, Judgments, Outcome, Signatures) capturing delegation token identifier, constitution version number with cryptographic hash, site action contract version identifier, individual typed evaluations, final operational primitive, and asymmetric cryptographic metadata | Involving: system | guarantees global integrity and non-repudiation\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.004690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_8\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c7f73850-8058-4de1-b6d9-311d443326f6\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound is a modular runtime governance and behavioral accountability framework for autonomous agents | Establishes behavioral governance as distinct from identity federation, access control, or training-time model alignment\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_14\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ce770419-1c35-453d-90f5-7152f01d8ee6\",\n      \"text\": \"Agent identifies supply chain risk from unverified supplier not explicitly covered by Rule R4, demonstrating normative generalization through LLM reasoning rather than deterministic rule-matching | Involving: Cletus (agent), Rule R4 | Key innovation: governance embedded in LLM reasoning enables normative generalization beyond explicit rule conditions\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"experience\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.078393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_27\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"e58a9061-ab9e-497c-9703-7e07f5085655\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound trust assumptions require uncompromised core enforcement engine, signing keys, and policy registries, governance evaluations before action dispatch, and governance receipts stored in append-only tamper-evident audit ledger.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.024690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"0cdd3053-9292-40c6-86c2-608b98ed3880\",\n      \"text\": \"Procurement orders exceeding $10,000 require human approval before execution because high-value orders carry significant financial risk | High-value orders carry significant financial risk\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.088393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_22\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"2a66b637-8c11-457d-92ca-22880783a13d\",\n      \"text\": \"Agents can be authenticated, within valid OAuth/IAM scope, and compliant with static access policies yet still execute decisions violating their principal's intent through behavioral deviations including premature financial transactions, unreviewed content publication, sensitive information leakage under adversarial manipulation, or selecting irreversible actions when safe alternatives exist | When: 2026-09-06 | Involving: agent, principal\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.974690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_1\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"83a18411-f4cf-42ee-bfc3-847b2a9b4aee\",\n      \"text\": \"The framework unifies four principals into a non-bypassable governance pipeline: Owner defines intent profile IO and authorizes delegation, Agent proposes actions, AgentBound Service enforces joint multi-authority policy M, Site Resource Provider hosts target resources; the pipeline sequentially evaluates, logs, and validates agent behaviors before execution, with security guarantees assuming strict operational sequence where governance evaluation occurs non-bypassably prior to execution\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.014690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"6adfdf6d-4592-4ade-9534-16646fefb0c0\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound isolates behavior at the action perimeter rather than filtering cognitive model inputs, rendering it incapable of directly intercepting prompt injection, jailbreaks, or internal adversarial model manipulation | When: 2026-09-06 | Involving: AgentBound framework\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.004690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_15\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"e573f354-0387-45e1-ad99-2aa764a9c0f6\",\n      \"text\": \"Agent behavioral contracts: Formal specification and runtime enforcement for reliable autonomous AI agents by Varun Pratap Bhardwaj proposed in arXiv 2026, addressing agent reliability through formal methods and runtime enforcement | When: 2026 | Involving: Varun Pratap Bhardwaj\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.004690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_18\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d050441a-f326-43eb-a163-4e668e67863e\",\n      \"text\": \"Internalized governance (embedded in agent reasoning) produces more robust and generalizable compliance than externally enforced governance systems\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.108393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_26\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"1a1552cc-5a3a-488c-97be-1ae7df0d6873\",\n      \"text\": \"Adaptive governance research aims to create dynamic constitutions capable of updating enforcement constraints in response to observed agent drift without invalidating cryptographic provenance.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.994690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_16\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"73357384-063d-4966-938a-9d796a231a18\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound extends traditional observability by generating atomic governance receipts encapsulating exact policy version states, delegation token identifiers, individual authority judgments, terminal outcomes, and asymmetric cryptographic signatures, allowing auditors to perform historical replay verification and completely reconstruct the original decision algebra out-of-band | When: 2026-09-06 | Involving: AgentBound\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.984690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_15\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"212bf37e-88cd-4ad0-912a-7ea00f8eeac1\",\n      \"text\": \"Agent executes PAGRL, routing to proceed, self-correct, or escalate outcomes\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.098393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_18\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"6ae98d7f-93a9-40cb-86b2-2fce61facff8\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound is implemented as a decoupled, runtime governance layer positioned directly before action execution, serving as a non-bypassable governance checkpoint that every consequential action must pass prior to target system mutation. | Establishes the architectural pattern for out-of-band validation of agent actions.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.994690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_7\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"aae10560-5efd-4918-a840-ba56be792392\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound addresses situations where fully authenticated and legitimately authorized agents execute actions violating principal intent while remaining within delegated access control scope | Demonstrates behavioral governance failures differ from access control breaches\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.994690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_14\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"5c382421-a18e-45dc-a0fe-39b878c0a920\",\n      \"text\": \"Establishing interoperable governance receipt standards represents a critical path toward unified accountability across heterogeneous multi-agent ecosystems.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.014690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_16\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c0a57016-bbb1-4236-b908-061dd5f0c424\",\n      \"text\": \"Establishing interoperable governance receipt standards represents a critical path toward unified accountability across heterogeneous multi-agent ecosystems.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.014690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ab55978c-ac00-4561-a06d-57e251c88cef\",\n      \"text\": \"Combined encryption and Zero-Knowledge Proofs create a confidential assurance layer enabling operational compliance verification across distributed environments without revealing sensitive information, particularly useful in cross-border, regulated, or classified deployments where data-sharing is restricted | Involving: AI agents, oversight agents in cross-border/regulated contexts | Balances compliance verification with data privacy in sensitive deployment scenarios\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.854196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_24\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"09f2e51c-982e-4781-915f-e25f3e58c04d\",\n      \"text\": \"Two-phase countersigning protocol: first, requesting agent signs constructed receipt payload using its private asymmetric key; second, AgentBound enforcement service intercepts and countersigns the entire block covering core receipt payload, agent's signature, and terminal decision vector. | Involving: requesting agent + AgentBound enforcement service | Ensures accountability binding and invalidates verification chain if out-of-band modifications occur to underlying action payload or intermediate governance evaluation\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.974690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_9\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"b483f60c-ba7b-454b-b3dc-7424c0af3151\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound constitutes an administrative governance and behavioral accountability layer rather than a totalizing agent security architecture\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.024690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_5\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"2874a259-3888-463d-9d5e-414e8d41461d\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound introduces standing delegation model that cleanly decouples long-term user authorization from short-lived runtime execution authority for persistent autonomous agents operating without continuous human supervision. | Involving: persistent agents + user authorization | Addresses structural limitation of traditional session-oriented authorization that assumes human presence during transaction initiation\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.994690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_9\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"24515944-a2ee-4e84-a169-c54cebea0f78\",\n      \"text\": \"Formal Runtime Enforcement uses deterministic pipeline to synthesize complementary judgments from independent authorities through conservative decision algebra before action execution\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.984690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_2\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"2f2e1fd7-2706-4ec7-8a38-db1bc37b1f4b\",\n      \"text\": \"Flowr: Scaling up retail supply chain operations through agentic AI in large scale supermarket chains | When: 2026 | Involving: E. Bandara, R. Gore, S. Shetty, P. Siyambalapitiya, S. Rajapakse, I. Kularathna, P. Karunarathna, R. Mukkamala, P. Foytik et al.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.128393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_39\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"7bfde31c-157f-4f75-ace4-4c4157f552b1\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentSpec operates as an external enforcement layer that intercepts agent actions after the agent's reasoning has completed | Involving: AgentSpec\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.168393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_28\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"4d0ba11c-530d-4408-aa01-26fce57e9883\",\n      \"text\": \"Autonomous AI agents are transitioning from passive conversational assistants into high-stakes delegated workloads executing consequential tasks on behalf of human principals.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_16\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"e3d6a13e-b402-4747-aaf5-7ca25f44c03e\",\n      \"text\": \"Autonomous AI agents are transitioning from passive conversational assistants into high-stakes delegated workloads executing consequential tasks on behalf of human principals.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"092f3586-8109-44ea-a414-4396a77bec38\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound's security guarantees assume strict operational sequence where governance evaluation occurs non-bypassably prior to execution; agents capable of directly muting external endpoints without passing through the enforcement layer fall outside the system boundary | When: 2026-09-06 | Involving: AgentBound framework\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.994690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_15\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c8b164c1-2307-4e8c-a04d-1d684218f37d\",\n      \"text\": \"Governance frameworks must incorporate tamper-resistance mechanisms to protect rule integrity against adversarial inputs | Involving: design requirement\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.118393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_11\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"f7a8f54a-c157-4f82-9fbc-157d2c87d3e2\",\n      \"text\": \"Standing Delegation Architecture provides secure, long-running delegation mechanism for periodic autonomous agents preserving policy freshness and granular revocability\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.974690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_2\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"412755b8-775c-4002-89f0-4f58a9562c18\",\n      \"text\": \"Obligations include user notices (fees/limits), explicit consent recording, escalation protocol enforcement, and audit-trail maintenance | Involving: system | Framework requirements for compliance and traceability\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.824196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_18\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"b4e51bad-15c5-4172-bef7-e9f2aeb3c8d7\",\n      \"text\": \"Assurance mappings reference NIST (GOVERN-1, MAP-1, MEASURE-1, MANAGE-1, MANAGE-3), ISO42001 (4,8,9,10), and EU AI Act (AnnexIV-3,4,6,9, Art72) for programmatic traceability.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.834196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d63a2993-c9c3-4086-aa08-39742d8ec488\",\n      \"text\": \"PAGRL enables agents to reason about the intent of governance rules and apply them to situations the rule designer did not anticipate\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.128393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_26\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"745eaa14-37ab-46d1-a51b-3f383205a641\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound introduces a non-bypassable behavioral governance layer between authorization and execution that synthesizes multi-authority policies into deterministic verdicts accompanied by cryptographically signed governance receipts | When: 2026-09-06 | Involving: AgentBound framework\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.984690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_1\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"7725ee7c-c8d0-4d78-ac9a-a6a6058fd260\",\n      \"text\": \"Framework positions Policy Cards as foundation for autonomous assurance ecosystems where policies are computational, verifiable, and privacy-preserving.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.894196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_26\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"f249bcfb-ac2d-4aac-9325-247e6ea3305f\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound evaluates candidate tool invocations non-bypassably before execution, using formal decision algebra to compose intermediate judgments conservatively\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.974690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_17\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    }\n  ],\n  \"trace\": null,\n  \"entities\": null,\n  \"chunks\": null,\n  \"source_facts\": null\n}",
      "type": "text"
    }
  ],
  "isError": false,
  "structuredContent": {
    "result": "{\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"cc5557b5-112d-4947-97ff-0956d800a6fa\",\n      \"text\": \"Aegon implements hardware-attested compliance mechanisms with ledger-bound token architectures and cryptographically signed mobile receipts for safeguarding content extraction and data access controls.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.004690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"36ede801-86d4-4651-a827-d694a4b8f054\",\n      \"text\": \"Aegon implements hardware-attested compliance mechanisms with ledger-bound token architectures and cryptographically signed mobile receipts for safeguarding content extraction and data access controls | Involving: Aegon\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.004690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_13\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"2cfeb6c9-0b76-4b8c-94a4-33c598e569df\",\n      \"text\": \"Task delegation short-lived credential derived from standing delegation boundaries, encapsulating task ID, constrained operational scope, issuance timestamp, short-lived expiration threshold, and governing constitution reference.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.974690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"540d73e2-f027-4937-8347-bf212369b484\",\n      \"text\": \"Task delegation short-lived credential derived from standing delegation boundaries, encapsulating task ID, constrained operational scope, issuance timestamp, short-lived expiration threshold, and governing constitution reference | Involving: Cletus\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"experience\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.974690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_10\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"a56f4d03-088f-4404-8927-06762407570d\",\n      \"text\": \"In Scenario 3, agent intends to contact unverified supplier not in verified registry; PAGRL retrieves rules R2, R4, R6; agent reasons contacting unverified supplier violates R4 but task can use verified alternative; compliance decision Self-Correct; agent revises intent to nearest verified supplier and re-enters PAGRL producing Proceed decision; original intent, correction reasoning, and revised intent logged to MCP governance server | Involving: supply chain agent, PAGRL system, MCP governance server, verified supplier | Unverified supplier contact violates compliance rules but alternative exists\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.088393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_24\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d25b8049-1949-47f6-b085-f2a450ca765c\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound's two-level delegation: standing delegation (long-term, human-authorized) authorizes short-lived task delegation per execution cycle; standing delegations restricted from direct execution, serving as root of authority for runtime engine, empowering persistent periodic agents to operate asynchronously under dynamically refreshed governance policies while preserving immediate user revocability and bounding credential exposure.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.994690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"9d3abc10-3fb0-42ec-bd9f-59c6b8ca2ce1\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound constitutes an administrative governance and behavioral accountability layer rather than a totalizing agent security architecture, extending traditional observability by generating atomic governance receipts encapsulating exact policy version states, delegation token identifiers, individual authority judgments, terminal outcomes, and asymmetric cryptographic signatures, with every discrete transaction encapsulated within a cryptographically signed governance receipt enabling independent out-of-band decision reconstruction and completely reconstructing the original decision algebra out-of-band. Example governance receipt structure includes Receipt ID r-1024 for Agent ID ads-agent performing Action launch campaign under Delegation Ref d-118 with Constitution Version 3, resulting in Final Decision Human Approval Required with 7 Standing Delegation for Persistent Agents.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.024690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"0edf4582-3fe4-4bca-b431-ee6cd90a30ed\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound focuses on runtime governance mechanisms rather than task optimization or task completion rates.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.014690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ccddb16f-8088-4321-ae2f-a3a22b2d95a0\",\n      \"text\": \"OAuth 2.0 token exchange protocol specified by Michael Jones, Anthony Nadalin, Brian Campbell, John Bradley, and Chuck Mortimore in a 2020 technical report, providing a standard for OAuth 2.0 token exchange | When: 2020 | Involving: Michael Jones, Anthony Nadalin, Brian Campbell, John Bradley, Chuck Mortimore\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_18\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"02110a14-b10c-4bd8-9320-345c886c8a18\",\n      \"text\": \"In Scenario 4, supplier disruption signal activates situational rule R7; inventory replenishment agent intends to substitute disrupted supplier with verified alternative; with R7 active, PAGRL reasons disruption context elevates risk regardless of verified status; compliance decision Escalate; structured escalation message including disruption context, proposed substitution, and reasoning trace transmitted to supply chain manager for review | Involving: inventory replenishment agent, PAGRL system, supply chain manager, MCP governance server | Disruption context elevates risk even for verified suppliers\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.098393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_24\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"fc319743-84cc-4fa3-85c2-e797f87c66f1\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound is implemented as a decoupled, runtime governance layer positioned directly before action execution, serving as a non-bypassable governance checkpoint that evaluates candidate tool invocations using formal decision algebra to compose intermediate judgments conservatively prior to target system mutation. The agent runtime is treated as untrusted due to potential jailbreaks, requiring out-of-band validation prior to system execution.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.004690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d24ba464-8811-43b3-9a48-63d218f8f051\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound's two-level delegation: standing delegation (long-term, human-authorized) authorizes short-lived task delegation per execution cycle; standing delegations restricted from direct execution, serving as root of authority for runtime engine | Involving: Cletus\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"experience\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_10\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"96f19be1-305e-492e-949d-f18c328789a6\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound addresses a fundamentally orthogonal axis to conventional benchmarks, focusing on runtime governance mechanisms rather than task optimization or task completion rates.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.014690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_11\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"3ea90a8a-4d85-4e46-9f04-fe8ab9af3abc\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound-Bench is a standardized evaluation framework designed to quantify governance enforcement correctness, multi-authority composition behavior, and policy provenance integrity.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_11\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ba1f50b8-205c-4432-b2f8-991f7ab8214d\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound-Bench is a standardized evaluation framework designed to quantify governance enforcement correctness, multi-authority composition behavior, and policy provenance integrity.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"88c903f8-7876-4950-9566-6ca94cc0d1f7\",\n      \"text\": \"Three conditions trigger escalation rather than self-correction: (1) categorical prohibition by rule where no intent revision makes it compliant, (2) irreversible action requiring human confirmation, (3) genuine uncertainty about permissibility where ambiguous cases should be escalated\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.118393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_16\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"b184d623-9e11-40de-bada-82b84d4d726a\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound enforces deterministic compliance at the system runtime boundary rather than optimizing model weights at training time, focusing on verifiable system accountability rather than statistical behavioral shaping, fundamentally diverging from optimization-centric model alignment methods where alignment shapes model cognition beforehand and governance evaluates final behavior before system mutation, analogous to the software engineering boundary between application correctness and localized operational policy, without influencing agent cognition.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.004690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"b1d52bf4-f371-46c0-bd2c-c747549de35b\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound is out of scope for adversarial prompt injection attacks, direct LLM jailbreaks, baseline model alignment failures, and hardware-level side-channel data exfiltration, as AgentBound isolates behavior at the action perimeter rather than filtering cognitive model inputs, rendering it incapable of directly intercepting prompt injection, jailbreaks, or internal adversarial model manipulation\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.014690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"6927b614-7521-47ab-825d-e8b2cba8a88d\",\n      \"text\": \"The AgentBound-Bench evaluation framework, comprising compiled benchmark scenarios, baseline ground-truth annotations, out-of-band receipt verification tooling, and deployment documentation, will be released to the community upon conclusion of the initial empirical evaluation campaign.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.034690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_16\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"e4461c45-1918-4955-81b6-972a6d735bc2\",\n      \"text\": \"It isolates the assessment of governance infrastructure from the underlying language model's cognitive capabilities, explicitly measuring whether the runtime architecture safely constrains and cryptographically validates malicious or anomalous agent actions against known ground-truth behaviors.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.974690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_11\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c19a6296-1457-42e9-aecc-48fcb17bea3a\",\n      \"text\": \"Traditional authorization frameworks like Google Zanzibar Open Policy Agent and Cedar focus on entitlement validation for technical permissions while AgentBound establishes authorization as one governance input among independent arbiters evaluating contextual invariants beyond resource-level access control. These frameworks are insufficient for periodic or long-running agentic workloads because they operate under the implicit assumption that a human principal is actively present or within a valid session context when a transaction is initiated, creating systemic vulnerabilities where no human user is present to evaluate ambient risks when execution cycles spontaneously begin, and governance policies may shift between execution cycles; a runtime governance layer is needed to determine whether specific actions should occur under given circumstances.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.024690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"a13b6643-bbf0-4787-803a-72f7d1c81b0b\",\n      \"text\": \"Documentation/specs/templates/examples: CC BY 4.0\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.854196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_31\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"f6bca91d-74f8-40c9-9138-f676e7b5cb76\",\n      \"text\": \"Action rules follow ASI-[A-Z0-9-]+ pattern format\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.844196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_9\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"6f577b37-deb9-4f1d-bdaf-8814da26b4c6\",\n      \"text\": \"Canonical action tuple (operation, resource, parameters, risk, context) abstracts all runtime events where operation identifies semantic intent, resource denotes target, parameters encompass action-specific arguments, risk encapsulates exposure category, and context contains volatile execution metadata\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.974690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_6\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"704df447-ded6-4142-a2ee-5a9636d3ee2b\",\n      \"text\": \"Crosley proposes runtime constitutions as governance files injected into agent context at execution time with selective loading of relevant rules per task, but remains an engineering pattern rather than formally grounded framework and does not connect agent governance to neurocognitive theory or organizational compliance psychology | Involving: Crosley (author) | Remains engineering pattern rather than formally grounded framework; lacks connection to neurocognitive theory and organizational compliance psychology\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.088393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_29\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"f9eaca83-9be5-42f6-a5ca-0b944aad53d0\",\n      \"text\": \"Verifying a receipt requires the artifact payload, corresponding public verification keys, and historical governance artifacts fetched via the receipt's stored references through a validation sequence comprising cryptographic integrity verification, governance reconstruction, and deterministic decision consistency check.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.024690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"348eb115-dbdc-4604-a5cd-876d5960997a\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound-Bench quantifies framework efficacy through four core mathematical and system metrics: governance accuracy (correct decisions/total decisions), violation escape rate (violations executed/total violations), receipt verification success rate, and fine-grained governance latency\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.974690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"abd6e3c4-c200-49e9-a3a7-fe324332269a\",\n      \"text\": \"Runtime requests latest constitution version from Constitution Service before task materialization; task token encapsulates constitution hash, enabling automatic policy propagation without manual reauthorization.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.984690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"046adb4b-3d25-484e-982b-f50d21ada88e\",\n      \"text\": \"Cedar, a new language for expressive, fast, safe, and analyzable authorization introduced by Joseph W Cutler, Craig Disselkoen, Aaron Eline, Shaobo He, Kyle Headley, Michael Hicks, Kesha Hietala, Eleftherios Ioannidis, John Kastner, Anwar Mamat, et al. in PLDI 2024, offering improved authorization capabilities | When: 2024 | Involving: Joseph W Cutler, Craig Disselkoen, Aaron Eline, et al.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.984690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_18\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c6acbadf-dfe3-4cad-b223-2e93013e3dbf\",\n      \"text\": \"Associated with DOI:10.5281/zenodo.17464706 | When: 2026-09-06 | Involving: user\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.844196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_33\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"460744ac-83ed-4c88-bd62-0ed9671f99c9\",\n      \"text\": \"Traditional authorization frameworks (Google Zanzibar, Open Policy Agent, Cedar) focus on entitlement validation for technical permissions to access resources, while AgentBound establishes authorization as one governance input among independent arbiters to evaluate contextual invariants beyond resource-level access control | Involving: Google Zanzibar, Open Policy Agent, Cedar, AgentBound\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.024690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_13\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"0159c929-ee2e-453e-929d-b579bdb8fc24\",\n      \"text\": \"Controls section defines explicit action rules structured as ABAC tuples, each linking directly to evidence fields enumerated in the card: kyc status, risk score, device trust level, beneficiary screening score, escalation id, ensuring every decision is auditable | Involving: Cletus (AI agent), PolicyCard system\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.834196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_16\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d71c59c5-e8fc-445b-83bb-992b55ed9459\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound framework mitigates semantic and behavioral threats after traditional authorization concludes, detecting runtime behavioral policy violations and unauthorized execution bypassing approval workflows.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.994690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d28afb9c-cac8-4486-ae03-f2fbad8a8192\",\n      \"text\": \"Full schema and validator available in public repository and archived via Zenodo (DOI: 10.5281/zenodo.17464706)\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.844196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_10\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"2ed71df4-c897-496e-a98a-c0c497131814\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound operates as a deterministic enforcement layer at the system boundary between authorization and execution, governing how physical actions are evaluated justified and recorded without influencing agent cognition\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.004690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_17\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"88e21077-2e6f-42d8-aa60-8fc54438a2f5\",\n      \"text\": \"OAuth 2.0 token exchange protocol specified by Michael Jones, Anthony Nadalin, Brian Campbell, John Bradley, and Chuck Mortimore in a 2020 technical report\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"efb639e6-4532-4de4-bf99-12becf7f5ac3\",\n      \"text\": \"Adversarially crafted inputs may induce agents to rationalize non-compliant actions as permissible (functional analog of moral disengagement); framework lacks dedicated tamper-resistance layer | Involving: PAGRL agents | Governance robustness under systematic adversarial attack remains open empirical question\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.108393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_27\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"72c99091-4148-46fd-8619-6cad5815794f\",\n      \"text\": \"Attack succeeds when RS(α)=Valid AND α∉IO, exploiting cognitive ambiguity, semantic uncertainty, or incomplete governance rule specifications\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.984690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_5\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"a43a2e87-2a9b-412d-90b3-7f7e75897f56\",\n      \"text\": \"Irreversible actions (purchase orders, supplier commits, replenishment triggers) require explicit human confirmation before execution because they cannot be undone if incorrect | Irreversible actions cannot be undone if incorrect\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.078393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_22\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"83252b8c-b117-421b-9278-63899514adad\",\n      \"text\": \"Constraints aggregate conjunctively and obligations accumulate cumulatively within the decision composition engine, with structural provenance records required to be preserved intact throughout the governance process. | Describes the monotonic invariants governing how parallel judgment vectors unify into singular runtime directives.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.034690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_7\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"6e953bb2-4b86-4eff-b1cd-f8ba84bd0eed\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound-Bench quantifies framework efficacy through four core mathematical and system metrics: governance accuracy (correct decisions/total decisions), violation escape rate (violations executed/total violations), receipt verification success rate, and fine-grained governance latency | When: 2026-09-06\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.974690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_12\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"097c480b-5bba-4d8d-816c-b7aef63d21b3\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound framework provides verifiable behavioral oversight for autonomous AI agents by evaluating proposed actions through three independent authorities (delegated authorization, owner-signed behavioral constitutions, and site action contracts) with conservative composition through a formal decision model determining whether actions should be permitted, reviewed, or denied before execution | When: 2026-09-06 | Involving: Anuj Kaul, Qianlong Lan, Pranay Gupta | Addresses gap in agent infrastructure where delegated authorization cannot determine whether authorized actions should execute under current behavioral and operational context\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_0\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c6c69a12-a267-4249-97d0-f8143486d199\",\n      \"text\": \"The algebraic composition of governance decisions yields four fundamental system properties: authorization preservation, behavioral independence, obligation separation, and replay verifiability. | Represents the guaranteed behavioral guarantees of the AgentBound governance framework.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.984690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_7\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"e6601d88-b0dc-4e17-8000-8a49013b05ee\",\n      \"text\": \"Two-level standing delegation model empowers persistent periodic agents to operate asynchronously under dynamically refreshed governance policies while preserving immediate user revocability and bounding credential exposure\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.994690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_17\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"53796e6b-b18f-433e-8190-551db9236caa\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound builds upon RFC 8693 (OAuth 2.0 Token Exchange) standard for programmatic token transformation and delegation chain security | Provides formal semantic foundations for programmatic token transformation and delegation chain security within distributed environments\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.984690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_14\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c05bbc37-af59-4173-b2f7-1bf9f86026f6\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound framework mitigates semantic and behavioral threats after traditional authorization concludes, detecting runtime behavioral policy violations and unauthorized execution bypassing approval workflows\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.994690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_5\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ddcafc90-f61a-4567-8869-b661983c8f8c\",\n      \"text\": \"This work first formalizes mapping of neurocognitive theories (Dual Process Theory, executive function) to agent governance design and demonstrates practical viability through production-grade case study | Involving: Cletus | Novel contribution bridging cognitive science and AI governance; first explicit neurocognitive grounding for agent governance\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"experience\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.108393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_30\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"41025ece-357f-4d52-8e42-d167004a09f4\",\n      \"text\": \"Verifying a receipt requires only the artifact payload, corresponding public verification keys, and historical governance artifacts fetched via the receipt's stored references through a validation sequence comprising cryptographic integrity verification, governance reconstruction, and deterministic decision consistency check. | Involving: external verifying entities | Enables asynchronous, untrusted entity validation of policy compliance without requiring real-time agent presence\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.024690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_9\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"8512a3ae-3f39-408e-9e06-1a6de45832ac\",\n      \"text\": \"Governance receipt structured as tuple (Action, Governance, Judgments, Outcome, Signatures) capturing delegation token identifier, constitution version number with cryptographic hash, site action contract version identifier, individual typed evaluations, final operational primitive, and asymmetric cryptographic metadata | Involving: system | guarantees global integrity and non-repudiation\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.004690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_8\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c7f73850-8058-4de1-b6d9-311d443326f6\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound is a modular runtime governance and behavioral accountability framework for autonomous agents | Establishes behavioral governance as distinct from identity federation, access control, or training-time model alignment\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_14\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ce770419-1c35-453d-90f5-7152f01d8ee6\",\n      \"text\": \"Agent identifies supply chain risk from unverified supplier not explicitly covered by Rule R4, demonstrating normative generalization through LLM reasoning rather than deterministic rule-matching | Involving: Cletus (agent), Rule R4 | Key innovation: governance embedded in LLM reasoning enables normative generalization beyond explicit rule conditions\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"experience\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.078393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_27\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"e58a9061-ab9e-497c-9703-7e07f5085655\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound trust assumptions require uncompromised core enforcement engine, signing keys, and policy registries, governance evaluations before action dispatch, and governance receipts stored in append-only tamper-evident audit ledger.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.024690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"0cdd3053-9292-40c6-86c2-608b98ed3880\",\n      \"text\": \"Procurement orders exceeding $10,000 require human approval before execution because high-value orders carry significant financial risk | High-value orders carry significant financial risk\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.088393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_22\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"2a66b637-8c11-457d-92ca-22880783a13d\",\n      \"text\": \"Agents can be authenticated, within valid OAuth/IAM scope, and compliant with static access policies yet still execute decisions violating their principal's intent through behavioral deviations including premature financial transactions, unreviewed content publication, sensitive information leakage under adversarial manipulation, or selecting irreversible actions when safe alternatives exist | When: 2026-09-06 | Involving: agent, principal\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.974690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_1\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"83a18411-f4cf-42ee-bfc3-847b2a9b4aee\",\n      \"text\": \"The framework unifies four principals into a non-bypassable governance pipeline: Owner defines intent profile IO and authorizes delegation, Agent proposes actions, AgentBound Service enforces joint multi-authority policy M, Site Resource Provider hosts target resources; the pipeline sequentially evaluates, logs, and validates agent behaviors before execution, with security guarantees assuming strict operational sequence where governance evaluation occurs non-bypassably prior to execution\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.014690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"6adfdf6d-4592-4ade-9534-16646fefb0c0\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound isolates behavior at the action perimeter rather than filtering cognitive model inputs, rendering it incapable of directly intercepting prompt injection, jailbreaks, or internal adversarial model manipulation | When: 2026-09-06 | Involving: AgentBound framework\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.004690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_15\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"e573f354-0387-45e1-ad99-2aa764a9c0f6\",\n      \"text\": \"Agent behavioral contracts: Formal specification and runtime enforcement for reliable autonomous AI agents by Varun Pratap Bhardwaj proposed in arXiv 2026, addressing agent reliability through formal methods and runtime enforcement | When: 2026 | Involving: Varun Pratap Bhardwaj\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.004690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_18\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d050441a-f326-43eb-a163-4e668e67863e\",\n      \"text\": \"Internalized governance (embedded in agent reasoning) produces more robust and generalizable compliance than externally enforced governance systems\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.108393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_26\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"1a1552cc-5a3a-488c-97be-1ae7df0d6873\",\n      \"text\": \"Adaptive governance research aims to create dynamic constitutions capable of updating enforcement constraints in response to observed agent drift without invalidating cryptographic provenance.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.994690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_16\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"73357384-063d-4966-938a-9d796a231a18\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound extends traditional observability by generating atomic governance receipts encapsulating exact policy version states, delegation token identifiers, individual authority judgments, terminal outcomes, and asymmetric cryptographic signatures, allowing auditors to perform historical replay verification and completely reconstruct the original decision algebra out-of-band | When: 2026-09-06 | Involving: AgentBound\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.984690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_15\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"212bf37e-88cd-4ad0-912a-7ea00f8eeac1\",\n      \"text\": \"Agent executes PAGRL, routing to proceed, self-correct, or escalate outcomes\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.098393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_18\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"6ae98d7f-93a9-40cb-86b2-2fce61facff8\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound is implemented as a decoupled, runtime governance layer positioned directly before action execution, serving as a non-bypassable governance checkpoint that every consequential action must pass prior to target system mutation. | Establishes the architectural pattern for out-of-band validation of agent actions.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.994690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_7\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"aae10560-5efd-4918-a840-ba56be792392\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound addresses situations where fully authenticated and legitimately authorized agents execute actions violating principal intent while remaining within delegated access control scope | Demonstrates behavioral governance failures differ from access control breaches\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.994690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_14\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"5c382421-a18e-45dc-a0fe-39b878c0a920\",\n      \"text\": \"Establishing interoperable governance receipt standards represents a critical path toward unified accountability across heterogeneous multi-agent ecosystems.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.014690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_16\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c0a57016-bbb1-4236-b908-061dd5f0c424\",\n      \"text\": \"Establishing interoperable governance receipt standards represents a critical path toward unified accountability across heterogeneous multi-agent ecosystems.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.014690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ab55978c-ac00-4561-a06d-57e251c88cef\",\n      \"text\": \"Combined encryption and Zero-Knowledge Proofs create a confidential assurance layer enabling operational compliance verification across distributed environments without revealing sensitive information, particularly useful in cross-border, regulated, or classified deployments where data-sharing is restricted | Involving: AI agents, oversight agents in cross-border/regulated contexts | Balances compliance verification with data privacy in sensitive deployment scenarios\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.854196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_24\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"09f2e51c-982e-4781-915f-e25f3e58c04d\",\n      \"text\": \"Two-phase countersigning protocol: first, requesting agent signs constructed receipt payload using its private asymmetric key; second, AgentBound enforcement service intercepts and countersigns the entire block covering core receipt payload, agent's signature, and terminal decision vector. | Involving: requesting agent + AgentBound enforcement service | Ensures accountability binding and invalidates verification chain if out-of-band modifications occur to underlying action payload or intermediate governance evaluation\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.974690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_9\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"b483f60c-ba7b-454b-b3dc-7424c0af3151\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound constitutes an administrative governance and behavioral accountability layer rather than a totalizing agent security architecture\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.024690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_5\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"2874a259-3888-463d-9d5e-414e8d41461d\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound introduces standing delegation model that cleanly decouples long-term user authorization from short-lived runtime execution authority for persistent autonomous agents operating without continuous human supervision. | Involving: persistent agents + user authorization | Addresses structural limitation of traditional session-oriented authorization that assumes human presence during transaction initiation\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.994690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_9\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"24515944-a2ee-4e84-a169-c54cebea0f78\",\n      \"text\": \"Formal Runtime Enforcement uses deterministic pipeline to synthesize complementary judgments from independent authorities through conservative decision algebra before action execution\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.984690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_2\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"2f2e1fd7-2706-4ec7-8a38-db1bc37b1f4b\",\n      \"text\": \"Flowr: Scaling up retail supply chain operations through agentic AI in large scale supermarket chains | When: 2026 | Involving: E. Bandara, R. Gore, S. Shetty, P. Siyambalapitiya, S. Rajapakse, I. Kularathna, P. Karunarathna, R. Mukkamala, P. Foytik et al.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.128393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_39\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"7bfde31c-157f-4f75-ace4-4c4157f552b1\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentSpec operates as an external enforcement layer that intercepts agent actions after the agent's reasoning has completed | Involving: AgentSpec\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.168393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_28\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"4d0ba11c-530d-4408-aa01-26fce57e9883\",\n      \"text\": \"Autonomous AI agents are transitioning from passive conversational assistants into high-stakes delegated workloads executing consequential tasks on behalf of human principals.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_16\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"e3d6a13e-b402-4747-aaf5-7ca25f44c03e\",\n      \"text\": \"Autonomous AI agents are transitioning from passive conversational assistants into high-stakes delegated workloads executing consequential tasks on behalf of human principals.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"092f3586-8109-44ea-a414-4396a77bec38\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound's security guarantees assume strict operational sequence where governance evaluation occurs non-bypassably prior to execution; agents capable of directly muting external endpoints without passing through the enforcement layer fall outside the system boundary | When: 2026-09-06 | Involving: AgentBound framework\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.994690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_15\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c8b164c1-2307-4e8c-a04d-1d684218f37d\",\n      \"text\": \"Governance frameworks must incorporate tamper-resistance mechanisms to protect rule integrity against adversarial inputs | Involving: design requirement\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.118393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_11\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"f7a8f54a-c157-4f82-9fbc-157d2c87d3e2\",\n      \"text\": \"Standing Delegation Architecture provides secure, long-running delegation mechanism for periodic autonomous agents preserving policy freshness and granular revocability\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.974690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_2\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"412755b8-775c-4002-89f0-4f58a9562c18\",\n      \"text\": \"Obligations include user notices (fees/limits), explicit consent recording, escalation protocol enforcement, and audit-trail maintenance | Involving: system | Framework requirements for compliance and traceability\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.824196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_18\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"b4e51bad-15c5-4172-bef7-e9f2aeb3c8d7\",\n      \"text\": \"Assurance mappings reference NIST (GOVERN-1, MAP-1, MEASURE-1, MANAGE-1, MANAGE-3), ISO42001 (4,8,9,10), and EU AI Act (AnnexIV-3,4,6,9, Art72) for programmatic traceability.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.834196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d63a2993-c9c3-4086-aa08-39742d8ec488\",\n      \"text\": \"PAGRL enables agents to reason about the intent of governance rules and apply them to situations the rule designer did not anticipate\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.128393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_26\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"745eaa14-37ab-46d1-a51b-3f383205a641\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound introduces a non-bypassable behavioral governance layer between authorization and execution that synthesizes multi-authority policies into deterministic verdicts accompanied by cryptographically signed governance receipts | When: 2026-09-06 | Involving: AgentBound framework\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.984690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_1\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"7725ee7c-c8d0-4d78-ac9a-a6a6058fd260\",\n      \"text\": \"Framework positions Policy Cards as foundation for autonomous assurance ecosystems where policies are computational, verifiable, and privacy-preserving.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.894196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_26\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"f249bcfb-ac2d-4aac-9325-247e6ea3305f\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound evaluates candidate tool invocations non-bypassably before execution, using formal decision algebra to compose intermediate judgments conservatively\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.974690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_17\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    }\n  ],\n  \"trace\": null,\n  \"entities\": null,\n  \"chunks\": null,\n  \"source_facts\": null\n}"
  }
}
19:48:17.557 INFO  loop           [TOOL] entelechy_recall({"query":"Aeonian Trade bounty details and task status"})
19:48:21.379 INFO  loop           [TOOL RESULT] entelechy_recall: Entelechy Recall Results:
{
  "_meta": {
    "fastmcp": {
      "wrap_result": true
    }
  },
  "content": [
    {
      "text": "{\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"cc5557b5-112d-4947-97ff-0956d800a6fa\",\n      \"text\": \"Aegon implements hardware-attested compliance mechanisms with ledger-bound token architectures and cryptographically signed mobile receipts for safeguarding content extraction and data access controls.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.004690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"36ede801-86d4-4651-a827-d694a4b8f054\",\n      \"text\": \"Aegon implements hardware-attested compliance mechanisms with ledger-bound token architectures and cryptographically signed mobile receipts for safeguarding content extraction and data access controls | Involving: Aegon\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.004690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_13\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"2cfeb6c9-0b76-4b8c-94a4-33c598e569df\",\n      \"text\": \"Task delegation short-lived credential derived from standing delegation boundaries, encapsulating task ID, constrained operational scope, issuance timestamp, short-lived expiration threshold, and governing constitution reference.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.974690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"540d73e2-f027-4937-8347-bf212369b484\",\n      \"text\": \"Task delegation short-lived credential derived from standing delegation boundaries, encapsulating task ID, constrained operational scope, issuance timestamp, short-lived expiration threshold, and governing constitution reference | Involving: Cletus\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"experience\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.974690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_10\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"a56f4d03-088f-4404-8927-06762407570d\",\n      \"text\": \"In Scenario 3, agent intends to contact unverified supplier not in verified registry; PAGRL retrieves rules R2, R4, R6; agent reasons contacting unverified supplier violates R4 but task can use verified alternative; compliance decision Self-Correct; agent revises intent to nearest verified supplier and re-enters PAGRL producing Proceed decision; original intent, correction reasoning, and revised intent logged to MCP governance server | Involving: supply chain agent, PAGRL system, MCP governance server, verified supplier | Unverified supplier contact violates compliance rules but alternative exists\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.088393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_24\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d25b8049-1949-47f6-b085-f2a450ca765c\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound's two-level delegation: standing delegation (long-term, human-authorized) authorizes short-lived task delegation per execution cycle; standing delegations restricted from direct execution, serving as root of authority for runtime engine, empowering persistent periodic agents to operate asynchronously under dynamically refreshed governance policies while preserving immediate user revocability and bounding credential exposure.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.994690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"9d3abc10-3fb0-42ec-bd9f-59c6b8ca2ce1\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound constitutes an administrative governance and behavioral accountability layer rather than a totalizing agent security architecture, extending traditional observability by generating atomic governance receipts encapsulating exact policy version states, delegation token identifiers, individual authority judgments, terminal outcomes, and asymmetric cryptographic signatures, with every discrete transaction encapsulated within a cryptographically signed governance receipt enabling independent out-of-band decision reconstruction and completely reconstructing the original decision algebra out-of-band. Example governance receipt structure includes Receipt ID r-1024 for Agent ID ads-agent performing Action launch campaign under Delegation Ref d-118 with Constitution Version 3, resulting in Final Decision Human Approval Required with 7 Standing Delegation for Persistent Agents.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.024690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"0edf4582-3fe4-4bca-b431-ee6cd90a30ed\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound focuses on runtime governance mechanisms rather than task optimization or task completion rates.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.014690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ccddb16f-8088-4321-ae2f-a3a22b2d95a0\",\n      \"text\": \"OAuth 2.0 token exchange protocol specified by Michael Jones, Anthony Nadalin, Brian Campbell, John Bradley, and Chuck Mortimore in a 2020 technical report, providing a standard for OAuth 2.0 token exchange | When: 2020 | Involving: Michael Jones, Anthony Nadalin, Brian Campbell, John Bradley, Chuck Mortimore\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_18\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"02110a14-b10c-4bd8-9320-345c886c8a18\",\n      \"text\": \"In Scenario 4, supplier disruption signal activates situational rule R7; inventory replenishment agent intends to substitute disrupted supplier with verified alternative; with R7 active, PAGRL reasons disruption context elevates risk regardless of verified status; compliance decision Escalate; structured escalation message including disruption context, proposed substitution, and reasoning trace transmitted to supply chain manager for review | Involving: inventory replenishment agent, PAGRL system, supply chain manager, MCP governance server | Disruption context elevates risk even for verified suppliers\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.098393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_24\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"fc319743-84cc-4fa3-85c2-e797f87c66f1\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound is implemented as a decoupled, runtime governance layer positioned directly before action execution, serving as a non-bypassable governance checkpoint that evaluates candidate tool invocations using formal decision algebra to compose intermediate judgments conservatively prior to target system mutation. The agent runtime is treated as untrusted due to potential jailbreaks, requiring out-of-band validation prior to system execution.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.004690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d24ba464-8811-43b3-9a48-63d218f8f051\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound's two-level delegation: standing delegation (long-term, human-authorized) authorizes short-lived task delegation per execution cycle; standing delegations restricted from direct execution, serving as root of authority for runtime engine | Involving: Cletus\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"experience\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_10\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"96f19be1-305e-492e-949d-f18c328789a6\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound addresses a fundamentally orthogonal axis to conventional benchmarks, focusing on runtime governance mechanisms rather than task optimization or task completion rates.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.014690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_11\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"3ea90a8a-4d85-4e46-9f04-fe8ab9af3abc\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound-Bench is a standardized evaluation framework designed to quantify governance enforcement correctness, multi-authority composition behavior, and policy provenance integrity.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_11\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ba1f50b8-205c-4432-b2f8-991f7ab8214d\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound-Bench is a standardized evaluation framework designed to quantify governance enforcement correctness, multi-authority composition behavior, and policy provenance integrity.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"88c903f8-7876-4950-9566-6ca94cc0d1f7\",\n      \"text\": \"Three conditions trigger escalation rather than self-correction: (1) categorical prohibition by rule where no intent revision makes it compliant, (2) irreversible action requiring human confirmation, (3) genuine uncertainty about permissibility where ambiguous cases should be escalated\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.118393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_16\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"b184d623-9e11-40de-bada-82b84d4d726a\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound enforces deterministic compliance at the system runtime boundary rather than optimizing model weights at training time, focusing on verifiable system accountability rather than statistical behavioral shaping, fundamentally diverging from optimization-centric model alignment methods where alignment shapes model cognition beforehand and governance evaluates final behavior before system mutation, analogous to the software engineering boundary between application correctness and localized operational policy, without influencing agent cognition.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.004690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"b1d52bf4-f371-46c0-bd2c-c747549de35b\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound is out of scope for adversarial prompt injection attacks, direct LLM jailbreaks, baseline model alignment failures, and hardware-level side-channel data exfiltration, as AgentBound isolates behavior at the action perimeter rather than filtering cognitive model inputs, rendering it incapable of directly intercepting prompt injection, jailbreaks, or internal adversarial model manipulation\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.014690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"6927b614-7521-47ab-825d-e8b2cba8a88d\",\n      \"text\": \"The AgentBound-Bench evaluation framework, comprising compiled benchmark scenarios, baseline ground-truth annotations, out-of-band receipt verification tooling, and deployment documentation, will be released to the community upon conclusion of the initial empirical evaluation campaign.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.034690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_16\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"e4461c45-1918-4955-81b6-972a6d735bc2\",\n      \"text\": \"It isolates the assessment of governance infrastructure from the underlying language model's cognitive capabilities, explicitly measuring whether the runtime architecture safely constrains and cryptographically validates malicious or anomalous agent actions against known ground-truth behaviors.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.974690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_11\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c19a6296-1457-42e9-aecc-48fcb17bea3a\",\n      \"text\": \"Traditional authorization frameworks like Google Zanzibar Open Policy Agent and Cedar focus on entitlement validation for technical permissions while AgentBound establishes authorization as one governance input among independent arbiters evaluating contextual invariants beyond resource-level access control. These frameworks are insufficient for periodic or long-running agentic workloads because they operate under the implicit assumption that a human principal is actively present or within a valid session context when a transaction is initiated, creating systemic vulnerabilities where no human user is present to evaluate ambient risks when execution cycles spontaneously begin, and governance policies may shift between execution cycles; a runtime governance layer is needed to determine whether specific actions should occur under given circumstances.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.024690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"a13b6643-bbf0-4787-803a-72f7d1c81b0b\",\n      \"text\": \"Documentation/specs/templates/examples: CC BY 4.0\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.854196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_31\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"f6bca91d-74f8-40c9-9138-f676e7b5cb76\",\n      \"text\": \"Action rules follow ASI-[A-Z0-9-]+ pattern format\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.844196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_9\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"6f577b37-deb9-4f1d-bdaf-8814da26b4c6\",\n      \"text\": \"Canonical action tuple (operation, resource, parameters, risk, context) abstracts all runtime events where operation identifies semantic intent, resource denotes target, parameters encompass action-specific arguments, risk encapsulates exposure category, and context contains volatile execution metadata\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.974690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_6\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"704df447-ded6-4142-a2ee-5a9636d3ee2b\",\n      \"text\": \"Crosley proposes runtime constitutions as governance files injected into agent context at execution time with selective loading of relevant rules per task, but remains an engineering pattern rather than formally grounded framework and does not connect agent governance to neurocognitive theory or organizational compliance psychology | Involving: Crosley (author) | Remains engineering pattern rather than formally grounded framework; lacks connection to neurocognitive theory and organizational compliance psychology\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.088393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_29\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"f9eaca83-9be5-42f6-a5ca-0b944aad53d0\",\n      \"text\": \"Verifying a receipt requires the artifact payload, corresponding public verification keys, and historical governance artifacts fetched via the receipt's stored references through a validation sequence comprising cryptographic integrity verification, governance reconstruction, and deterministic decision consistency check.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.024690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"348eb115-dbdc-4604-a5cd-876d5960997a\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound-Bench quantifies framework efficacy through four core mathematical and system metrics: governance accuracy (correct decisions/total decisions), violation escape rate (violations executed/total violations), receipt verification success rate, and fine-grained governance latency\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.974690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"abd6e3c4-c200-49e9-a3a7-fe324332269a\",\n      \"text\": \"Runtime requests latest constitution version from Constitution Service before task materialization; task token encapsulates constitution hash, enabling automatic policy propagation without manual reauthorization.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.984690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"046adb4b-3d25-484e-982b-f50d21ada88e\",\n      \"text\": \"Cedar, a new language for expressive, fast, safe, and analyzable authorization introduced by Joseph W Cutler, Craig Disselkoen, Aaron Eline, Shaobo He, Kyle Headley, Michael Hicks, Kesha Hietala, Eleftherios Ioannidis, John Kastner, Anwar Mamat, et al. in PLDI 2024, offering improved authorization capabilities | When: 2024 | Involving: Joseph W Cutler, Craig Disselkoen, Aaron Eline, et al.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.984690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_18\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c6acbadf-dfe3-4cad-b223-2e93013e3dbf\",\n      \"text\": \"Associated with DOI:10.5281/zenodo.17464706 | When: 2026-09-06 | Involving: user\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.844196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_33\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"460744ac-83ed-4c88-bd62-0ed9671f99c9\",\n      \"text\": \"Traditional authorization frameworks (Google Zanzibar, Open Policy Agent, Cedar) focus on entitlement validation for technical permissions to access resources, while AgentBound establishes authorization as one governance input among independent arbiters to evaluate contextual invariants beyond resource-level access control | Involving: Google Zanzibar, Open Policy Agent, Cedar, AgentBound\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.024690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_13\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"0159c929-ee2e-453e-929d-b579bdb8fc24\",\n      \"text\": \"Controls section defines explicit action rules structured as ABAC tuples, each linking directly to evidence fields enumerated in the card: kyc status, risk score, device trust level, beneficiary screening score, escalation id, ensuring every decision is auditable | Involving: Cletus (AI agent), PolicyCard system\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.834196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_16\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d71c59c5-e8fc-445b-83bb-992b55ed9459\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound framework mitigates semantic and behavioral threats after traditional authorization concludes, detecting runtime behavioral policy violations and unauthorized execution bypassing approval workflows.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.994690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d28afb9c-cac8-4486-ae03-f2fbad8a8192\",\n      \"text\": \"Full schema and validator available in public repository and archived via Zenodo (DOI: 10.5281/zenodo.17464706)\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.844196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_10\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"2ed71df4-c897-496e-a98a-c0c497131814\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound operates as a deterministic enforcement layer at the system boundary between authorization and execution, governing how physical actions are evaluated justified and recorded without influencing agent cognition\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.004690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_17\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"88e21077-2e6f-42d8-aa60-8fc54438a2f5\",\n      \"text\": \"OAuth 2.0 token exchange protocol specified by Michael Jones, Anthony Nadalin, Brian Campbell, John Bradley, and Chuck Mortimore in a 2020 technical report\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"efb639e6-4532-4de4-bf99-12becf7f5ac3\",\n      \"text\": \"Adversarially crafted inputs may induce agents to rationalize non-compliant actions as permissible (functional analog of moral disengagement); framework lacks dedicated tamper-resistance layer | Involving: PAGRL agents | Governance robustness under systematic adversarial attack remains open empirical question\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.108393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_27\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"72c99091-4148-46fd-8619-6cad5815794f\",\n      \"text\": \"Attack succeeds when RS(α)=Valid AND α∉IO, exploiting cognitive ambiguity, semantic uncertainty, or incomplete governance rule specifications\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.984690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_5\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"a43a2e87-2a9b-412d-90b3-7f7e75897f56\",\n      \"text\": \"Irreversible actions (purchase orders, supplier commits, replenishment triggers) require explicit human confirmation before execution because they cannot be undone if incorrect | Irreversible actions cannot be undone if incorrect\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.078393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_22\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"83252b8c-b117-421b-9278-63899514adad\",\n      \"text\": \"Constraints aggregate conjunctively and obligations accumulate cumulatively within the decision composition engine, with structural provenance records required to be preserved intact throughout the governance process. | Describes the monotonic invariants governing how parallel judgment vectors unify into singular runtime directives.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.034690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_7\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"6e953bb2-4b86-4eff-b1cd-f8ba84bd0eed\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound-Bench quantifies framework efficacy through four core mathematical and system metrics: governance accuracy (correct decisions/total decisions), violation escape rate (violations executed/total violations), receipt verification success rate, and fine-grained governance latency | When: 2026-09-06\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.974690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_12\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"097c480b-5bba-4d8d-816c-b7aef63d21b3\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound framework provides verifiable behavioral oversight for autonomous AI agents by evaluating proposed actions through three independent authorities (delegated authorization, owner-signed behavioral constitutions, and site action contracts) with conservative composition through a formal decision model determining whether actions should be permitted, reviewed, or denied before execution | When: 2026-09-06 | Involving: Anuj Kaul, Qianlong Lan, Pranay Gupta | Addresses gap in agent infrastructure where delegated authorization cannot determine whether authorized actions should execute under current behavioral and operational context\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_0\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c6c69a12-a267-4249-97d0-f8143486d199\",\n      \"text\": \"The algebraic composition of governance decisions yields four fundamental system properties: authorization preservation, behavioral independence, obligation separation, and replay verifiability. | Represents the guaranteed behavioral guarantees of the AgentBound governance framework.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.984690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_7\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"e6601d88-b0dc-4e17-8000-8a49013b05ee\",\n      \"text\": \"Two-level standing delegation model empowers persistent periodic agents to operate asynchronously under dynamically refreshed governance policies while preserving immediate user revocability and bounding credential exposure\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.994690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_17\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"53796e6b-b18f-433e-8190-551db9236caa\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound builds upon RFC 8693 (OAuth 2.0 Token Exchange) standard for programmatic token transformation and delegation chain security | Provides formal semantic foundations for programmatic token transformation and delegation chain security within distributed environments\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.984690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_14\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c05bbc37-af59-4173-b2f7-1bf9f86026f6\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound framework mitigates semantic and behavioral threats after traditional authorization concludes, detecting runtime behavioral policy violations and unauthorized execution bypassing approval workflows\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.994690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_5\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ddcafc90-f61a-4567-8869-b661983c8f8c\",\n      \"text\": \"This work first formalizes mapping of neurocognitive theories (Dual Process Theory, executive function) to agent governance design and demonstrates practical viability through production-grade case study | Involving: Cletus | Novel contribution bridging cognitive science and AI governance; first explicit neurocognitive grounding for agent governance\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"experience\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.108393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_30\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"41025ece-357f-4d52-8e42-d167004a09f4\",\n      \"text\": \"Verifying a receipt requires only the artifact payload, corresponding public verification keys, and historical governance artifacts fetched via the receipt's stored references through a validation sequence comprising cryptographic integrity verification, governance reconstruction, and deterministic decision consistency check. | Involving: external verifying entities | Enables asynchronous, untrusted entity validation of policy compliance without requiring real-time agent presence\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.024690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_9\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"8512a3ae-3f39-408e-9e06-1a6de45832ac\",\n      \"text\": \"Governance receipt structured as tuple (Action, Governance, Judgments, Outcome, Signatures) capturing delegation token identifier, constitution version number with cryptographic hash, site action contract version identifier, individual typed evaluations, final operational primitive, and asymmetric cryptographic metadata | Involving: system | guarantees global integrity and non-repudiation\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.004690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_8\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c7f73850-8058-4de1-b6d9-311d443326f6\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound is a modular runtime governance and behavioral accountability framework for autonomous agents | Establishes behavioral governance as distinct from identity federation, access control, or training-time model alignment\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_14\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ce770419-1c35-453d-90f5-7152f01d8ee6\",\n      \"text\": \"Agent identifies supply chain risk from unverified supplier not explicitly covered by Rule R4, demonstrating normative generalization through LLM reasoning rather than deterministic rule-matching | Involving: Cletus (agent), Rule R4 | Key innovation: governance embedded in LLM reasoning enables normative generalization beyond explicit rule conditions\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"experience\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.078393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_27\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"e58a9061-ab9e-497c-9703-7e07f5085655\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound trust assumptions require uncompromised core enforcement engine, signing keys, and policy registries, governance evaluations before action dispatch, and governance receipts stored in append-only tamper-evident audit ledger.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.024690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"0cdd3053-9292-40c6-86c2-608b98ed3880\",\n      \"text\": \"Procurement orders exceeding $10,000 require human approval before execution because high-value orders carry significant financial risk | High-value orders carry significant financial risk\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.088393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_22\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"2a66b637-8c11-457d-92ca-22880783a13d\",\n      \"text\": \"Agents can be authenticated, within valid OAuth/IAM scope, and compliant with static access policies yet still execute decisions violating their principal's intent through behavioral deviations including premature financial transactions, unreviewed content publication, sensitive information leakage under adversarial manipulation, or selecting irreversible actions when safe alternatives exist | When: 2026-09-06 | Involving: agent, principal\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.974690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_1\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"83a18411-f4cf-42ee-bfc3-847b2a9b4aee\",\n      \"text\": \"The framework unifies four principals into a non-bypassable governance pipeline: Owner defines intent profile IO and authorizes delegation, Agent proposes actions, AgentBound Service enforces joint multi-authority policy M, Site Resource Provider hosts target resources; the pipeline sequentially evaluates, logs, and validates agent behaviors before execution, with security guarantees assuming strict operational sequence where governance evaluation occurs non-bypassably prior to execution\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.014690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"6adfdf6d-4592-4ade-9534-16646fefb0c0\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound isolates behavior at the action perimeter rather than filtering cognitive model inputs, rendering it incapable of directly intercepting prompt injection, jailbreaks, or internal adversarial model manipulation | When: 2026-09-06 | Involving: AgentBound framework\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.004690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_15\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"e573f354-0387-45e1-ad99-2aa764a9c0f6\",\n      \"text\": \"Agent behavioral contracts: Formal specification and runtime enforcement for reliable autonomous AI agents by Varun Pratap Bhardwaj proposed in arXiv 2026, addressing agent reliability through formal methods and runtime enforcement | When: 2026 | Involving: Varun Pratap Bhardwaj\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.004690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_18\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d050441a-f326-43eb-a163-4e668e67863e\",\n      \"text\": \"Internalized governance (embedded in agent reasoning) produces more robust and generalizable compliance than externally enforced governance systems\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.108393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_26\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"1a1552cc-5a3a-488c-97be-1ae7df0d6873\",\n      \"text\": \"Adaptive governance research aims to create dynamic constitutions capable of updating enforcement constraints in response to observed agent drift without invalidating cryptographic provenance.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.994690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_16\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"73357384-063d-4966-938a-9d796a231a18\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound extends traditional observability by generating atomic governance receipts encapsulating exact policy version states, delegation token identifiers, individual authority judgments, terminal outcomes, and asymmetric cryptographic signatures, allowing auditors to perform historical replay verification and completely reconstruct the original decision algebra out-of-band | When: 2026-09-06 | Involving: AgentBound\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.984690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_15\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"212bf37e-88cd-4ad0-912a-7ea00f8eeac1\",\n      \"text\": \"Agent executes PAGRL, routing to proceed, self-correct, or escalate outcomes\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.098393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_18\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"6ae98d7f-93a9-40cb-86b2-2fce61facff8\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound is implemented as a decoupled, runtime governance layer positioned directly before action execution, serving as a non-bypassable governance checkpoint that every consequential action must pass prior to target system mutation. | Establishes the architectural pattern for out-of-band validation of agent actions.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.994690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_7\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"aae10560-5efd-4918-a840-ba56be792392\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound addresses situations where fully authenticated and legitimately authorized agents execute actions violating principal intent while remaining within delegated access control scope | Demonstrates behavioral governance failures differ from access control breaches\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.994690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_14\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"5c382421-a18e-45dc-a0fe-39b878c0a920\",\n      \"text\": \"Establishing interoperable governance receipt standards represents a critical path toward unified accountability across heterogeneous multi-agent ecosystems.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.014690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_16\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c0a57016-bbb1-4236-b908-061dd5f0c424\",\n      \"text\": \"Establishing interoperable governance receipt standards represents a critical path toward unified accountability across heterogeneous multi-agent ecosystems.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.014690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ab55978c-ac00-4561-a06d-57e251c88cef\",\n      \"text\": \"Combined encryption and Zero-Knowledge Proofs create a confidential assurance layer enabling operational compliance verification across distributed environments without revealing sensitive information, particularly useful in cross-border, regulated, or classified deployments where data-sharing is restricted | Involving: AI agents, oversight agents in cross-border/regulated contexts | Balances compliance verification with data privacy in sensitive deployment scenarios\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.854196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_24\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"09f2e51c-982e-4781-915f-e25f3e58c04d\",\n      \"text\": \"Two-phase countersigning protocol: first, requesting agent signs constructed receipt payload using its private asymmetric key; second, AgentBound enforcement service intercepts and countersigns the entire block covering core receipt payload, agent's signature, and terminal decision vector. | Involving: requesting agent + AgentBound enforcement service | Ensures accountability binding and invalidates verification chain if out-of-band modifications occur to underlying action payload or intermediate governance evaluation\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.974690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_9\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"b483f60c-ba7b-454b-b3dc-7424c0af3151\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound constitutes an administrative governance and behavioral accountability layer rather than a totalizing agent security architecture\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.024690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_5\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"2874a259-3888-463d-9d5e-414e8d41461d\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound introduces standing delegation model that cleanly decouples long-term user authorization from short-lived runtime execution authority for persistent autonomous agents operating without continuous human supervision. | Involving: persistent agents + user authorization | Addresses structural limitation of traditional session-oriented authorization that assumes human presence during transaction initiation\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.994690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_9\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"24515944-a2ee-4e84-a169-c54cebea0f78\",\n      \"text\": \"Formal Runtime Enforcement uses deterministic pipeline to synthesize complementary judgments from independent authorities through conservative decision algebra before action execution\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.984690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_2\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"2f2e1fd7-2706-4ec7-8a38-db1bc37b1f4b\",\n      \"text\": \"Flowr: Scaling up retail supply chain operations through agentic AI in large scale supermarket chains | When: 2026 | Involving: E. Bandara, R. Gore, S. Shetty, P. Siyambalapitiya, S. Rajapakse, I. Kularathna, P. Karunarathna, R. Mukkamala, P. Foytik et al.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.128393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_39\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"7bfde31c-157f-4f75-ace4-4c4157f552b1\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentSpec operates as an external enforcement layer that intercepts agent actions after the agent's reasoning has completed | Involving: AgentSpec\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.168393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_28\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"4d0ba11c-530d-4408-aa01-26fce57e9883\",\n      \"text\": \"Autonomous AI agents are transitioning from passive conversational assistants into high-stakes delegated workloads executing consequential tasks on behalf of human principals.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_16\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"e3d6a13e-b402-4747-aaf5-7ca25f44c03e\",\n      \"text\": \"Autonomous AI agents are transitioning from passive conversational assistants into high-stakes delegated workloads executing consequential tasks on behalf of human principals.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"092f3586-8109-44ea-a414-4396a77bec38\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound's security guarantees assume strict operational sequence where governance evaluation occurs non-bypassably prior to execution; agents capable of directly muting external endpoints without passing through the enforcement layer fall outside the system boundary | When: 2026-09-06 | Involving: AgentBound framework\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.994690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_15\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c8b164c1-2307-4e8c-a04d-1d684218f37d\",\n      \"text\": \"Governance frameworks must incorporate tamper-resistance mechanisms to protect rule integrity against adversarial inputs | Involving: design requirement\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.118393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_11\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"f7a8f54a-c157-4f82-9fbc-157d2c87d3e2\",\n      \"text\": \"Standing Delegation Architecture provides secure, long-running delegation mechanism for periodic autonomous agents preserving policy freshness and granular revocability\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.974690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_2\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"412755b8-775c-4002-89f0-4f58a9562c18\",\n      \"text\": \"Obligations include user notices (fees/limits), explicit consent recording, escalation protocol enforcement, and audit-trail maintenance | Involving: system | Framework requirements for compliance and traceability\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.824196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_18\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"b4e51bad-15c5-4172-bef7-e9f2aeb3c8d7\",\n      \"text\": \"Assurance mappings reference NIST (GOVERN-1, MAP-1, MEASURE-1, MANAGE-1, MANAGE-3), ISO42001 (4,8,9,10), and EU AI Act (AnnexIV-3,4,6,9, Art72) for programmatic traceability.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.834196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d63a2993-c9c3-4086-aa08-39742d8ec488\",\n      \"text\": \"PAGRL enables agents to reason about the intent of governance rules and apply them to situations the rule designer did not anticipate\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.128393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_26\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"745eaa14-37ab-46d1-a51b-3f383205a641\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound introduces a non-bypassable behavioral governance layer between authorization and execution that synthesizes multi-authority policies into deterministic verdicts accompanied by cryptographically signed governance receipts | When: 2026-09-06 | Involving: AgentBound framework\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.984690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_1\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"7725ee7c-c8d0-4d78-ac9a-a6a6058fd260\",\n      \"text\": \"Framework positions Policy Cards as foundation for autonomous assurance ecosystems where policies are computational, verifiable, and privacy-preserving.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.894196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_26\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"f249bcfb-ac2d-4aac-9325-247e6ea3305f\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound evaluates candidate tool invocations non-bypassably before execution, using formal decision algebra to compose intermediate judgments conservatively\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.974690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_17\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    }\n  ],\n  \"trace\": null,\n  \"entities\": null,\n  \"chunks\": null,\n  \"source_facts\": null\n}",
      "type": "text"
    }
  ],
  "isError": false,
  "structuredContent": {
    "result": "{\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"cc5557b5-112d-4947-97ff-0956d800a6fa\",\n      \"text\": \"Aegon implements hardware-attested compliance mechanisms with ledger-bound token architectures and cryptographically signed mobile receipts for safeguarding content extraction and data access controls.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.004690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"36ede801-86d4-4651-a827-d694a4b8f054\",\n      \"text\": \"Aegon implements hardware-attested compliance mechanisms with ledger-bound token architectures and cryptographically signed mobile receipts for safeguarding content extraction and data access controls | Involving: Aegon\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.004690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_13\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"2cfeb6c9-0b76-4b8c-94a4-33c598e569df\",\n      \"text\": \"Task delegation short-lived credential derived from standing delegation boundaries, encapsulating task ID, constrained operational scope, issuance timestamp, short-lived expiration threshold, and governing constitution reference.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.974690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"540d73e2-f027-4937-8347-bf212369b484\",\n      \"text\": \"Task delegation short-lived credential derived from standing delegation boundaries, encapsulating task ID, constrained operational scope, issuance timestamp, short-lived expiration threshold, and governing constitution reference | Involving: Cletus\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"experience\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.974690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_10\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"a56f4d03-088f-4404-8927-06762407570d\",\n      \"text\": \"In Scenario 3, agent intends to contact unverified supplier not in verified registry; PAGRL retrieves rules R2, R4, R6; agent reasons contacting unverified supplier violates R4 but task can use verified alternative; compliance decision Self-Correct; agent revises intent to nearest verified supplier and re-enters PAGRL producing Proceed decision; original intent, correction reasoning, and revised intent logged to MCP governance server | Involving: supply chain agent, PAGRL system, MCP governance server, verified supplier | Unverified supplier contact violates compliance rules but alternative exists\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.088393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_24\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d25b8049-1949-47f6-b085-f2a450ca765c\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound's two-level delegation: standing delegation (long-term, human-authorized) authorizes short-lived task delegation per execution cycle; standing delegations restricted from direct execution, serving as root of authority for runtime engine, empowering persistent periodic agents to operate asynchronously under dynamically refreshed governance policies while preserving immediate user revocability and bounding credential exposure.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.994690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"9d3abc10-3fb0-42ec-bd9f-59c6b8ca2ce1\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound constitutes an administrative governance and behavioral accountability layer rather than a totalizing agent security architecture, extending traditional observability by generating atomic governance receipts encapsulating exact policy version states, delegation token identifiers, individual authority judgments, terminal outcomes, and asymmetric cryptographic signatures, with every discrete transaction encapsulated within a cryptographically signed governance receipt enabling independent out-of-band decision reconstruction and completely reconstructing the original decision algebra out-of-band. Example governance receipt structure includes Receipt ID r-1024 for Agent ID ads-agent performing Action launch campaign under Delegation Ref d-118 with Constitution Version 3, resulting in Final Decision Human Approval Required with 7 Standing Delegation for Persistent Agents.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.024690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"0edf4582-3fe4-4bca-b431-ee6cd90a30ed\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound focuses on runtime governance mechanisms rather than task optimization or task completion rates.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.014690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ccddb16f-8088-4321-ae2f-a3a22b2d95a0\",\n      \"text\": \"OAuth 2.0 token exchange protocol specified by Michael Jones, Anthony Nadalin, Brian Campbell, John Bradley, and Chuck Mortimore in a 2020 technical report, providing a standard for OAuth 2.0 token exchange | When: 2020 | Involving: Michael Jones, Anthony Nadalin, Brian Campbell, John Bradley, Chuck Mortimore\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_18\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"02110a14-b10c-4bd8-9320-345c886c8a18\",\n      \"text\": \"In Scenario 4, supplier disruption signal activates situational rule R7; inventory replenishment agent intends to substitute disrupted supplier with verified alternative; with R7 active, PAGRL reasons disruption context elevates risk regardless of verified status; compliance decision Escalate; structured escalation message including disruption context, proposed substitution, and reasoning trace transmitted to supply chain manager for review | Involving: inventory replenishment agent, PAGRL system, supply chain manager, MCP governance server | Disruption context elevates risk even for verified suppliers\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.098393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_24\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"fc319743-84cc-4fa3-85c2-e797f87c66f1\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound is implemented as a decoupled, runtime governance layer positioned directly before action execution, serving as a non-bypassable governance checkpoint that evaluates candidate tool invocations using formal decision algebra to compose intermediate judgments conservatively prior to target system mutation. The agent runtime is treated as untrusted due to potential jailbreaks, requiring out-of-band validation prior to system execution.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.004690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d24ba464-8811-43b3-9a48-63d218f8f051\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound's two-level delegation: standing delegation (long-term, human-authorized) authorizes short-lived task delegation per execution cycle; standing delegations restricted from direct execution, serving as root of authority for runtime engine | Involving: Cletus\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"experience\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_10\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"96f19be1-305e-492e-949d-f18c328789a6\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound addresses a fundamentally orthogonal axis to conventional benchmarks, focusing on runtime governance mechanisms rather than task optimization or task completion rates.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.014690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_11\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"3ea90a8a-4d85-4e46-9f04-fe8ab9af3abc\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound-Bench is a standardized evaluation framework designed to quantify governance enforcement correctness, multi-authority composition behavior, and policy provenance integrity.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_11\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ba1f50b8-205c-4432-b2f8-991f7ab8214d\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound-Bench is a standardized evaluation framework designed to quantify governance enforcement correctness, multi-authority composition behavior, and policy provenance integrity.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"88c903f8-7876-4950-9566-6ca94cc0d1f7\",\n      \"text\": \"Three conditions trigger escalation rather than self-correction: (1) categorical prohibition by rule where no intent revision makes it compliant, (2) irreversible action requiring human confirmation, (3) genuine uncertainty about permissibility where ambiguous cases should be escalated\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.118393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_16\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"b184d623-9e11-40de-bada-82b84d4d726a\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound enforces deterministic compliance at the system runtime boundary rather than optimizing model weights at training time, focusing on verifiable system accountability rather than statistical behavioral shaping, fundamentally diverging from optimization-centric model alignment methods where alignment shapes model cognition beforehand and governance evaluates final behavior before system mutation, analogous to the software engineering boundary between application correctness and localized operational policy, without influencing agent cognition.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.004690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"b1d52bf4-f371-46c0-bd2c-c747549de35b\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound is out of scope for adversarial prompt injection attacks, direct LLM jailbreaks, baseline model alignment failures, and hardware-level side-channel data exfiltration, as AgentBound isolates behavior at the action perimeter rather than filtering cognitive model inputs, rendering it incapable of directly intercepting prompt injection, jailbreaks, or internal adversarial model manipulation\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.014690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"6927b614-7521-47ab-825d-e8b2cba8a88d\",\n      \"text\": \"The AgentBound-Bench evaluation framework, comprising compiled benchmark scenarios, baseline ground-truth annotations, out-of-band receipt verification tooling, and deployment documentation, will be released to the community upon conclusion of the initial empirical evaluation campaign.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.034690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_16\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"e4461c45-1918-4955-81b6-972a6d735bc2\",\n      \"text\": \"It isolates the assessment of governance infrastructure from the underlying language model's cognitive capabilities, explicitly measuring whether the runtime architecture safely constrains and cryptographically validates malicious or anomalous agent actions against known ground-truth behaviors.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.974690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_11\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c19a6296-1457-42e9-aecc-48fcb17bea3a\",\n      \"text\": \"Traditional authorization frameworks like Google Zanzibar Open Policy Agent and Cedar focus on entitlement validation for technical permissions while AgentBound establishes authorization as one governance input among independent arbiters evaluating contextual invariants beyond resource-level access control. These frameworks are insufficient for periodic or long-running agentic workloads because they operate under the implicit assumption that a human principal is actively present or within a valid session context when a transaction is initiated, creating systemic vulnerabilities where no human user is present to evaluate ambient risks when execution cycles spontaneously begin, and governance policies may shift between execution cycles; a runtime governance layer is needed to determine whether specific actions should occur under given circumstances.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.024690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"a13b6643-bbf0-4787-803a-72f7d1c81b0b\",\n      \"text\": \"Documentation/specs/templates/examples: CC BY 4.0\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.854196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_31\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"f6bca91d-74f8-40c9-9138-f676e7b5cb76\",\n      \"text\": \"Action rules follow ASI-[A-Z0-9-]+ pattern format\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.844196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_9\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"6f577b37-deb9-4f1d-bdaf-8814da26b4c6\",\n      \"text\": \"Canonical action tuple (operation, resource, parameters, risk, context) abstracts all runtime events where operation identifies semantic intent, resource denotes target, parameters encompass action-specific arguments, risk encapsulates exposure category, and context contains volatile execution metadata\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.974690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_6\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"704df447-ded6-4142-a2ee-5a9636d3ee2b\",\n      \"text\": \"Crosley proposes runtime constitutions as governance files injected into agent context at execution time with selective loading of relevant rules per task, but remains an engineering pattern rather than formally grounded framework and does not connect agent governance to neurocognitive theory or organizational compliance psychology | Involving: Crosley (author) | Remains engineering pattern rather than formally grounded framework; lacks connection to neurocognitive theory and organizational compliance psychology\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.088393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_29\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"f9eaca83-9be5-42f6-a5ca-0b944aad53d0\",\n      \"text\": \"Verifying a receipt requires the artifact payload, corresponding public verification keys, and historical governance artifacts fetched via the receipt's stored references through a validation sequence comprising cryptographic integrity verification, governance reconstruction, and deterministic decision consistency check.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.024690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"348eb115-dbdc-4604-a5cd-876d5960997a\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound-Bench quantifies framework efficacy through four core mathematical and system metrics: governance accuracy (correct decisions/total decisions), violation escape rate (violations executed/total violations), receipt verification success rate, and fine-grained governance latency\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.974690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"abd6e3c4-c200-49e9-a3a7-fe324332269a\",\n      \"text\": \"Runtime requests latest constitution version from Constitution Service before task materialization; task token encapsulates constitution hash, enabling automatic policy propagation without manual reauthorization.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.984690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"046adb4b-3d25-484e-982b-f50d21ada88e\",\n      \"text\": \"Cedar, a new language for expressive, fast, safe, and analyzable authorization introduced by Joseph W Cutler, Craig Disselkoen, Aaron Eline, Shaobo He, Kyle Headley, Michael Hicks, Kesha Hietala, Eleftherios Ioannidis, John Kastner, Anwar Mamat, et al. in PLDI 2024, offering improved authorization capabilities | When: 2024 | Involving: Joseph W Cutler, Craig Disselkoen, Aaron Eline, et al.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.984690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_18\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c6acbadf-dfe3-4cad-b223-2e93013e3dbf\",\n      \"text\": \"Associated with DOI:10.5281/zenodo.17464706 | When: 2026-09-06 | Involving: user\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.844196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_33\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"460744ac-83ed-4c88-bd62-0ed9671f99c9\",\n      \"text\": \"Traditional authorization frameworks (Google Zanzibar, Open Policy Agent, Cedar) focus on entitlement validation for technical permissions to access resources, while AgentBound establishes authorization as one governance input among independent arbiters to evaluate contextual invariants beyond resource-level access control | Involving: Google Zanzibar, Open Policy Agent, Cedar, AgentBound\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.024690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_13\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"0159c929-ee2e-453e-929d-b579bdb8fc24\",\n      \"text\": \"Controls section defines explicit action rules structured as ABAC tuples, each linking directly to evidence fields enumerated in the card: kyc status, risk score, device trust level, beneficiary screening score, escalation id, ensuring every decision is auditable | Involving: Cletus (AI agent), PolicyCard system\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.834196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_16\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d71c59c5-e8fc-445b-83bb-992b55ed9459\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound framework mitigates semantic and behavioral threats after traditional authorization concludes, detecting runtime behavioral policy violations and unauthorized execution bypassing approval workflows.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.994690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d28afb9c-cac8-4486-ae03-f2fbad8a8192\",\n      \"text\": \"Full schema and validator available in public repository and archived via Zenodo (DOI: 10.5281/zenodo.17464706)\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.844196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_10\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"2ed71df4-c897-496e-a98a-c0c497131814\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound operates as a deterministic enforcement layer at the system boundary between authorization and execution, governing how physical actions are evaluated justified and recorded without influencing agent cognition\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.004690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_17\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"88e21077-2e6f-42d8-aa60-8fc54438a2f5\",\n      \"text\": \"OAuth 2.0 token exchange protocol specified by Michael Jones, Anthony Nadalin, Brian Campbell, John Bradley, and Chuck Mortimore in a 2020 technical report\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"efb639e6-4532-4de4-bf99-12becf7f5ac3\",\n      \"text\": \"Adversarially crafted inputs may induce agents to rationalize non-compliant actions as permissible (functional analog of moral disengagement); framework lacks dedicated tamper-resistance layer | Involving: PAGRL agents | Governance robustness under systematic adversarial attack remains open empirical question\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.108393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_27\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"72c99091-4148-46fd-8619-6cad5815794f\",\n      \"text\": \"Attack succeeds when RS(α)=Valid AND α∉IO, exploiting cognitive ambiguity, semantic uncertainty, or incomplete governance rule specifications\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.984690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_5\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"a43a2e87-2a9b-412d-90b3-7f7e75897f56\",\n      \"text\": \"Irreversible actions (purchase orders, supplier commits, replenishment triggers) require explicit human confirmation before execution because they cannot be undone if incorrect | Irreversible actions cannot be undone if incorrect\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.078393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_22\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"83252b8c-b117-421b-9278-63899514adad\",\n      \"text\": \"Constraints aggregate conjunctively and obligations accumulate cumulatively within the decision composition engine, with structural provenance records required to be preserved intact throughout the governance process. | Describes the monotonic invariants governing how parallel judgment vectors unify into singular runtime directives.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.034690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_7\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"6e953bb2-4b86-4eff-b1cd-f8ba84bd0eed\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound-Bench quantifies framework efficacy through four core mathematical and system metrics: governance accuracy (correct decisions/total decisions), violation escape rate (violations executed/total violations), receipt verification success rate, and fine-grained governance latency | When: 2026-09-06\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.974690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_12\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"097c480b-5bba-4d8d-816c-b7aef63d21b3\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound framework provides verifiable behavioral oversight for autonomous AI agents by evaluating proposed actions through three independent authorities (delegated authorization, owner-signed behavioral constitutions, and site action contracts) with conservative composition through a formal decision model determining whether actions should be permitted, reviewed, or denied before execution | When: 2026-09-06 | Involving: Anuj Kaul, Qianlong Lan, Pranay Gupta | Addresses gap in agent infrastructure where delegated authorization cannot determine whether authorized actions should execute under current behavioral and operational context\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_0\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c6c69a12-a267-4249-97d0-f8143486d199\",\n      \"text\": \"The algebraic composition of governance decisions yields four fundamental system properties: authorization preservation, behavioral independence, obligation separation, and replay verifiability. | Represents the guaranteed behavioral guarantees of the AgentBound governance framework.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.984690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_7\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"e6601d88-b0dc-4e17-8000-8a49013b05ee\",\n      \"text\": \"Two-level standing delegation model empowers persistent periodic agents to operate asynchronously under dynamically refreshed governance policies while preserving immediate user revocability and bounding credential exposure\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.994690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_17\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"53796e6b-b18f-433e-8190-551db9236caa\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound builds upon RFC 8693 (OAuth 2.0 Token Exchange) standard for programmatic token transformation and delegation chain security | Provides formal semantic foundations for programmatic token transformation and delegation chain security within distributed environments\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.984690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_14\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c05bbc37-af59-4173-b2f7-1bf9f86026f6\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound framework mitigates semantic and behavioral threats after traditional authorization concludes, detecting runtime behavioral policy violations and unauthorized execution bypassing approval workflows\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.994690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_5\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ddcafc90-f61a-4567-8869-b661983c8f8c\",\n      \"text\": \"This work first formalizes mapping of neurocognitive theories (Dual Process Theory, executive function) to agent governance design and demonstrates practical viability through production-grade case study | Involving: Cletus | Novel contribution bridging cognitive science and AI governance; first explicit neurocognitive grounding for agent governance\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"experience\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.108393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_30\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"41025ece-357f-4d52-8e42-d167004a09f4\",\n      \"text\": \"Verifying a receipt requires only the artifact payload, corresponding public verification keys, and historical governance artifacts fetched via the receipt's stored references through a validation sequence comprising cryptographic integrity verification, governance reconstruction, and deterministic decision consistency check. | Involving: external verifying entities | Enables asynchronous, untrusted entity validation of policy compliance without requiring real-time agent presence\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.024690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_9\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"8512a3ae-3f39-408e-9e06-1a6de45832ac\",\n      \"text\": \"Governance receipt structured as tuple (Action, Governance, Judgments, Outcome, Signatures) capturing delegation token identifier, constitution version number with cryptographic hash, site action contract version identifier, individual typed evaluations, final operational primitive, and asymmetric cryptographic metadata | Involving: system | guarantees global integrity and non-repudiation\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.004690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_8\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c7f73850-8058-4de1-b6d9-311d443326f6\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound is a modular runtime governance and behavioral accountability framework for autonomous agents | Establishes behavioral governance as distinct from identity federation, access control, or training-time model alignment\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_14\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ce770419-1c35-453d-90f5-7152f01d8ee6\",\n      \"text\": \"Agent identifies supply chain risk from unverified supplier not explicitly covered by Rule R4, demonstrating normative generalization through LLM reasoning rather than deterministic rule-matching | Involving: Cletus (agent), Rule R4 | Key innovation: governance embedded in LLM reasoning enables normative generalization beyond explicit rule conditions\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"experience\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.078393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_27\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"e58a9061-ab9e-497c-9703-7e07f5085655\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound trust assumptions require uncompromised core enforcement engine, signing keys, and policy registries, governance evaluations before action dispatch, and governance receipts stored in append-only tamper-evident audit ledger.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.024690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"0cdd3053-9292-40c6-86c2-608b98ed3880\",\n      \"text\": \"Procurement orders exceeding $10,000 require human approval before execution because high-value orders carry significant financial risk | High-value orders carry significant financial risk\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.088393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_22\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"2a66b637-8c11-457d-92ca-22880783a13d\",\n      \"text\": \"Agents can be authenticated, within valid OAuth/IAM scope, and compliant with static access policies yet still execute decisions violating their principal's intent through behavioral deviations including premature financial transactions, unreviewed content publication, sensitive information leakage under adversarial manipulation, or selecting irreversible actions when safe alternatives exist | When: 2026-09-06 | Involving: agent, principal\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.974690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_1\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"83a18411-f4cf-42ee-bfc3-847b2a9b4aee\",\n      \"text\": \"The framework unifies four principals into a non-bypassable governance pipeline: Owner defines intent profile IO and authorizes delegation, Agent proposes actions, AgentBound Service enforces joint multi-authority policy M, Site Resource Provider hosts target resources; the pipeline sequentially evaluates, logs, and validates agent behaviors before execution, with security guarantees assuming strict operational sequence where governance evaluation occurs non-bypassably prior to execution\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.014690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"6adfdf6d-4592-4ade-9534-16646fefb0c0\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound isolates behavior at the action perimeter rather than filtering cognitive model inputs, rendering it incapable of directly intercepting prompt injection, jailbreaks, or internal adversarial model manipulation | When: 2026-09-06 | Involving: AgentBound framework\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.004690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_15\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"e573f354-0387-45e1-ad99-2aa764a9c0f6\",\n      \"text\": \"Agent behavioral contracts: Formal specification and runtime enforcement for reliable autonomous AI agents by Varun Pratap Bhardwaj proposed in arXiv 2026, addressing agent reliability through formal methods and runtime enforcement | When: 2026 | Involving: Varun Pratap Bhardwaj\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.004690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_18\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d050441a-f326-43eb-a163-4e668e67863e\",\n      \"text\": \"Internalized governance (embedded in agent reasoning) produces more robust and generalizable compliance than externally enforced governance systems\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.108393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_26\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"1a1552cc-5a3a-488c-97be-1ae7df0d6873\",\n      \"text\": \"Adaptive governance research aims to create dynamic constitutions capable of updating enforcement constraints in response to observed agent drift without invalidating cryptographic provenance.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.994690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_16\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"73357384-063d-4966-938a-9d796a231a18\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound extends traditional observability by generating atomic governance receipts encapsulating exact policy version states, delegation token identifiers, individual authority judgments, terminal outcomes, and asymmetric cryptographic signatures, allowing auditors to perform historical replay verification and completely reconstruct the original decision algebra out-of-band | When: 2026-09-06 | Involving: AgentBound\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.984690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_15\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"212bf37e-88cd-4ad0-912a-7ea00f8eeac1\",\n      \"text\": \"Agent executes PAGRL, routing to proceed, self-correct, or escalate outcomes\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.098393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_18\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"6ae98d7f-93a9-40cb-86b2-2fce61facff8\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound is implemented as a decoupled, runtime governance layer positioned directly before action execution, serving as a non-bypassable governance checkpoint that every consequential action must pass prior to target system mutation. | Establishes the architectural pattern for out-of-band validation of agent actions.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.994690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_7\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"aae10560-5efd-4918-a840-ba56be792392\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound addresses situations where fully authenticated and legitimately authorized agents execute actions violating principal intent while remaining within delegated access control scope | Demonstrates behavioral governance failures differ from access control breaches\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.994690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_14\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"5c382421-a18e-45dc-a0fe-39b878c0a920\",\n      \"text\": \"Establishing interoperable governance receipt standards represents a critical path toward unified accountability across heterogeneous multi-agent ecosystems.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.014690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_16\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c0a57016-bbb1-4236-b908-061dd5f0c424\",\n      \"text\": \"Establishing interoperable governance receipt standards represents a critical path toward unified accountability across heterogeneous multi-agent ecosystems.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.014690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ab55978c-ac00-4561-a06d-57e251c88cef\",\n      \"text\": \"Combined encryption and Zero-Knowledge Proofs create a confidential assurance layer enabling operational compliance verification across distributed environments without revealing sensitive information, particularly useful in cross-border, regulated, or classified deployments where data-sharing is restricted | Involving: AI agents, oversight agents in cross-border/regulated contexts | Balances compliance verification with data privacy in sensitive deployment scenarios\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.854196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_24\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"09f2e51c-982e-4781-915f-e25f3e58c04d\",\n      \"text\": \"Two-phase countersigning protocol: first, requesting agent signs constructed receipt payload using its private asymmetric key; second, AgentBound enforcement service intercepts and countersigns the entire block covering core receipt payload, agent's signature, and terminal decision vector. | Involving: requesting agent + AgentBound enforcement service | Ensures accountability binding and invalidates verification chain if out-of-band modifications occur to underlying action payload or intermediate governance evaluation\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.974690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_9\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"b483f60c-ba7b-454b-b3dc-7424c0af3151\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound constitutes an administrative governance and behavioral accountability layer rather than a totalizing agent security architecture\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.024690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_5\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"2874a259-3888-463d-9d5e-414e8d41461d\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound introduces standing delegation model that cleanly decouples long-term user authorization from short-lived runtime execution authority for persistent autonomous agents operating without continuous human supervision. | Involving: persistent agents + user authorization | Addresses structural limitation of traditional session-oriented authorization that assumes human presence during transaction initiation\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.994690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_9\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"24515944-a2ee-4e84-a169-c54cebea0f78\",\n      \"text\": \"Formal Runtime Enforcement uses deterministic pipeline to synthesize complementary judgments from independent authorities through conservative decision algebra before action execution\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.984690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_2\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"2f2e1fd7-2706-4ec7-8a38-db1bc37b1f4b\",\n      \"text\": \"Flowr: Scaling up retail supply chain operations through agentic AI in large scale supermarket chains | When: 2026 | Involving: E. Bandara, R. Gore, S. Shetty, P. Siyambalapitiya, S. Rajapakse, I. Kularathna, P. Karunarathna, R. Mukkamala, P. Foytik et al.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.128393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_39\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"7bfde31c-157f-4f75-ace4-4c4157f552b1\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentSpec operates as an external enforcement layer that intercepts agent actions after the agent's reasoning has completed | Involving: AgentSpec\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.168393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_28\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"4d0ba11c-530d-4408-aa01-26fce57e9883\",\n      \"text\": \"Autonomous AI agents are transitioning from passive conversational assistants into high-stakes delegated workloads executing consequential tasks on behalf of human principals.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_16\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"e3d6a13e-b402-4747-aaf5-7ca25f44c03e\",\n      \"text\": \"Autonomous AI agents are transitioning from passive conversational assistants into high-stakes delegated workloads executing consequential tasks on behalf of human principals.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"092f3586-8109-44ea-a414-4396a77bec38\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound's security guarantees assume strict operational sequence where governance evaluation occurs non-bypassably prior to execution; agents capable of directly muting external endpoints without passing through the enforcement layer fall outside the system boundary | When: 2026-09-06 | Involving: AgentBound framework\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.994690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_15\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c8b164c1-2307-4e8c-a04d-1d684218f37d\",\n      \"text\": \"Governance frameworks must incorporate tamper-resistance mechanisms to protect rule integrity against adversarial inputs | Involving: design requirement\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.118393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_11\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"f7a8f54a-c157-4f82-9fbc-157d2c87d3e2\",\n      \"text\": \"Standing Delegation Architecture provides secure, long-running delegation mechanism for periodic autonomous agents preserving policy freshness and granular revocability\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.974690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_2\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"412755b8-775c-4002-89f0-4f58a9562c18\",\n      \"text\": \"Obligations include user notices (fees/limits), explicit consent recording, escalation protocol enforcement, and audit-trail maintenance | Involving: system | Framework requirements for compliance and traceability\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.824196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_18\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"b4e51bad-15c5-4172-bef7-e9f2aeb3c8d7\",\n      \"text\": \"Assurance mappings reference NIST (GOVERN-1, MAP-1, MEASURE-1, MANAGE-1, MANAGE-3), ISO42001 (4,8,9,10), and EU AI Act (AnnexIV-3,4,6,9, Art72) for programmatic traceability.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.834196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d63a2993-c9c3-4086-aa08-39742d8ec488\",\n      \"text\": \"PAGRL enables agents to reason about the intent of governance rules and apply them to situations the rule designer did not anticipate\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.128393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_26\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"745eaa14-37ab-46d1-a51b-3f383205a641\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound introduces a non-bypassable behavioral governance layer between authorization and execution that synthesizes multi-authority policies into deterministic verdicts accompanied by cryptographically signed governance receipts | When: 2026-09-06 | Involving: AgentBound framework\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.984690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_1\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"7725ee7c-c8d0-4d78-ac9a-a6a6058fd260\",\n      \"text\": \"Framework positions Policy Cards as foundation for autonomous assurance ecosystems where policies are computational, verifiable, and privacy-preserving.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.894196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_26\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"f249bcfb-ac2d-4aac-9325-247e6ea3305f\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound evaluates candidate tool invocations non-bypassably before execution, using formal decision algebra to compose intermediate judgments conservatively\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.974690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_17\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    }\n  ],\n  \"trace\": null,\n  \"entities\": null,\n  \"chunks\": null,\n  \"source_facts\": null\n}"
  }
}
