  "content": [
    {
      "text": "{\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"cc5557b5-112d-4947-97ff-0956d800a6fa\",\n      \"text\": \"Aegon implements hardware-attested compliance mechanisms with ledger-bound token architectures and cryptographically signed mobile receipts for safeguarding content extraction and data access controls.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.004690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"36ede801-86d4-4651-a827-d694a4b8f054\",\n      \"text\": \"Aegon implements hardware-attested compliance mechanisms with ledger-bound token architectures and cryptographically signed mobile receipts for safeguarding content extraction and data access controls | Involving: Aegon\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.004690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_13\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ccddb16f-8088-4321-ae2f-a3a22b2d95a0\",\n      \"text\": \"OAuth 2.0 token exchange protocol specified by Michael Jones, Anthony Nadalin, Brian Campbell, John Bradley, and Chuck Mortimore in a 2020 technical report, providing a standard for OAuth 2.0 token exchange | When: 2020 | Involving: Michael Jones, Anthony Nadalin, Brian Campbell, John Bradley, Chuck Mortimore\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_18\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"02110a14-b10c-4bd8-9320-345c886c8a18\",\n      \"text\": \"In Scenario 4, supplier disruption signal activates situational rule R7; inventory replenishment agent intends to substitute disrupted supplier with verified alternative; with R7 active, PAGRL reasons disruption context elevates risk regardless of verified status; compliance decision Escalate; structured escalation message including disruption context, proposed substitution, and reasoning trace transmitted to supply chain manager for review | Involving: inventory replenishment agent, PAGRL system, supply chain manager, MCP governance server | Disruption context elevates risk even for verified suppliers\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.098393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_24\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"9d3abc10-3fb0-42ec-bd9f-59c6b8ca2ce1\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound constitutes an administrative governance and behavioral accountability layer rather than a totalizing agent security architecture, extending traditional observability by generating atomic governance receipts encapsulating exact policy version states, delegation token identifiers, individual authority judgments, terminal outcomes, and asymmetric cryptographic signatures, with every discrete transaction encapsulated within a cryptographically signed governance receipt enabling independent out-of-band decision reconstruction and completely reconstructing the original decision algebra out-of-band. Example governance receipt structure includes Receipt ID r-1024 for Agent ID ads-agent performing Action launch campaign under Delegation Ref d-118 with Constitution Version 3, resulting in Final Decision Human Approval Required with 7 Standing Delegation for Persistent Agents.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.024690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"b184d623-9e11-40de-bada-82b84d4d726a\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound enforces deterministic compliance at the system runtime boundary rather than optimizing model weights at training time, focusing on verifiable system accountability rather than statistical behavioral shaping, fundamentally diverging from optimization-centric model alignment methods where alignment shapes model cognition beforehand and governance evaluates final behavior before system mutation, analogous to the software engineering boundary between application correctness and localized operational policy, without influencing agent cognition.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.004690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"fc319743-84cc-4fa3-85c2-e797f87c66f1\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound is implemented as a decoupled, runtime governance layer positioned directly before action execution, serving as a non-bypassable governance checkpoint that evaluates candidate tool invocations using formal decision algebra to compose intermediate judgments conservatively prior to target system mutation. The agent runtime is treated as untrusted due to potential jailbreaks, requiring out-of-band validation prior to system execution.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.004690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"3ea90a8a-4d85-4e46-9f04-fe8ab9af3abc\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound-Bench is a standardized evaluation framework designed to quantify governance enforcement correctness, multi-authority composition behavior, and policy provenance integrity.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_11\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ba1f50b8-205c-4432-b2f8-991f7ab8214d\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound-Bench is a standardized evaluation framework designed to quantify governance enforcement correctness, multi-authority composition behavior, and policy provenance integrity.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d25b8049-1949-47f6-b085-f2a450ca765c\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound's two-level delegation: standing delegation (long-term, human-authorized) authorizes short-lived task delegation per execution cycle; standing delegations restricted from direct execution, serving as root of authority for runtime engine, empowering persistent periodic agents to operate asynchronously under dynamically refreshed governance policies while preserving immediate user revocability and bounding credential exposure.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.994690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c19a6296-1457-42e9-aecc-48fcb17bea3a\",\n      \"text\": \"Traditional authorization frameworks like Google Zanzibar Open Policy Agent and Cedar focus on entitlement validation for technical permissions while AgentBound establishes authorization as one governance input among independent arbiters evaluating contextual invariants beyond resource-level access control. These frameworks are insufficient for periodic or long-running agentic workloads because they operate under the implicit assumption that a human principal is actively present or within a valid session context when a transaction is initiated, creating systemic vulnerabilities where no human user is present to evaluate ambient risks when execution cycles spontaneously begin, and governance policies may shift between execution cycles; a runtime governance layer is needed to determine whether specific actions should occur under given circumstances.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.024690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"2554d39d-574e-4142-8295-4320fd5ccf86\",\n      \"text\": \"Schema was validated on September 6, 2026 | When: 2026-09-06\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.814196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_7\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"b1d52bf4-f371-46c0-bd2c-c747549de35b\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound is out of scope for adversarial prompt injection attacks, direct LLM jailbreaks, baseline model alignment failures, and hardware-level side-channel data exfiltration, as AgentBound isolates behavior at the action perimeter rather than filtering cognitive model inputs, rendering it incapable of directly intercepting prompt injection, jailbreaks, or internal adversarial model manipulation\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.014690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"88c903f8-7876-4950-9566-6ca94cc0d1f7\",\n      \"text\": \"Three conditions trigger escalation rather than self-correction: (1) categorical prohibition by rule where no intent revision makes it compliant, (2) irreversible action requiring human confirmation, (3) genuine uncertainty about permissibility where ambiguous cases should be escalated\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.118393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_16\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"6927b614-7521-47ab-825d-e8b2cba8a88d\",\n      \"text\": \"The AgentBound-Bench evaluation framework, comprising compiled benchmark scenarios, baseline ground-truth annotations, out-of-band receipt verification tooling, and deployment documentation, will be released to the community upon conclusion of the initial empirical evaluation campaign.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.034690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_16\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"f9eaca83-9be5-42f6-a5ca-0b944aad53d0\",\n      \"text\": \"Verifying a receipt requires the artifact payload, corresponding public verification keys, and historical governance artifacts fetched via the receipt's stored references through a validation sequence comprising cryptographic integrity verification, governance reconstruction, and deterministic decision consistency check.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.024690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"5708b4f0-6ad9-412e-a6a0-7a6fe2e210d9\",\n      \"text\": \"Action receives physical execution clearance if and only if the final composed decision evaluates to Permit AND all accumulated runtime obligations are fully satisfied; constraints aggregate conjunctively and obligations accumulate cumulatively; satisfying review obligations fulfills behavioral policy requirements but does not alter the underlying authorization boundary. Structural provenance records are required to be preserved intact throughout the governance process.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.034690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"96f19be1-305e-492e-949d-f18c328789a6\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound addresses a fundamentally orthogonal axis to conventional benchmarks, focusing on runtime governance mechanisms rather than task optimization or task completion rates.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.014690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_11\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"8c975716-819f-478f-9c94-4a25bb367bfc\",\n      \"text\": \"Obligations are auditable commitments linked to evidence fields under specified conditions, including mandatory notifications, consent checks, and safety statements.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.844196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"460744ac-83ed-4c88-bd62-0ed9671f99c9\",\n      \"text\": \"Traditional authorization frameworks (Google Zanzibar, Open Policy Agent, Cedar) focus on entitlement validation for technical permissions to access resources, while AgentBound establishes authorization as one governance input among independent arbiters to evaluate contextual invariants beyond resource-level access control | Involving: Google Zanzibar, Open Policy Agent, Cedar, AgentBound\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.024690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_13\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"88e21077-2e6f-42d8-aa60-8fc54438a2f5\",\n      \"text\": \"OAuth 2.0 token exchange protocol specified by Michael Jones, Anthony Nadalin, Brian Campbell, John Bradley, and Chuck Mortimore in a 2020 technical report\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"348eb115-dbdc-4604-a5cd-876d5960997a\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound-Bench quantifies framework efficacy through four core mathematical and system metrics: governance accuracy (correct decisions/total decisions), violation escape rate (violations executed/total violations), receipt verification success rate, and fine-grained governance latency\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.974690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d050441a-f326-43eb-a163-4e668e67863e\",\n      \"text\": \"Internalized governance (embedded in agent reasoning) produces more robust and generalizable compliance than externally enforced governance systems\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.108393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_26\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"72c99091-4148-46fd-8619-6cad5815794f\",\n      \"text\": \"Attack succeeds when RS(α)=Valid AND α∉IO, exploiting cognitive ambiguity, semantic uncertainty, or incomplete governance rule specifications\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.984690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_5\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"8ad3eb92-f404-4310-b09c-b8e40db21963\",\n      \"text\": \"Obligations defined as auditable commitments linked to evidence fields under specified conditions, including mandatory notifications, consent checks, and safety statements\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.844196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_8\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"a56f4d03-088f-4404-8927-06762407570d\",\n      \"text\": \"In Scenario 3, agent intends to contact unverified supplier not in verified registry; PAGRL retrieves rules R2, R4, R6; agent reasons contacting unverified supplier violates R4 but task can use verified alternative; compliance decision Self-Correct; agent revises intent to nearest verified supplier and re-enters PAGRL producing Proceed decision; original intent, correction reasoning, and revised intent logged to MCP governance server | Involving: supply chain agent, PAGRL system, MCP governance server, verified supplier | Unverified supplier contact violates compliance rules but alternative exists\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.088393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_24\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"f6bca91d-74f8-40c9-9138-f676e7b5cb76\",\n      \"text\": \"Action rules follow ASI-[A-Z0-9-]+ pattern format\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.844196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_9\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"9f47ee44-41e2-448c-8e79-61331aeda896\",\n      \"text\": \"RFC3339 timestamp format required for temporal fields\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.834196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_9\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"2cfeb6c9-0b76-4b8c-94a4-33c598e569df\",\n      \"text\": \"Task delegation short-lived credential derived from standing delegation boundaries, encapsulating task ID, constrained operational scope, issuance timestamp, short-lived expiration threshold, and governing constitution reference.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.974690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d71c59c5-e8fc-445b-83bb-992b55ed9459\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound framework mitigates semantic and behavioral threats after traditional authorization concludes, detecting runtime behavioral policy violations and unauthorized execution bypassing approval workflows.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.994690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ab55978c-ac00-4561-a06d-57e251c88cef\",\n      \"text\": \"Combined encryption and Zero-Knowledge Proofs create a confidential assurance layer enabling operational compliance verification across distributed environments without revealing sensitive information, particularly useful in cross-border, regulated, or classified deployments where data-sharing is restricted | Involving: AI agents, oversight agents in cross-border/regulated contexts | Balances compliance verification with data privacy in sensitive deployment scenarios\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.854196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_24\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"473f8ebd-17ea-4343-b2c0-40c2024d957f\",\n      \"text\": \"Rules should be specific enough for deterministic compliance while remaining general enough to cover novel situations; layered architecture supports this with broad global rules and precise agent-specific rules\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.098393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_16\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d28afb9c-cac8-4486-ae03-f2fbad8a8192\",\n      \"text\": \"Full schema and validator available in public repository and archived via Zenodo (DOI: 10.5281/zenodo.17464706)\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.844196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_10\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"7fa86949-9d37-41b5-9c5b-223a68f61e36\",\n      \"text\": \"Banks, hospitals, and public agencies require guarantees that AI system decisions are reliable\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.844196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_4\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"83252b8c-b117-421b-9278-63899514adad\",\n      \"text\": \"Constraints aggregate conjunctively and obligations accumulate cumulatively within the decision composition engine, with structural provenance records required to be preserved intact throughout the governance process. | Describes the monotonic invariants governing how parallel judgment vectors unify into singular runtime directives.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.034690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_7\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"2ed71df4-c897-496e-a98a-c0c497131814\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound operates as a deterministic enforcement layer at the system boundary between authorization and execution, governing how physical actions are evaluated justified and recorded without influencing agent cognition\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.004690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_17\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c05bbc37-af59-4173-b2f7-1bf9f86026f6\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound framework mitigates semantic and behavioral threats after traditional authorization concludes, detecting runtime behavioral policy violations and unauthorized execution bypassing approval workflows\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.994690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_5\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"6adfdf6d-4592-4ade-9534-16646fefb0c0\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound isolates behavior at the action perimeter rather than filtering cognitive model inputs, rendering it incapable of directly intercepting prompt injection, jailbreaks, or internal adversarial model manipulation | When: 2026-09-06 | Involving: AgentBound framework\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.004690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_15\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"2a66b637-8c11-457d-92ca-22880783a13d\",\n      \"text\": \"Agents can be authenticated, within valid OAuth/IAM scope, and compliant with static access policies yet still execute decisions violating their principal's intent through behavioral deviations including premature financial transactions, unreviewed content publication, sensitive information leakage under adversarial manipulation, or selecting irreversible actions when safe alternatives exist | When: 2026-09-06 | Involving: agent, principal\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.974690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_1\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"caab4851-86fb-43b7-8aac-3dbbfc844b01\",\n      \"text\": \"Pre-Action Governance Reasoning Loop (PA-GRL) proposed as formal mechanism through which agents consult structured governance rule sets before every consequential action, determining whether to proceed, self-correct, or escalate to human oversight, mirroring human deliberative compliance behavior | Involving: agents/researchers | To formalize human-like compliance behavior in AI agent governance\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.088393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_3\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"a43a2e87-2a9b-412d-90b3-7f7e75897f56\",\n      \"text\": \"Irreversible actions (purchase orders, supplier commits, replenishment triggers) require explicit human confirmation before execution because they cannot be undone if incorrect | Irreversible actions cannot be undone if incorrect\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.078393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_22\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c6acbadf-dfe3-4cad-b223-2e93013e3dbf\",\n      \"text\": \"Associated with DOI:10.5281/zenodo.17464706 | When: 2026-09-06 | Involving: user\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.844196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_33\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"5c382421-a18e-45dc-a0fe-39b878c0a920\",\n      \"text\": \"Establishing interoperable governance receipt standards represents a critical path toward unified accountability across heterogeneous multi-agent ecosystems.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.014690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_16\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"41025ece-357f-4d52-8e42-d167004a09f4\",\n      \"text\": \"Verifying a receipt requires only the artifact payload, corresponding public verification keys, and historical governance artifacts fetched via the receipt's stored references through a validation sequence comprising cryptographic integrity verification, governance reconstruction, and deterministic decision consistency check. | Involving: external verifying entities | Enables asynchronous, untrusted entity validation of policy compliance without requiring real-time agent presence\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.024690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_9\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c6c69a12-a267-4249-97d0-f8143486d199\",\n      \"text\": \"The algebraic composition of governance decisions yields four fundamental system properties: authorization preservation, behavioral independence, obligation separation, and replay verifiability. | Represents the guaranteed behavioral guarantees of the AgentBound governance framework.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.984690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_7\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"b4e51bad-15c5-4172-bef7-e9f2aeb3c8d7\",\n      \"text\": \"Assurance mappings reference NIST (GOVERN-1, MAP-1, MEASURE-1, MANAGE-1, MANAGE-3), ISO42001 (4,8,9,10), and EU AI Act (AnnexIV-3,4,6,9, Art72) for programmatic traceability.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.834196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"b90a0113-cf8a-4db5-bf2c-30ca8d64327c\",\n      \"text\": \"The framework achieved 95% compliance decision accuracy (38/40 correct decisions) across 40 evaluation runs, with two errors from edge-case input phrasings producing ambiguous permissibility reasoning | Involving: the framework\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.088393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_25\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"1a1552cc-5a3a-488c-97be-1ae7df0d6873\",\n      \"text\": \"Adaptive governance research aims to create dynamic constitutions capable of updating enforcement constraints in response to observed agent drift without invalidating cryptographic provenance.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.994690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_16\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"f9f4ff40-ac7c-4c79-9e4d-6d062d4af526\",\n      \"text\": \"Rule hierarchy structure: Layer 2 (workflow-specific), Layer 3 (agent-specific), Layer 4 (situational), all extending global rules without overriding them\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.078393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_15\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ddcafc90-f61a-4567-8869-b661983c8f8c\",\n      \"text\": \"This work first formalizes mapping of neurocognitive theories (Dual Process Theory, executive function) to agent governance design and demonstrates practical viability through production-grade case study | Involving: Cletus | Novel contribution bridging cognitive science and AI governance; first explicit neurocognitive grounding for agent governance\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"experience\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.108393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_30\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"0bef11c9-21a3-4b35-852e-408f35185b30\",\n      \"text\": \"In collaborative scenarios (e.g., Clinical Trial Coordinator), agents exchange digital attestations representing partial fulfillment of obligations (e.g., data anonymization, consent verification, statistical integrity), verifiable by peers and aggregable into a composite assurance graph enabling federated compliance | Involving: AI agents in collaborative scenarios | Enables federated compliance where trust emerges from a network of mutually validating agents\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.834196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_24\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"0159c929-ee2e-453e-929d-b579bdb8fc24\",\n      \"text\": \"Controls section defines explicit action rules structured as ABAC tuples, each linking directly to evidence fields enumerated in the card: kyc status, risk score, device trust level, beneficiary screening score, escalation id, ensuring every decision is auditable | Involving: Cletus (AI agent), PolicyCard system\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.834196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_16\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"e6601d88-b0dc-4e17-8000-8a49013b05ee\",\n      \"text\": \"Two-level standing delegation model empowers persistent periodic agents to operate asynchronously under dynamically refreshed governance policies while preserving immediate user revocability and bounding credential exposure\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.994690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_17\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"6e953bb2-4b86-4eff-b1cd-f8ba84bd0eed\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound-Bench quantifies framework efficacy through four core mathematical and system metrics: governance accuracy (correct decisions/total decisions), violation escape rate (violations executed/total violations), receipt verification success rate, and fine-grained governance latency | When: 2026-09-06\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.974690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_12\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ce770419-1c35-453d-90f5-7152f01d8ee6\",\n      \"text\": \"Agent identifies supply chain risk from unverified supplier not explicitly covered by Rule R4, demonstrating normative generalization through LLM reasoning rather than deterministic rule-matching | Involving: Cletus (agent), Rule R4 | Key innovation: governance embedded in LLM reasoning enables normative generalization beyond explicit rule conditions\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"experience\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.078393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_27\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"53796e6b-b18f-433e-8190-551db9236caa\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound builds upon RFC 8693 (OAuth 2.0 Token Exchange) standard for programmatic token transformation and delegation chain security | Provides formal semantic foundations for programmatic token transformation and delegation chain security within distributed environments\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.984690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_14\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c7f73850-8058-4de1-b6d9-311d443326f6\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound is a modular runtime governance and behavioral accountability framework for autonomous agents | Establishes behavioral governance as distinct from identity federation, access control, or training-time model alignment\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_14\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"31e84f05-37b4-44ea-90bc-428e742c36e4\",\n      \"text\": \"Each schema section can be traced to clauses/functions within frameworks, enabling automated validation of compliance claims\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.824196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_4\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"aba7ba91-274e-4a6c-b6b9-2c9774278c90\",\n      \"text\": \"Audit Service provides observability for system-wide accountability and non-repudiation by appending governance events and persisting signed receipts to append-only audit ledger | Involving: system | observability substrate required for system-wide accountability\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.994690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_8\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"9fbb19db-7caa-4b72-8296-9596af0d17b4\",\n      \"text\": \"Training-time alignment methods embed behavioral principles into model weights during training but produce probabilistic rather than deterministic compliance, with alignment degrading as agents operate in open-ended, adversarial, or out-of-distribution environments | Involving: AI models, training systems\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.098393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_2\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"20e86df0-5fce-49d4-9a12-65da8fdd0d32\",\n      \"text\": \"Financial institutions operate within stringent regulatory frameworks such as PSD2 (EU), AMLD (Anti-Money Laundering Directive), and jurisdictional Know-Your-Customer (KYC) mandates, requiring automated payment agents to operate within well-defined authorization and escalation boundaries | Involving: Cletus (AI agent), financial institutions, automated payment agents\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.854196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_16\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c8b164c1-2307-4e8c-a04d-1d684218f37d\",\n      \"text\": \"Governance frameworks must incorporate tamper-resistance mechanisms to protect rule integrity against adversarial inputs | Involving: design requirement\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.118393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_11\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"029b038b-467e-4e49-b552-f72e76fb3104\",\n      \"text\": \"Five core security invariants yielded by the verification architecture: integrity, non-repudiation, policy provenance, replay verifiability, and decision transparency. | Involving: system architecture | Defines the security properties guaranteed by the receipt verification system\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.984690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_9\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"320db885-6eb2-463f-b9ff-c64bbcc0750b\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound fundamentally diverges from optimization-centric model alignment methods, where alignment shapes model cognition beforehand and governance evaluates final behavior before system mutation, analogous to the software engineering boundary between application correctness and localized operational policy | When: 2026-09-06 | Involving: AgentBound framework\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_15\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"efb639e6-4532-4de4-bf99-12becf7f5ac3\",\n      \"text\": \"Adversarially crafted inputs may induce agents to rationalize non-compliant actions as permissible (functional analog of moral disengagement); framework lacks dedicated tamper-resistance layer | Involving: PAGRL agents | Governance robustness under systematic adversarial attack remains open empirical question\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.108393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_27\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"b7dfb392-ee7d-44f1-ba2c-ba092c2a85b7\",\n      \"text\": \"Work intersects four research areas: agentic AI governance and safety, training-time alignment, organizational compliance psychology, and neuroscience of decision-making | Involving: work\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.138393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_28\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"7aa44718-fe39-4e17-873e-0b7fab2170fb\",\n      \"text\": \"Validates consistency between sections by cross-checking evidence fields listed in monitoring against those referenced under obligations or controls\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.824196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_10\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"6ae98d7f-93a9-40cb-86b2-2fce61facff8\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound is implemented as a decoupled, runtime governance layer positioned directly before action execution, serving as a non-bypassable governance checkpoint that every consequential action must pass prior to target system mutation. | Establishes the architectural pattern for out-of-band validation of agent actions.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.994690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_7\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"1e7d8b48-e706-4824-8116-b4a26566f704\",\n      \"text\": \"External governance systems achieve high compliance within their defined rule scope but cannot generalize to novel situations not explicitly covered by their rule specifications\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.118393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_26\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"02b192ec-044a-49ca-8a16-3c69c0c0cb33\",\n      \"text\": \"Schema contains 'controls' section requiring 'action_rules' array with minimum 1 item\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.814196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_14\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"8644e70e-b152-4f7b-ad01-2aa2ed7b097c\",\n      \"text\": \"Validation performed using Ajv8.x JSON Schema validator with custom linting logic enforcing schema conformance and semantic relationships between fields beyond structural validation\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.904196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_8\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"83a18411-f4cf-42ee-bfc3-847b2a9b4aee\",\n      \"text\": \"The framework unifies four principals into a non-bypassable governance pipeline: Owner defines intent profile IO and authorizes delegation, Agent proposes actions, AgentBound Service enforces joint multi-authority policy M, Site Resource Provider hosts target resources; the pipeline sequentially evaluates, logs, and validates agent behaviors before execution, with security guarantees assuming strict operational sequence where governance evaluation occurs non-bypassably prior to execution\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.014690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"b483f60c-ba7b-454b-b3dc-7424c0af3151\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound constitutes an administrative governance and behavioral accountability layer rather than a totalizing agent security architecture\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.024690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_5\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"4a71566e-6bd0-4445-9378-0e1a9bbe3c92\",\n      \"text\": \"The Policy Card framework enables verifiable compliance for autonomous agents through automatic validation, version control, and integration with runtime enforcement or continuous-audit pipelines, forming a foundation for distributed assurance in multi-agent ecosystems | Involving: autonomous agents\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.834196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_0\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"42694569-e601-4d09-b194-5f7e1f9199ab\",\n      \"text\": \"RS(α) is the standard access control and delegation verification function for site S under delegated authorization scope Gauth\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_5\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"6140b11f-4488-4a31-aafc-96bb9ad59836\",\n      \"text\": \"The reasoning trace log is queryable through the MCP interface, enabling human operators to inspect governance decisions in real time and supporting post-hoc compliance audit and review.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.108393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_19\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"8c03b367-8fac-4b70-908b-17a0cbb698d0\",\n      \"text\": \"Validates that every rule in controls uses permitted effect tokens (allow, deny, or require escalation) preventing logically inconsistent or incomplete policy definitions\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.834196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_10\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"5b29fff7-d4db-4bce-a7f3-0f6c62489bf6\",\n      \"text\": \"The Policy Card schema is formally specified using JSON Schema 2020-12, defining mandatory fields including required top-level keys, permitted data types, pattern constraints, and enumerations governing how valid cards must be authored and validated, with additionalProperties: false preventing unspecified properties.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.914196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"f37c14f6-560c-44e6-bd8a-0fd60f5a3098\",\n      \"text\": \"Receipt generation proceeds via a deterministic four-stage pipeline: evaluation, raw payload construction, two-phase ordered countersigning protocol, and verification architecture enabling asynchronous policy compliance validation by external untrusted entities. | Involving: system architecture | Establishes the complete receipt generation and verification process with five core security invariants\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_9\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d8849b46-627f-4b04-93df-0900883c23a1\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound enforces deterministic compliance at the system runtime boundary rather than optimizing model weights at training time, focusing on verifiable system accountability rather than statistical behavioral shaping | Involving: AgentBound\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.984690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_13\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"f249bcfb-ac2d-4aac-9325-247e6ea3305f\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound evaluates candidate tool invocations non-bypassably before execution, using formal decision algebra to compose intermediate judgments conservatively\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.974690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_17\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"8512a3ae-3f39-408e-9e06-1a6de45832ac\",\n      \"text\": \"Governance receipt structured as tuple (Action, Governance, Judgments, Outcome, Signatures) capturing delegation token identifier, constitution version number with cryptographic hash, site action contract version identifier, individual typed evaluations, final operational primitive, and asymmetric cryptographic metadata | Involving: system | guarantees global integrity and non-repudiation\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.004690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_8\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"b1286291-ff34-4f00-bff9-45d32b965ac2\",\n      \"text\": \"Exception EX-TRIAGE-REMOTE-CLINIC-OVERRIDE for remote clinical sites is time-bound to 12 hours, requiring two person approval and reference as evidence\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.834196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_19\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"9f4b9ed0-311d-491e-b0e5-df484fdf0191\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound framework integrates three governance authorities (delegated authorization, owner-signed behavioral constitutions, and site action contracts) into a unified multi-authority decision engine for autonomous systems.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d24ba464-8811-43b3-9a48-63d218f8f051\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound's two-level delegation: standing delegation (long-term, human-authorized) authorizes short-lived task delegation per execution cycle; standing delegations restricted from direct execution, serving as root of authority for runtime engine | Involving: Cletus\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"experience\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_10\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"097c480b-5bba-4d8d-816c-b7aef63d21b3\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound framework provides verifiable behavioral oversight for autonomous AI agents by evaluating proposed actions through three independent authorities (delegated authorization, owner-signed behavioral constitutions, and site action contracts) with conservative composition through a formal decision model determining whether actions should be permitted, reviewed, or denied before execution | When: 2026-09-06 | Involving: Anuj Kaul, Qianlong Lan, Pranay Gupta | Addresses gap in agent infrastructure where delegated authorization cannot determine whether authorized actions should execute under current behavioral and operational context\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_0\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    }\n  ],\n  \"trace\": null,\n  \"entities\": null,\n  \"chunks\": null,\n  \"source_facts\": null\n}",
      "type": "text"
    }
  ],
  "isError": false,
  "structuredContent": {
    "result": "{\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"cc5557b5-112d-4947-97ff-0956d800a6fa\",\n      \"text\": \"Aegon implements hardware-attested compliance mechanisms with ledger-bound token architectures and cryptographically signed mobile receipts for safeguarding content extraction and data access controls.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.004690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"36ede801-86d4-4651-a827-d694a4b8f054\",\n      \"text\": \"Aegon implements hardware-attested compliance mechanisms with ledger-bound token architectures and cryptographically signed mobile receipts for safeguarding content extraction and data access controls | Involving: Aegon\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.004690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_13\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ccddb16f-8088-4321-ae2f-a3a22b2d95a0\",\n      \"text\": \"OAuth 2.0 token exchange protocol specified by Michael Jones, Anthony Nadalin, Brian Campbell, John Bradley, and Chuck Mortimore in a 2020 technical report, providing a standard for OAuth 2.0 token exchange | When: 2020 | Involving: Michael Jones, Anthony Nadalin, Brian Campbell, John Bradley, Chuck Mortimore\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_18\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"02110a14-b10c-4bd8-9320-345c886c8a18\",\n      \"text\": \"In Scenario 4, supplier disruption signal activates situational rule R7; inventory replenishment agent intends to substitute disrupted supplier with verified alternative; with R7 active, PAGRL reasons disruption context elevates risk regardless of verified status; compliance decision Escalate; structured escalation message including disruption context, proposed substitution, and reasoning trace transmitted to supply chain manager for review | Involving: inventory replenishment agent, PAGRL system, supply chain manager, MCP governance server | Disruption context elevates risk even for verified suppliers\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.098393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_24\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"9d3abc10-3fb0-42ec-bd9f-59c6b8ca2ce1\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound constitutes an administrative governance and behavioral accountability layer rather than a totalizing agent security architecture, extending traditional observability by generating atomic governance receipts encapsulating exact policy version states, delegation token identifiers, individual authority judgments, terminal outcomes, and asymmetric cryptographic signatures, with every discrete transaction encapsulated within a cryptographically signed governance receipt enabling independent out-of-band decision reconstruction and completely reconstructing the original decision algebra out-of-band. Example governance receipt structure includes Receipt ID r-1024 for Agent ID ads-agent performing Action launch campaign under Delegation Ref d-118 with Constitution Version 3, resulting in Final Decision Human Approval Required with 7 Standing Delegation for Persistent Agents.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.024690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"b184d623-9e11-40de-bada-82b84d4d726a\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound enforces deterministic compliance at the system runtime boundary rather than optimizing model weights at training time, focusing on verifiable system accountability rather than statistical behavioral shaping, fundamentally diverging from optimization-centric model alignment methods where alignment shapes model cognition beforehand and governance evaluates final behavior before system mutation, analogous to the software engineering boundary between application correctness and localized operational policy, without influencing agent cognition.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.004690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"fc319743-84cc-4fa3-85c2-e797f87c66f1\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound is implemented as a decoupled, runtime governance layer positioned directly before action execution, serving as a non-bypassable governance checkpoint that evaluates candidate tool invocations using formal decision algebra to compose intermediate judgments conservatively prior to target system mutation. The agent runtime is treated as untrusted due to potential jailbreaks, requiring out-of-band validation prior to system execution.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.004690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"3ea90a8a-4d85-4e46-9f04-fe8ab9af3abc\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound-Bench is a standardized evaluation framework designed to quantify governance enforcement correctness, multi-authority composition behavior, and policy provenance integrity.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_11\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ba1f50b8-205c-4432-b2f8-991f7ab8214d\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound-Bench is a standardized evaluation framework designed to quantify governance enforcement correctness, multi-authority composition behavior, and policy provenance integrity.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d25b8049-1949-47f6-b085-f2a450ca765c\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound's two-level delegation: standing delegation (long-term, human-authorized) authorizes short-lived task delegation per execution cycle; standing delegations restricted from direct execution, serving as root of authority for runtime engine, empowering persistent periodic agents to operate asynchronously under dynamically refreshed governance policies while preserving immediate user revocability and bounding credential exposure.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.994690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c19a6296-1457-42e9-aecc-48fcb17bea3a\",\n      \"text\": \"Traditional authorization frameworks like Google Zanzibar Open Policy Agent and Cedar focus on entitlement validation for technical permissions while AgentBound establishes authorization as one governance input among independent arbiters evaluating contextual invariants beyond resource-level access control. These frameworks are insufficient for periodic or long-running agentic workloads because they operate under the implicit assumption that a human principal is actively present or within a valid session context when a transaction is initiated, creating systemic vulnerabilities where no human user is present to evaluate ambient risks when execution cycles spontaneously begin, and governance policies may shift between execution cycles; a runtime governance layer is needed to determine whether specific actions should occur under given circumstances.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.024690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"2554d39d-574e-4142-8295-4320fd5ccf86\",\n      \"text\": \"Schema was validated on September 6, 2026 | When: 2026-09-06\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.814196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_7\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"b1d52bf4-f371-46c0-bd2c-c747549de35b\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound is out of scope for adversarial prompt injection attacks, direct LLM jailbreaks, baseline model alignment failures, and hardware-level side-channel data exfiltration, as AgentBound isolates behavior at the action perimeter rather than filtering cognitive model inputs, rendering it incapable of directly intercepting prompt injection, jailbreaks, or internal adversarial model manipulation\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.014690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"88c903f8-7876-4950-9566-6ca94cc0d1f7\",\n      \"text\": \"Three conditions trigger escalation rather than self-correction: (1) categorical prohibition by rule where no intent revision makes it compliant, (2) irreversible action requiring human confirmation, (3) genuine uncertainty about permissibility where ambiguous cases should be escalated\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.118393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_16\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"6927b614-7521-47ab-825d-e8b2cba8a88d\",\n      \"text\": \"The AgentBound-Bench evaluation framework, comprising compiled benchmark scenarios, baseline ground-truth annotations, out-of-band receipt verification tooling, and deployment documentation, will be released to the community upon conclusion of the initial empirical evaluation campaign.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.034690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_16\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"f9eaca83-9be5-42f6-a5ca-0b944aad53d0\",\n      \"text\": \"Verifying a receipt requires the artifact payload, corresponding public verification keys, and historical governance artifacts fetched via the receipt's stored references through a validation sequence comprising cryptographic integrity verification, governance reconstruction, and deterministic decision consistency check.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.024690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"5708b4f0-6ad9-412e-a6a0-7a6fe2e210d9\",\n      \"text\": \"Action receives physical execution clearance if and only if the final composed decision evaluates to Permit AND all accumulated runtime obligations are fully satisfied; constraints aggregate conjunctively and obligations accumulate cumulatively; satisfying review obligations fulfills behavioral policy requirements but does not alter the underlying authorization boundary. Structural provenance records are required to be preserved intact throughout the governance process.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.034690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"96f19be1-305e-492e-949d-f18c328789a6\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound addresses a fundamentally orthogonal axis to conventional benchmarks, focusing on runtime governance mechanisms rather than task optimization or task completion rates.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.014690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_11\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"8c975716-819f-478f-9c94-4a25bb367bfc\",\n      \"text\": \"Obligations are auditable commitments linked to evidence fields under specified conditions, including mandatory notifications, consent checks, and safety statements.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.844196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"460744ac-83ed-4c88-bd62-0ed9671f99c9\",\n      \"text\": \"Traditional authorization frameworks (Google Zanzibar, Open Policy Agent, Cedar) focus on entitlement validation for technical permissions to access resources, while AgentBound establishes authorization as one governance input among independent arbiters to evaluate contextual invariants beyond resource-level access control | Involving: Google Zanzibar, Open Policy Agent, Cedar, AgentBound\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.024690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_13\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"88e21077-2e6f-42d8-aa60-8fc54438a2f5\",\n      \"text\": \"OAuth 2.0 token exchange protocol specified by Michael Jones, Anthony Nadalin, Brian Campbell, John Bradley, and Chuck Mortimore in a 2020 technical report\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"348eb115-dbdc-4604-a5cd-876d5960997a\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound-Bench quantifies framework efficacy through four core mathematical and system metrics: governance accuracy (correct decisions/total decisions), violation escape rate (violations executed/total violations), receipt verification success rate, and fine-grained governance latency\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.974690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d050441a-f326-43eb-a163-4e668e67863e\",\n      \"text\": \"Internalized governance (embedded in agent reasoning) produces more robust and generalizable compliance than externally enforced governance systems\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.108393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_26\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"72c99091-4148-46fd-8619-6cad5815794f\",\n      \"text\": \"Attack succeeds when RS(α)=Valid AND α∉IO, exploiting cognitive ambiguity, semantic uncertainty, or incomplete governance rule specifications\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.984690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_5\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"8ad3eb92-f404-4310-b09c-b8e40db21963\",\n      \"text\": \"Obligations defined as auditable commitments linked to evidence fields under specified conditions, including mandatory notifications, consent checks, and safety statements\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.844196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_8\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"a56f4d03-088f-4404-8927-06762407570d\",\n      \"text\": \"In Scenario 3, agent intends to contact unverified supplier not in verified registry; PAGRL retrieves rules R2, R4, R6; agent reasons contacting unverified supplier violates R4 but task can use verified alternative; compliance decision Self-Correct; agent revises intent to nearest verified supplier and re-enters PAGRL producing Proceed decision; original intent, correction reasoning, and revised intent logged to MCP governance server | Involving: supply chain agent, PAGRL system, MCP governance server, verified supplier | Unverified supplier contact violates compliance rules but alternative exists\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.088393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_24\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"f6bca91d-74f8-40c9-9138-f676e7b5cb76\",\n      \"text\": \"Action rules follow ASI-[A-Z0-9-]+ pattern format\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.844196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_9\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"9f47ee44-41e2-448c-8e79-61331aeda896\",\n      \"text\": \"RFC3339 timestamp format required for temporal fields\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.834196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_9\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"2cfeb6c9-0b76-4b8c-94a4-33c598e569df\",\n      \"text\": \"Task delegation short-lived credential derived from standing delegation boundaries, encapsulating task ID, constrained operational scope, issuance timestamp, short-lived expiration threshold, and governing constitution reference.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.974690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d71c59c5-e8fc-445b-83bb-992b55ed9459\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound framework mitigates semantic and behavioral threats after traditional authorization concludes, detecting runtime behavioral policy violations and unauthorized execution bypassing approval workflows.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.994690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ab55978c-ac00-4561-a06d-57e251c88cef\",\n      \"text\": \"Combined encryption and Zero-Knowledge Proofs create a confidential assurance layer enabling operational compliance verification across distributed environments without revealing sensitive information, particularly useful in cross-border, regulated, or classified deployments where data-sharing is restricted | Involving: AI agents, oversight agents in cross-border/regulated contexts | Balances compliance verification with data privacy in sensitive deployment scenarios\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.854196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_24\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"473f8ebd-17ea-4343-b2c0-40c2024d957f\",\n      \"text\": \"Rules should be specific enough for deterministic compliance while remaining general enough to cover novel situations; layered architecture supports this with broad global rules and precise agent-specific rules\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.098393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_16\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d28afb9c-cac8-4486-ae03-f2fbad8a8192\",\n      \"text\": \"Full schema and validator available in public repository and archived via Zenodo (DOI: 10.5281/zenodo.17464706)\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.844196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_10\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"7fa86949-9d37-41b5-9c5b-223a68f61e36\",\n      \"text\": \"Banks, hospitals, and public agencies require guarantees that AI system decisions are reliable\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.844196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_4\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"83252b8c-b117-421b-9278-63899514adad\",\n      \"text\": \"Constraints aggregate conjunctively and obligations accumulate cumulatively within the decision composition engine, with structural provenance records required to be preserved intact throughout the governance process. | Describes the monotonic invariants governing how parallel judgment vectors unify into singular runtime directives.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.034690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_7\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"2ed71df4-c897-496e-a98a-c0c497131814\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound operates as a deterministic enforcement layer at the system boundary between authorization and execution, governing how physical actions are evaluated justified and recorded without influencing agent cognition\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.004690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_17\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c05bbc37-af59-4173-b2f7-1bf9f86026f6\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound framework mitigates semantic and behavioral threats after traditional authorization concludes, detecting runtime behavioral policy violations and unauthorized execution bypassing approval workflows\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.994690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_5\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"6adfdf6d-4592-4ade-9534-16646fefb0c0\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound isolates behavior at the action perimeter rather than filtering cognitive model inputs, rendering it incapable of directly intercepting prompt injection, jailbreaks, or internal adversarial model manipulation | When: 2026-09-06 | Involving: AgentBound framework\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.004690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_15\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"2a66b637-8c11-457d-92ca-22880783a13d\",\n      \"text\": \"Agents can be authenticated, within valid OAuth/IAM scope, and compliant with static access policies yet still execute decisions violating their principal's intent through behavioral deviations including premature financial transactions, unreviewed content publication, sensitive information leakage under adversarial manipulation, or selecting irreversible actions when safe alternatives exist | When: 2026-09-06 | Involving: agent, principal\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.974690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_1\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"caab4851-86fb-43b7-8aac-3dbbfc844b01\",\n      \"text\": \"Pre-Action Governance Reasoning Loop (PA-GRL) proposed as formal mechanism through which agents consult structured governance rule sets before every consequential action, determining whether to proceed, self-correct, or escalate to human oversight, mirroring human deliberative compliance behavior | Involving: agents/researchers | To formalize human-like compliance behavior in AI agent governance\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.088393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_3\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"a43a2e87-2a9b-412d-90b3-7f7e75897f56\",\n      \"text\": \"Irreversible actions (purchase orders, supplier commits, replenishment triggers) require explicit human confirmation before execution because they cannot be undone if incorrect | Irreversible actions cannot be undone if incorrect\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.078393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_22\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c6acbadf-dfe3-4cad-b223-2e93013e3dbf\",\n      \"text\": \"Associated with DOI:10.5281/zenodo.17464706 | When: 2026-09-06 | Involving: user\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.844196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_33\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"5c382421-a18e-45dc-a0fe-39b878c0a920\",\n      \"text\": \"Establishing interoperable governance receipt standards represents a critical path toward unified accountability across heterogeneous multi-agent ecosystems.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.014690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_16\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"41025ece-357f-4d52-8e42-d167004a09f4\",\n      \"text\": \"Verifying a receipt requires only the artifact payload, corresponding public verification keys, and historical governance artifacts fetched via the receipt's stored references through a validation sequence comprising cryptographic integrity verification, governance reconstruction, and deterministic decision consistency check. | Involving: external verifying entities | Enables asynchronous, untrusted entity validation of policy compliance without requiring real-time agent presence\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.024690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_9\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c6c69a12-a267-4249-97d0-f8143486d199\",\n      \"text\": \"The algebraic composition of governance decisions yields four fundamental system properties: authorization preservation, behavioral independence, obligation separation, and replay verifiability. | Represents the guaranteed behavioral guarantees of the AgentBound governance framework.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.984690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_7\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"b4e51bad-15c5-4172-bef7-e9f2aeb3c8d7\",\n      \"text\": \"Assurance mappings reference NIST (GOVERN-1, MAP-1, MEASURE-1, MANAGE-1, MANAGE-3), ISO42001 (4,8,9,10), and EU AI Act (AnnexIV-3,4,6,9, Art72) for programmatic traceability.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.834196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"b90a0113-cf8a-4db5-bf2c-30ca8d64327c\",\n      \"text\": \"The framework achieved 95% compliance decision accuracy (38/40 correct decisions) across 40 evaluation runs, with two errors from edge-case input phrasings producing ambiguous permissibility reasoning | Involving: the framework\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.088393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_25\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"1a1552cc-5a3a-488c-97be-1ae7df0d6873\",\n      \"text\": \"Adaptive governance research aims to create dynamic constitutions capable of updating enforcement constraints in response to observed agent drift without invalidating cryptographic provenance.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.994690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_16\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"f9f4ff40-ac7c-4c79-9e4d-6d062d4af526\",\n      \"text\": \"Rule hierarchy structure: Layer 2 (workflow-specific), Layer 3 (agent-specific), Layer 4 (situational), all extending global rules without overriding them\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.078393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_15\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ddcafc90-f61a-4567-8869-b661983c8f8c\",\n      \"text\": \"This work first formalizes mapping of neurocognitive theories (Dual Process Theory, executive function) to agent governance design and demonstrates practical viability through production-grade case study | Involving: Cletus | Novel contribution bridging cognitive science and AI governance; first explicit neurocognitive grounding for agent governance\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"experience\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.108393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_30\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"0bef11c9-21a3-4b35-852e-408f35185b30\",\n      \"text\": \"In collaborative scenarios (e.g., Clinical Trial Coordinator), agents exchange digital attestations representing partial fulfillment of obligations (e.g., data anonymization, consent verification, statistical integrity), verifiable by peers and aggregable into a composite assurance graph enabling federated compliance | Involving: AI agents in collaborative scenarios | Enables federated compliance where trust emerges from a network of mutually validating agents\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.834196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_24\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"0159c929-ee2e-453e-929d-b579bdb8fc24\",\n      \"text\": \"Controls section defines explicit action rules structured as ABAC tuples, each linking directly to evidence fields enumerated in the card: kyc status, risk score, device trust level, beneficiary screening score, escalation id, ensuring every decision is auditable | Involving: Cletus (AI agent), PolicyCard system\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.834196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_16\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"e6601d88-b0dc-4e17-8000-8a49013b05ee\",\n      \"text\": \"Two-level standing delegation model empowers persistent periodic agents to operate asynchronously under dynamically refreshed governance policies while preserving immediate user revocability and bounding credential exposure\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.994690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_17\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"6e953bb2-4b86-4eff-b1cd-f8ba84bd0eed\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound-Bench quantifies framework efficacy through four core mathematical and system metrics: governance accuracy (correct decisions/total decisions), violation escape rate (violations executed/total violations), receipt verification success rate, and fine-grained governance latency | When: 2026-09-06\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.974690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_12\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ce770419-1c35-453d-90f5-7152f01d8ee6\",\n      \"text\": \"Agent identifies supply chain risk from unverified supplier not explicitly covered by Rule R4, demonstrating normative generalization through LLM reasoning rather than deterministic rule-matching | Involving: Cletus (agent), Rule R4 | Key innovation: governance embedded in LLM reasoning enables normative generalization beyond explicit rule conditions\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"experience\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.078393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_27\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"53796e6b-b18f-433e-8190-551db9236caa\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound builds upon RFC 8693 (OAuth 2.0 Token Exchange) standard for programmatic token transformation and delegation chain security | Provides formal semantic foundations for programmatic token transformation and delegation chain security within distributed environments\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.984690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_14\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c7f73850-8058-4de1-b6d9-311d443326f6\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound is a modular runtime governance and behavioral accountability framework for autonomous agents | Establishes behavioral governance as distinct from identity federation, access control, or training-time model alignment\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_14\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"31e84f05-37b4-44ea-90bc-428e742c36e4\",\n      \"text\": \"Each schema section can be traced to clauses/functions within frameworks, enabling automated validation of compliance claims\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.824196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_4\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"aba7ba91-274e-4a6c-b6b9-2c9774278c90\",\n      \"text\": \"Audit Service provides observability for system-wide accountability and non-repudiation by appending governance events and persisting signed receipts to append-only audit ledger | Involving: system | observability substrate required for system-wide accountability\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.994690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_8\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"9fbb19db-7caa-4b72-8296-9596af0d17b4\",\n      \"text\": \"Training-time alignment methods embed behavioral principles into model weights during training but produce probabilistic rather than deterministic compliance, with alignment degrading as agents operate in open-ended, adversarial, or out-of-distribution environments | Involving: AI models, training systems\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.098393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_2\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"20e86df0-5fce-49d4-9a12-65da8fdd0d32\",\n      \"text\": \"Financial institutions operate within stringent regulatory frameworks such as PSD2 (EU), AMLD (Anti-Money Laundering Directive), and jurisdictional Know-Your-Customer (KYC) mandates, requiring automated payment agents to operate within well-defined authorization and escalation boundaries | Involving: Cletus (AI agent), financial institutions, automated payment agents\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.854196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_16\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c8b164c1-2307-4e8c-a04d-1d684218f37d\",\n      \"text\": \"Governance frameworks must incorporate tamper-resistance mechanisms to protect rule integrity against adversarial inputs | Involving: design requirement\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.118393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_11\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"029b038b-467e-4e49-b552-f72e76fb3104\",\n      \"text\": \"Five core security invariants yielded by the verification architecture: integrity, non-repudiation, policy provenance, replay verifiability, and decision transparency. | Involving: system architecture | Defines the security properties guaranteed by the receipt verification system\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.984690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_9\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"320db885-6eb2-463f-b9ff-c64bbcc0750b\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound fundamentally diverges from optimization-centric model alignment methods, where alignment shapes model cognition beforehand and governance evaluates final behavior before system mutation, analogous to the software engineering boundary between application correctness and localized operational policy | When: 2026-09-06 | Involving: AgentBound framework\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_15\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"efb639e6-4532-4de4-bf99-12becf7f5ac3\",\n      \"text\": \"Adversarially crafted inputs may induce agents to rationalize non-compliant actions as permissible (functional analog of moral disengagement); framework lacks dedicated tamper-resistance layer | Involving: PAGRL agents | Governance robustness under systematic adversarial attack remains open empirical question\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.108393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_27\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"b7dfb392-ee7d-44f1-ba2c-ba092c2a85b7\",\n      \"text\": \"Work intersects four research areas: agentic AI governance and safety, training-time alignment, organizational compliance psychology, and neuroscience of decision-making | Involving: work\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.138393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_28\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"7aa44718-fe39-4e17-873e-0b7fab2170fb\",\n      \"text\": \"Validates consistency between sections by cross-checking evidence fields listed in monitoring against those referenced under obligations or controls\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.824196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_10\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"6ae98d7f-93a9-40cb-86b2-2fce61facff8\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound is implemented as a decoupled, runtime governance layer positioned directly before action execution, serving as a non-bypassable governance checkpoint that every consequential action must pass prior to target system mutation. | Establishes the architectural pattern for out-of-band validation of agent actions.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.994690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_7\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"1e7d8b48-e706-4824-8116-b4a26566f704\",\n      \"text\": \"External governance systems achieve high compliance within their defined rule scope but cannot generalize to novel situations not explicitly covered by their rule specifications\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.118393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_26\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"02b192ec-044a-49ca-8a16-3c69c0c0cb33\",\n      \"text\": \"Schema contains 'controls' section requiring 'action_rules' array with minimum 1 item\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.814196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_14\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"8644e70e-b152-4f7b-ad01-2aa2ed7b097c\",\n      \"text\": \"Validation performed using Ajv8.x JSON Schema validator with custom linting logic enforcing schema conformance and semantic relationships between fields beyond structural validation\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.904196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_8\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"83a18411-f4cf-42ee-bfc3-847b2a9b4aee\",\n      \"text\": \"The framework unifies four principals into a non-bypassable governance pipeline: Owner defines intent profile IO and authorizes delegation, Agent proposes actions, AgentBound Service enforces joint multi-authority policy M, Site Resource Provider hosts target resources; the pipeline sequentially evaluates, logs, and validates agent behaviors before execution, with security guarantees assuming strict operational sequence where governance evaluation occurs non-bypassably prior to execution\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.014690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"b483f60c-ba7b-454b-b3dc-7424c0af3151\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound constitutes an administrative governance and behavioral accountability layer rather than a totalizing agent security architecture\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.024690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_5\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"4a71566e-6bd0-4445-9378-0e1a9bbe3c92\",\n      \"text\": \"The Policy Card framework enables verifiable compliance for autonomous agents through automatic validation, version control, and integration with runtime enforcement or continuous-audit pipelines, forming a foundation for distributed assurance in multi-agent ecosystems | Involving: autonomous agents\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.834196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_0\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"42694569-e601-4d09-b194-5f7e1f9199ab\",\n      \"text\": \"RS(α) is the standard access control and delegation verification function for site S under delegated authorization scope Gauth\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_5\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"6140b11f-4488-4a31-aafc-96bb9ad59836\",\n      \"text\": \"The reasoning trace log is queryable through the MCP interface, enabling human operators to inspect governance decisions in real time and supporting post-hoc compliance audit and review.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.108393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_19\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"8c03b367-8fac-4b70-908b-17a0cbb698d0\",\n      \"text\": \"Validates that every rule in controls uses permitted effect tokens (allow, deny, or require escalation) preventing logically inconsistent or incomplete policy definitions\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.834196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_10\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"5b29fff7-d4db-4bce-a7f3-0f6c62489bf6\",\n      \"text\": \"The Policy Card schema is formally specified using JSON Schema 2020-12, defining mandatory fields including required top-level keys, permitted data types, pattern constraints, and enumerations governing how valid cards must be authored and validated, with additionalProperties: false preventing unspecified properties.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.914196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"f37c14f6-560c-44e6-bd8a-0fd60f5a3098\",\n      \"text\": \"Receipt generation proceeds via a deterministic four-stage pipeline: evaluation, raw payload construction, two-phase ordered countersigning protocol, and verification architecture enabling asynchronous policy compliance validation by external untrusted entities. | Involving: system architecture | Establishes the complete receipt generation and verification process with five core security invariants\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_9\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d8849b46-627f-4b04-93df-0900883c23a1\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound enforces deterministic compliance at the system runtime boundary rather than optimizing model weights at training time, focusing on verifiable system accountability rather than statistical behavioral shaping | Involving: AgentBound\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.984690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_13\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"f249bcfb-ac2d-4aac-9325-247e6ea3305f\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound evaluates candidate tool invocations non-bypassably before execution, using formal decision algebra to compose intermediate judgments conservatively\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.974690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_17\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"8512a3ae-3f39-408e-9e06-1a6de45832ac\",\n      \"text\": \"Governance receipt structured as tuple (Action, Governance, Judgments, Outcome, Signatures) capturing delegation token identifier, constitution version number with cryptographic hash, site action contract version identifier, individual typed evaluations, final operational primitive, and asymmetric cryptographic metadata | Involving: system | guarantees global integrity and non-repudiation\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.004690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_8\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"b1286291-ff34-4f00-bff9-45d32b965ac2\",\n      \"text\": \"Exception EX-TRIAGE-REMOTE-CLINIC-OVERRIDE for remote clinical sites is time-bound to 12 hours, requiring two person approval and reference as evidence\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.834196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_19\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"9f4b9ed0-311d-491e-b0e5-df484fdf0191\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound framework integrates three governance authorities (delegated authorization, owner-signed behavioral constitutions, and site action contracts) into a unified multi-authority decision engine for autonomous systems.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d24ba464-8811-43b3-9a48-63d218f8f051\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound's two-level delegation: standing delegation (long-term, human-authorized) authorizes short-lived task delegation per execution cycle; standing delegations restricted from direct execution, serving as root of authority for runtime engine | Involving: Cletus\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"experience\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_10\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"097c480b-5bba-4d8d-816c-b7aef63d21b3\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound framework provides verifiable behavioral oversight for autonomous AI agents by evaluating proposed actions through three independent authorities (delegated authorization, owner-signed behavioral constitutions, and site action contracts) with conservative composition through a formal decision model determining whether actions should be permitted, reviewed, or denied before execution | When: 2026-09-06 | Involving: Anuj Kaul, Qianlong Lan, Pranay Gupta | Addresses gap in agent infrastructure where delegated authorization cannot determine whether authorized actions should execute under current behavioral and operational context\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_0\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    }\n  ],\n  \"trace\": null,\n  \"entities\": null,\n  \"chunks\": null,\n  \"source_facts\": null\n}"
  }
}
