      "text": "{\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"36ede801-86d4-4651-a827-d694a4b8f054\",\n      \"text\": \"Aegon implements hardware-attested compliance mechanisms with ledger-bound token architectures and cryptographically signed mobile receipts for safeguarding content extraction and data access controls | Involving: Aegon\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.004690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_13\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"2cfeb6c9-0b76-4b8c-94a4-33c598e569df\",\n      \"text\": \"Task delegation short-lived credential derived from standing delegation boundaries, encapsulating task ID, constrained operational scope, issuance timestamp, short-lived expiration threshold, and governing constitution reference.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.974690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"540d73e2-f027-4937-8347-bf212369b484\",\n      \"text\": \"Task delegation short-lived credential derived from standing delegation boundaries, encapsulating task ID, constrained operational scope, issuance timestamp, short-lived expiration threshold, and governing constitution reference | Involving: Cletus\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"experience\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.974690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_10\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d25b8049-1949-47f6-b085-f2a450ca765c\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound's two-level delegation: standing delegation (long-term, human-authorized) authorizes short-lived task delegation per execution cycle; standing delegations restricted from direct execution, serving as root of authority for runtime engine, empowering persistent periodic agents to operate asynchronously under dynamically refreshed governance policies while preserving immediate user revocability and bounding credential exposure.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.994690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"a56f4d03-088f-4404-8927-06762407570d\",\n      \"text\": \"In Scenario 3, agent intends to contact unverified supplier not in verified registry; PAGRL retrieves rules R2, R4, R6; agent reasons contacting unverified supplier violates R4 but task can use verified alternative; compliance decision Self-Correct; agent revises intent to nearest verified supplier and re-enters PAGRL producing Proceed decision; original intent, correction reasoning, and revised intent logged to MCP governance server | Involving: supply chain agent, PAGRL system, MCP governance server, verified supplier | Unverified supplier contact violates compliance rules but alternative exists\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.088393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_24\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"02110a14-b10c-4bd8-9320-345c886c8a18\",\n      \"text\": \"In Scenario 4, supplier disruption signal activates situational rule R7; inventory replenishment agent intends to substitute disrupted supplier with verified alternative; with R7 active, PAGRL reasons disruption context elevates risk regardless of verified status; compliance decision Escalate; structured escalation message including disruption context, proposed substitution, and reasoning trace transmitted to supply chain manager for review | Involving: inventory replenishment agent, PAGRL system, supply chain manager, MCP governance server | Disruption context elevates risk even for verified suppliers\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.098393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_24\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d24ba464-8811-43b3-9a48-63d218f8f051\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound's two-level delegation: standing delegation (long-term, human-authorized) authorizes short-lived task delegation per execution cycle; standing delegations restricted from direct execution, serving as root of authority for runtime engine | Involving: Cletus\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"experience\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_10\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ccddb16f-8088-4321-ae2f-a3a22b2d95a0\",\n      \"text\": \"OAuth 2.0 token exchange protocol specified by Michael Jones, Anthony Nadalin, Brian Campbell, John Bradley, and Chuck Mortimore in a 2020 technical report, providing a standard for OAuth 2.0 token exchange | When: 2020 | Involving: Michael Jones, Anthony Nadalin, Brian Campbell, John Bradley, Chuck Mortimore\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_18\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"96f19be1-305e-492e-949d-f18c328789a6\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound addresses a fundamentally orthogonal axis to conventional benchmarks, focusing on runtime governance mechanisms rather than task optimization or task completion rates.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.014690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_11\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"3ea90a8a-4d85-4e46-9f04-fe8ab9af3abc\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound-Bench is a standardized evaluation framework designed to quantify governance enforcement correctness, multi-authority composition behavior, and policy provenance integrity.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_11\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ba1f50b8-205c-4432-b2f8-991f7ab8214d\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound-Bench is a standardized evaluation framework designed to quantify governance enforcement correctness, multi-authority composition behavior, and policy provenance integrity.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"0edf4582-3fe4-4bca-b431-ee6cd90a30ed\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound focuses on runtime governance mechanisms rather than task optimization or task completion rates.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.014690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"9d3abc10-3fb0-42ec-bd9f-59c6b8ca2ce1\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound constitutes an administrative governance and behavioral accountability layer rather than a totalizing agent security architecture, extending traditional observability by generating atomic governance receipts encapsulating exact policy version states, delegation token identifiers, individual authority judgments, terminal outcomes, and asymmetric cryptographic signatures, with every discrete transaction encapsulated within a cryptographically signed governance receipt enabling independent out-of-band decision reconstruction and completely reconstructing the original decision algebra out-of-band. Example governance receipt structure includes Receipt ID r-1024 for Agent ID ads-agent performing Action launch campaign under Delegation Ref d-118 with Constitution Version 3, resulting in Final Decision Human Approval Required with 7 Standing Delegation for Persistent Agents.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.024690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"fc319743-84cc-4fa3-85c2-e797f87c66f1\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound is implemented as a decoupled, runtime governance layer positioned directly before action execution, serving as a non-bypassable governance checkpoint that evaluates candidate tool invocations using formal decision algebra to compose intermediate judgments conservatively prior to target system mutation. The agent runtime is treated as untrusted due to potential jailbreaks, requiring out-of-band validation prior to system execution.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.004690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"8c975716-819f-478f-9c94-4a25bb367bfc\",\n      \"text\": \"Obligations are auditable commitments linked to evidence fields under specified conditions, including mandatory notifications, consent checks, and safety statements.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.844196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"88c903f8-7876-4950-9566-6ca94cc0d1f7\",\n      \"text\": \"Three conditions trigger escalation rather than self-correction: (1) categorical prohibition by rule where no intent revision makes it compliant, (2) irreversible action requiring human confirmation, (3) genuine uncertainty about permissibility where ambiguous cases should be escalated\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.118393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_16\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"6927b614-7521-47ab-825d-e8b2cba8a88d\",\n      \"text\": \"The AgentBound-Bench evaluation framework, comprising compiled benchmark scenarios, baseline ground-truth annotations, out-of-band receipt verification tooling, and deployment documentation, will be released to the community upon conclusion of the initial empirical evaluation campaign.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.034690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_16\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"42694569-e601-4d09-b194-5f7e1f9199ab\",\n      \"text\": \"RS(α) is the standard access control and delegation verification function for site S under delegated authorization scope Gauth\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_5\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c19a6296-1457-42e9-aecc-48fcb17bea3a\",\n      \"text\": \"Traditional authorization frameworks like Google Zanzibar Open Policy Agent and Cedar focus on entitlement validation for technical permissions while AgentBound establishes authorization as one governance input among independent arbiters evaluating contextual invariants beyond resource-level access control. These frameworks are insufficient for periodic or long-running agentic workloads because they operate under the implicit assumption that a human principal is actively present or within a valid session context when a transaction is initiated, creating systemic vulnerabilities where no human user is present to evaluate ambient risks when execution cycles spontaneously begin, and governance policies may shift between execution cycles; a runtime governance layer is needed to determine whether specific actions should occur under given circumstances.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.024690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"2554d39d-574e-4142-8295-4320fd5ccf86\",\n      \"text\": \"Schema was validated on September 6, 2026 | When: 2026-09-06\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.814196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_7\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"348eb115-dbdc-4604-a5cd-876d5960997a\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound-Bench quantifies framework efficacy through four core mathematical and system metrics: governance accuracy (correct decisions/total decisions), violation escape rate (violations executed/total violations), receipt verification success rate, and fine-grained governance latency\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.974690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"b1d52bf4-f371-46c0-bd2c-c747549de35b\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound is out of scope for adversarial prompt injection attacks, direct LLM jailbreaks, baseline model alignment failures, and hardware-level side-channel data exfiltration, as AgentBound isolates behavior at the action perimeter rather than filtering cognitive model inputs, rendering it incapable of directly intercepting prompt injection, jailbreaks, or internal adversarial model manipulation\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.014690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"88e21077-2e6f-42d8-aa60-8fc54438a2f5\",\n      \"text\": \"OAuth 2.0 token exchange protocol specified by Michael Jones, Anthony Nadalin, Brian Campbell, John Bradley, and Chuck Mortimore in a 2020 technical report\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"e6601d88-b0dc-4e17-8000-8a49013b05ee\",\n      \"text\": \"Two-level standing delegation model empowers persistent periodic agents to operate asynchronously under dynamically refreshed governance policies while preserving immediate user revocability and bounding credential exposure\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.994690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_17\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"b184d623-9e11-40de-bada-82b84d4d726a\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound enforces deterministic compliance at the system runtime boundary rather than optimizing model weights at training time, focusing on verifiable system accountability rather than statistical behavioral shaping, fundamentally diverging from optimization-centric model alignment methods where alignment shapes model cognition beforehand and governance evaluates final behavior before system mutation, analogous to the software engineering boundary between application correctness and localized operational policy, without influencing agent cognition.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.004690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d050441a-f326-43eb-a163-4e668e67863e\",\n      \"text\": \"Internalized governance (embedded in agent reasoning) produces more robust and generalizable compliance than externally enforced governance systems\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.108393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_26\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"a43a2e87-2a9b-412d-90b3-7f7e75897f56\",\n      \"text\": \"Irreversible actions (purchase orders, supplier commits, replenishment triggers) require explicit human confirmation before execution because they cannot be undone if incorrect | Irreversible actions cannot be undone if incorrect\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.078393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_22\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"11d4ee89-01b6-4056-9498-b92aca08cd31\",\n      \"text\": \"During supplier disruption events, all supplier substitution decisions require human review regardless of order value because disruption contexts introduce elevated supply chain risk | Disruption contexts introduce elevated supply chain risk\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.128393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_22\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d71c59c5-e8fc-445b-83bb-992b55ed9459\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound framework mitigates semantic and behavioral threats after traditional authorization concludes, detecting runtime behavioral policy violations and unauthorized execution bypassing approval workflows.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.994690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"704df447-ded6-4142-a2ee-5a9636d3ee2b\",\n      \"text\": \"Crosley proposes runtime constitutions as governance files injected into agent context at execution time with selective loading of relevant rules per task, but remains an engineering pattern rather than formally grounded framework and does not connect agent governance to neurocognitive theory or organizational compliance psychology | Involving: Crosley (author) | Remains engineering pattern rather than formally grounded framework; lacks connection to neurocognitive theory and organizational compliance psychology\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.088393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_29\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"0cdd3053-9292-40c6-86c2-608b98ed3880\",\n      \"text\": \"Procurement orders exceeding $10,000 require human approval before execution because high-value orders carry significant financial risk | High-value orders carry significant financial risk\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.088393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_22\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"5c382421-a18e-45dc-a0fe-39b878c0a920\",\n      \"text\": \"Establishing interoperable governance receipt standards represents a critical path toward unified accountability across heterogeneous multi-agent ecosystems.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.014690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_16\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"2ed71df4-c897-496e-a98a-c0c497131814\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound operates as a deterministic enforcement layer at the system boundary between authorization and execution, governing how physical actions are evaluated justified and recorded without influencing agent cognition\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.004690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_17\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"a13b6643-bbf0-4787-803a-72f7d1c81b0b\",\n      \"text\": \"Documentation/specs/templates/examples: CC BY 4.0\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.854196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_31\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"b483f60c-ba7b-454b-b3dc-7424c0af3151\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound constitutes an administrative governance and behavioral accountability layer rather than a totalizing agent security architecture\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.024690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_5\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"097c480b-5bba-4d8d-816c-b7aef63d21b3\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound framework provides verifiable behavioral oversight for autonomous AI agents by evaluating proposed actions through three independent authorities (delegated authorization, owner-signed behavioral constitutions, and site action contracts) with conservative composition through a formal decision model determining whether actions should be permitted, reviewed, or denied before execution | When: 2026-09-06 | Involving: Anuj Kaul, Qianlong Lan, Pranay Gupta | Addresses gap in agent infrastructure where delegated authorization cannot determine whether authorized actions should execute under current behavioral and operational context\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_0\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"abd6e3c4-c200-49e9-a3a7-fe324332269a\",\n      \"text\": \"Runtime requests latest constitution version from Constitution Service before task materialization; task token encapsulates constitution hash, enabling automatic policy propagation without manual reauthorization.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.984690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"0ca4bd46-b3cd-4b78-a008-09f7f0909110\",\n      \"text\": \"System is explicitly non-diagnostic and must always defer to human judgment for high-risk or ambiguous cases\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.864196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_19\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"72c99091-4148-46fd-8619-6cad5815794f\",\n      \"text\": \"Attack succeeds when RS(α)=Valid AND α∉IO, exploiting cognitive ambiguity, semantic uncertainty, or incomplete governance rule specifications\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.984690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_5\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c05bbc37-af59-4173-b2f7-1bf9f86026f6\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound framework mitigates semantic and behavioral threats after traditional authorization concludes, detecting runtime behavioral policy violations and unauthorized execution bypassing approval workflows\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.994690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_5\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"6e953bb2-4b86-4eff-b1cd-f8ba84bd0eed\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound-Bench quantifies framework efficacy through four core mathematical and system metrics: governance accuracy (correct decisions/total decisions), violation escape rate (violations executed/total violations), receipt verification success rate, and fine-grained governance latency | When: 2026-09-06\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.974690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_12\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"460744ac-83ed-4c88-bd62-0ed9671f99c9\",\n      \"text\": \"Traditional authorization frameworks (Google Zanzibar, Open Policy Agent, Cedar) focus on entitlement validation for technical permissions to access resources, while AgentBound establishes authorization as one governance input among independent arbiters to evaluate contextual invariants beyond resource-level access control | Involving: Google Zanzibar, Open Policy Agent, Cedar, AgentBound\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.024690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_13\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"9f4b9ed0-311d-491e-b0e5-df484fdf0191\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound framework integrates three governance authorities (delegated authorization, owner-signed behavioral constitutions, and site action contracts) into a unified multi-authority decision engine for autonomous systems.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"53796e6b-b18f-433e-8190-551db9236caa\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound builds upon RFC 8693 (OAuth 2.0 Token Exchange) standard for programmatic token transformation and delegation chain security | Provides formal semantic foundations for programmatic token transformation and delegation chain security within distributed environments\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.984690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_14\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"fc44fe51-caf6-4e49-98c6-497bd46b4e49\",\n      \"text\": \"ClinicalTriagePolicyCard formalizes three key obligations: provide only advisory outputs supported by evidence and disclaimers, escalate any red-flag condition to qualified personnel or emergency services, and deny any autonomous diagnosis or prescription\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.814196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_19\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ce770419-1c35-453d-90f5-7152f01d8ee6\",\n      \"text\": \"Agent identifies supply chain risk from unverified supplier not explicitly covered by Rule R4, demonstrating normative generalization through LLM reasoning rather than deterministic rule-matching | Involving: Cletus (agent), Rule R4 | Key innovation: governance embedded in LLM reasoning enables normative generalization beyond explicit rule conditions\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"experience\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.078393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_27\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"f96a6ac4-9239-41cf-a824-ad10cf5d869b\",\n      \"text\": \"Valid to timestamp must be greater than or equal to valid from timestamp, and retention periods must exceed review cadence\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.824196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_9\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"e424c3cc-a088-4727-ab5e-5e4f0106affa\",\n      \"text\": \"PolicyCards act as structured metadata describing both operational policy and its cryptographic verification envelope\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.814196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_25\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"e3d6a13e-b402-4747-aaf5-7ca25f44c03e\",\n      \"text\": \"Autonomous AI agents are transitioning from passive conversational assistants into high-stakes delegated workloads executing consequential tasks on behalf of human principals.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"4d0ba11c-530d-4408-aa01-26fce57e9883\",\n      \"text\": \"Autonomous AI agents are transitioning from passive conversational assistants into high-stakes delegated workloads executing consequential tasks on behalf of human principals.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_16\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c7f73850-8058-4de1-b6d9-311d443326f6\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound is a modular runtime governance and behavioral accountability framework for autonomous agents | Establishes behavioral governance as distinct from identity federation, access control, or training-time model alignment\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_14\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"1a1552cc-5a3a-488c-97be-1ae7df0d6873\",\n      \"text\": \"Adaptive governance research aims to create dynamic constitutions capable of updating enforcement constraints in response to observed agent drift without invalidating cryptographic provenance.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.994690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_16\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"83a18411-f4cf-42ee-bfc3-847b2a9b4aee\",\n      \"text\": \"The framework unifies four principals into a non-bypassable governance pipeline: Owner defines intent profile IO and authorizes delegation, Agent proposes actions, AgentBound Service enforces joint multi-authority policy M, Site Resource Provider hosts target resources; the pipeline sequentially evaluates, logs, and validates agent behaviors before execution, with security guarantees assuming strict operational sequence where governance evaluation occurs non-bypassably prior to execution\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.014690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"0159c929-ee2e-453e-929d-b579bdb8fc24\",\n      \"text\": \"Controls section defines explicit action rules structured as ABAC tuples, each linking directly to evidence fields enumerated in the card: kyc status, risk score, device trust level, beneficiary screening score, escalation id, ensuring every decision is auditable | Involving: Cletus (AI agent), PolicyCard system\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.834196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_16\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"41025ece-357f-4d52-8e42-d167004a09f4\",\n      \"text\": \"Verifying a receipt requires only the artifact payload, corresponding public verification keys, and historical governance artifacts fetched via the receipt's stored references through a validation sequence comprising cryptographic integrity verification, governance reconstruction, and deterministic decision consistency check. | Involving: external verifying entities | Enables asynchronous, untrusted entity validation of policy compliance without requiring real-time agent presence\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.024690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_9\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"caab4851-86fb-43b7-8aac-3dbbfc844b01\",\n      \"text\": \"Pre-Action Governance Reasoning Loop (PA-GRL) proposed as formal mechanism through which agents consult structured governance rule sets before every consequential action, determining whether to proceed, self-correct, or escalate to human oversight, mirroring human deliberative compliance behavior | Involving: agents/researchers | To formalize human-like compliance behavior in AI agent governance\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.088393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_3\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c6c69a12-a267-4249-97d0-f8143486d199\",\n      \"text\": \"The algebraic composition of governance decisions yields four fundamental system properties: authorization preservation, behavioral independence, obligation separation, and replay verifiability. | Represents the guaranteed behavioral guarantees of the AgentBound governance framework.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.984690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_7\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"56b62400-7c29-48b3-a728-ec4b13e97a82\",\n      \"text\": \"Only suppliers present in the verified supplier registry may be contacted because unverified suppliers introduce supply chain and compliance risk | Unverified suppliers introduce supply chain and compliance risk\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.098393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_22\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"b4e51bad-15c5-4172-bef7-e9f2aeb3c8d7\",\n      \"text\": \"Assurance mappings reference NIST (GOVERN-1, MAP-1, MEASURE-1, MANAGE-1, MANAGE-3), ISO42001 (4,8,9,10), and EU AI Act (AnnexIV-3,4,6,9, Art72) for programmatic traceability.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.834196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"7725ee7c-c8d0-4d78-ac9a-a6a6058fd260\",\n      \"text\": \"Framework positions Policy Cards as foundation for autonomous assurance ecosystems where policies are computational, verifiable, and privacy-preserving.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.894196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_26\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"6df9eb59-a12e-484d-8206-21ee84f52653\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound framework integrates three governance authorities (delegated authorization, owner-signed behavioral constitutions, and site action contracts) into a unified multi-authority decision engine for autonomous systems\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_17\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c644676b-1322-439b-8ff4-e09b1dd455e6\",\n      \"text\": \"Traditional identity verification and resource-level access control are insufficient to secure execution perimeters for autonomous agents; a runtime governance layer is needed to determine whether specific actions should occur under given circumstances.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.974690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_16\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"2874a259-3888-463d-9d5e-414e8d41461d\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound introduces standing delegation model that cleanly decouples long-term user authorization from short-lived runtime execution authority for persistent autonomous agents operating without continuous human supervision. | Involving: persistent agents + user authorization | Addresses structural limitation of traditional session-oriented authorization that assumes human presence during transaction initiation\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.994690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_9\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"6ae98d7f-93a9-40cb-86b2-2fce61facff8\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound is implemented as a decoupled, runtime governance layer positioned directly before action execution, serving as a non-bypassable governance checkpoint that every consequential action must pass prior to target system mutation. | Establishes the architectural pattern for out-of-band validation of agent actions.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.994690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_7\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"24515944-a2ee-4e84-a169-c54cebea0f78\",\n      \"text\": \"Formal Runtime Enforcement uses deterministic pipeline to synthesize complementary judgments from independent authorities through conservative decision algebra before action execution\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.984690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_2\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"412755b8-775c-4002-89f0-4f58a9562c18\",\n      \"text\": \"Obligations include user notices (fees/limits), explicit consent recording, escalation protocol enforcement, and audit-trail maintenance | Involving: system | Framework requirements for compliance and traceability\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.824196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_18\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"26737e50-b69b-4fbb-b85f-56cee391b604\",\n      \"text\": \"Both humans and autonomous AI agents interact with their environments through the same mechanism where a reasoning source produces a natural language expression of intent that drives action, analogous to humans formulating instructions directed toward a task and AI agents formulating prompts directed toward an LLM\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.118393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_6\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"087da0a8-6b24-4099-83b9-5f222a324e3e\",\n      \"text\": \"Situational rules are stored as conditional entries with activation predicates; the governance server evaluates these predicates against runtime context signals (such as supplier disruption flag, active audit period, or elevated risk classification) to dynamically include matching rules in retrieval responses.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.088393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_19\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"6140b11f-4488-4a31-aafc-96bb9ad59836\",\n      \"text\": \"The reasoning trace log is queryable through the MCP interface, enabling human operators to inspect governance decisions in real time and supporting post-hoc compliance audit and review.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.108393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_19\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"aae10560-5efd-4918-a840-ba56be792392\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound addresses situations where fully authenticated and legitimately authorized agents execute actions violating principal intent while remaining within delegated access control scope | Demonstrates behavioral governance failures differ from access control breaches\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.994690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_14\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"5b29fff7-d4db-4bce-a7f3-0f6c62489bf6\",\n      \"text\": \"The Policy Card schema is formally specified using JSON Schema 2020-12, defining mandatory fields including required top-level keys, permitted data types, pattern constraints, and enumerations governing how valid cards must be authored and validated, with additionalProperties: false preventing unspecified properties.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.914196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"6adfdf6d-4592-4ade-9534-16646fefb0c0\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound isolates behavior at the action perimeter rather than filtering cognitive model inputs, rendering it incapable of directly intercepting prompt injection, jailbreaks, or internal adversarial model manipulation | When: 2026-09-06 | Involving: AgentBound framework\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.004690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_15\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"0bef11c9-21a3-4b35-852e-408f35185b30\",\n      \"text\": \"In collaborative scenarios (e.g., Clinical Trial Coordinator), agents exchange digital attestations representing partial fulfillment of obligations (e.g., data anonymization, consent verification, statistical integrity), verifiable by peers and aggregable into a composite assurance graph enabling federated compliance | Involving: AI agents in collaborative scenarios | Enables federated compliance where trust emerges from a network of mutually validating agents\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.834196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_24\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c8b164c1-2307-4e8c-a04d-1d684218f37d\",\n      \"text\": \"Governance frameworks must incorporate tamper-resistance mechanisms to protect rule integrity against adversarial inputs | Involving: design requirement\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.118393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_11\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"b90a0113-cf8a-4db5-bf2c-30ca8d64327c\",\n      \"text\": \"The framework achieved 95% compliance decision accuracy (38/40 correct decisions) across 40 evaluation runs, with two errors from edge-case input phrasings producing ambiguous permissibility reasoning | Involving: the framework\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.088393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_25\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"8c03b367-8fac-4b70-908b-17a0cbb698d0\",\n      \"text\": \"Validates that every rule in controls uses permitted effect tokens (allow, deny, or require escalation) preventing logically inconsistent or incomplete policy definitions\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.834196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_10\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"09f2e51c-982e-4781-915f-e25f3e58c04d\",\n      \"text\": \"Two-phase countersigning protocol: first, requesting agent signs constructed receipt payload using its private asymmetric key; second, AgentBound enforcement service intercepts and countersigns the entire block covering core receipt payload, agent's signature, and terminal decision vector. | Involving: requesting agent + AgentBound enforcement service | Ensures accountability binding and invalidates verification chain if out-of-band modifications occur to underlying action payload or intermediate governance evaluation\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.974690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_9\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"4a71566e-6bd0-4445-9378-0e1a9bbe3c92\",\n      \"text\": \"The Policy Card framework enables verifiable compliance for autonomous agents through automatic validation, version control, and integration with runtime enforcement or continuous-audit pipelines, forming a foundation for distributed assurance in multi-agent ecosystems | Involving: autonomous agents\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.834196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_0\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"f37c14f6-560c-44e6-bd8a-0fd60f5a3098\",\n      \"text\": \"Receipt generation proceeds via a deterministic four-stage pipeline: evaluation, raw payload construction, two-phase ordered countersigning protocol, and verification architecture enabling asynchronous policy compliance validation by external untrusted entities. | Involving: system architecture | Establishes the complete receipt generation and verification process with five core security invariants\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_9\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d8849b46-627f-4b04-93df-0900883c23a1\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound enforces deterministic compliance at the system runtime boundary rather than optimizing model weights at training time, focusing on verifiable system accountability rather than statistical behavioral shaping | Involving: AgentBound\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.984690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_13\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"029b038b-467e-4e49-b552-f72e76fb3104\",\n      \"text\": \"Five core security invariants yielded by the verification architecture: integrity, non-repudiation, policy provenance, replay verifiability, and decision transparency. | Involving: system architecture | Defines the security properties guaranteed by the receipt verification system\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.984690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_9\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"7aa44718-fe39-4e17-873e-0b7fab2170fb\",\n      \"text\": \"Validates consistency between sections by cross-checking evidence fields listed in monitoring against those referenced under obligations or controls\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.824196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_10\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"1acc06f1-e5fb-4d88-91c7-7cacb3ae3467\",\n      \"text\": \"Policy Cards are JSON-structured documents with semantic versioning (X.Y.Z) enabling traceable updates and diff-based analysis for auditors to verify what changed between policy revisions.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.814196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_6\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d28afb9c-cac8-4486-ae03-f2fbad8a8192\",\n      \"text\": \"Full schema and validator available in public repository and archived via Zenodo (DOI: 10.5281/zenodo.17464706)\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.844196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_10\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"31e84f05-37b4-44ea-90bc-428e742c36e4\",\n      \"text\": \"Each schema section can be traced to clauses/functions within frameworks, enabling automated validation of compliance claims\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.824196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_4\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"5712001a-8a47-404e-8490-f4d28b9ae781\",\n      \"text\": \"Monitoring defines loggable events, data fields, detectors, and thresholds with minimum retention >=1 day and review cadence >=1 day, linking operational telemetry with audit evidence.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.854196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"f9e87021-301e-4be2-92ca-cbd1e194fa4b\",\n      \"text\": \"Behavioral adversary Abeh manipulates authorized agents into executing actions violating Owner's intent while remaining within delegated permission scope\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.974690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_5\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"1267ec72-9d5c-487b-8b1c-71e29946a8fa\",\n      \"text\": \"Operational rules in Table 3 translate triage obligations into machine-verifiable conditions based on vitals present, risk level, confidence score, red flag status, patient age, and symptom presence (e.g., chest pain)\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.824196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_19\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"6fe42293-0d42-4fa8-9c5f-2f364271cdf1\",\n      \"text\": \"Automatic constitution refresh: runtime requests latest constitution version from Constitution Service before task materialization; task token encapsulates constitution hash, enabling automatic policy propagation without manual reauthorization | Involving: Cletus\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"experience\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.984690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_10\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"f249bcfb-ac2d-4aac-9325-247e6ea3305f\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound evaluates candidate tool invocations non-bypassably before execution, using formal decision algebra to compose intermediate judgments conservatively\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.974690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_17\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"e7fc775d-ca3a-41c5-9213-52c24ef235bb\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound's enforcement layer efficacy depends on the precision and quality of underlying constitutions and site action contracts.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.014690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    }\n  ],\n  \"trace\": null,\n  \"entities\": null,\n  \"chunks\": null,\n  \"source_facts\": null\n}",
      "type": "text"
    }
  ],
  "isError": false,
  "structuredContent": {
    "result": "{\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"36ede801-86d4-4651-a827-d694a4b8f054\",\n      \"text\": \"Aegon implements hardware-attested compliance mechanisms with ledger-bound token architectures and cryptographically signed mobile receipts for safeguarding content extraction and data access controls | Involving: Aegon\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.004690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_13\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"2cfeb6c9-0b76-4b8c-94a4-33c598e569df\",\n      \"text\": \"Task delegation short-lived credential derived from standing delegation boundaries, encapsulating task ID, constrained operational scope, issuance timestamp, short-lived expiration threshold, and governing constitution reference.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.974690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"540d73e2-f027-4937-8347-bf212369b484\",\n      \"text\": \"Task delegation short-lived credential derived from standing delegation boundaries, encapsulating task ID, constrained operational scope, issuance timestamp, short-lived expiration threshold, and governing constitution reference | Involving: Cletus\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"experience\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.974690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_10\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d25b8049-1949-47f6-b085-f2a450ca765c\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound's two-level delegation: standing delegation (long-term, human-authorized) authorizes short-lived task delegation per execution cycle; standing delegations restricted from direct execution, serving as root of authority for runtime engine, empowering persistent periodic agents to operate asynchronously under dynamically refreshed governance policies while preserving immediate user revocability and bounding credential exposure.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.994690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"a56f4d03-088f-4404-8927-06762407570d\",\n      \"text\": \"In Scenario 3, agent intends to contact unverified supplier not in verified registry; PAGRL retrieves rules R2, R4, R6; agent reasons contacting unverified supplier violates R4 but task can use verified alternative; compliance decision Self-Correct; agent revises intent to nearest verified supplier and re-enters PAGRL producing Proceed decision; original intent, correction reasoning, and revised intent logged to MCP governance server | Involving: supply chain agent, PAGRL system, MCP governance server, verified supplier | Unverified supplier contact violates compliance rules but alternative exists\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.088393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_24\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"02110a14-b10c-4bd8-9320-345c886c8a18\",\n      \"text\": \"In Scenario 4, supplier disruption signal activates situational rule R7; inventory replenishment agent intends to substitute disrupted supplier with verified alternative; with R7 active, PAGRL reasons disruption context elevates risk regardless of verified status; compliance decision Escalate; structured escalation message including disruption context, proposed substitution, and reasoning trace transmitted to supply chain manager for review | Involving: inventory replenishment agent, PAGRL system, supply chain manager, MCP governance server | Disruption context elevates risk even for verified suppliers\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.098393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_24\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d24ba464-8811-43b3-9a48-63d218f8f051\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound's two-level delegation: standing delegation (long-term, human-authorized) authorizes short-lived task delegation per execution cycle; standing delegations restricted from direct execution, serving as root of authority for runtime engine | Involving: Cletus\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"experience\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_10\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ccddb16f-8088-4321-ae2f-a3a22b2d95a0\",\n      \"text\": \"OAuth 2.0 token exchange protocol specified by Michael Jones, Anthony Nadalin, Brian Campbell, John Bradley, and Chuck Mortimore in a 2020 technical report, providing a standard for OAuth 2.0 token exchange | When: 2020 | Involving: Michael Jones, Anthony Nadalin, Brian Campbell, John Bradley, Chuck Mortimore\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_18\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"96f19be1-305e-492e-949d-f18c328789a6\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound addresses a fundamentally orthogonal axis to conventional benchmarks, focusing on runtime governance mechanisms rather than task optimization or task completion rates.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.014690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_11\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"3ea90a8a-4d85-4e46-9f04-fe8ab9af3abc\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound-Bench is a standardized evaluation framework designed to quantify governance enforcement correctness, multi-authority composition behavior, and policy provenance integrity.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_11\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ba1f50b8-205c-4432-b2f8-991f7ab8214d\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound-Bench is a standardized evaluation framework designed to quantify governance enforcement correctness, multi-authority composition behavior, and policy provenance integrity.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"0edf4582-3fe4-4bca-b431-ee6cd90a30ed\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound focuses on runtime governance mechanisms rather than task optimization or task completion rates.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.014690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"9d3abc10-3fb0-42ec-bd9f-59c6b8ca2ce1\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound constitutes an administrative governance and behavioral accountability layer rather than a totalizing agent security architecture, extending traditional observability by generating atomic governance receipts encapsulating exact policy version states, delegation token identifiers, individual authority judgments, terminal outcomes, and asymmetric cryptographic signatures, with every discrete transaction encapsulated within a cryptographically signed governance receipt enabling independent out-of-band decision reconstruction and completely reconstructing the original decision algebra out-of-band. Example governance receipt structure includes Receipt ID r-1024 for Agent ID ads-agent performing Action launch campaign under Delegation Ref d-118 with Constitution Version 3, resulting in Final Decision Human Approval Required with 7 Standing Delegation for Persistent Agents.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.024690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"fc319743-84cc-4fa3-85c2-e797f87c66f1\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound is implemented as a decoupled, runtime governance layer positioned directly before action execution, serving as a non-bypassable governance checkpoint that evaluates candidate tool invocations using formal decision algebra to compose intermediate judgments conservatively prior to target system mutation. The agent runtime is treated as untrusted due to potential jailbreaks, requiring out-of-band validation prior to system execution.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.004690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"8c975716-819f-478f-9c94-4a25bb367bfc\",\n      \"text\": \"Obligations are auditable commitments linked to evidence fields under specified conditions, including mandatory notifications, consent checks, and safety statements.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.844196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"88c903f8-7876-4950-9566-6ca94cc0d1f7\",\n      \"text\": \"Three conditions trigger escalation rather than self-correction: (1) categorical prohibition by rule where no intent revision makes it compliant, (2) irreversible action requiring human confirmation, (3) genuine uncertainty about permissibility where ambiguous cases should be escalated\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.118393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_16\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"6927b614-7521-47ab-825d-e8b2cba8a88d\",\n      \"text\": \"The AgentBound-Bench evaluation framework, comprising compiled benchmark scenarios, baseline ground-truth annotations, out-of-band receipt verification tooling, and deployment documentation, will be released to the community upon conclusion of the initial empirical evaluation campaign.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.034690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_16\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"42694569-e601-4d09-b194-5f7e1f9199ab\",\n      \"text\": \"RS(α) is the standard access control and delegation verification function for site S under delegated authorization scope Gauth\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_5\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c19a6296-1457-42e9-aecc-48fcb17bea3a\",\n      \"text\": \"Traditional authorization frameworks like Google Zanzibar Open Policy Agent and Cedar focus on entitlement validation for technical permissions while AgentBound establishes authorization as one governance input among independent arbiters evaluating contextual invariants beyond resource-level access control. These frameworks are insufficient for periodic or long-running agentic workloads because they operate under the implicit assumption that a human principal is actively present or within a valid session context when a transaction is initiated, creating systemic vulnerabilities where no human user is present to evaluate ambient risks when execution cycles spontaneously begin, and governance policies may shift between execution cycles; a runtime governance layer is needed to determine whether specific actions should occur under given circumstances.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.024690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"2554d39d-574e-4142-8295-4320fd5ccf86\",\n      \"text\": \"Schema was validated on September 6, 2026 | When: 2026-09-06\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.814196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_7\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"348eb115-dbdc-4604-a5cd-876d5960997a\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound-Bench quantifies framework efficacy through four core mathematical and system metrics: governance accuracy (correct decisions/total decisions), violation escape rate (violations executed/total violations), receipt verification success rate, and fine-grained governance latency\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.974690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"b1d52bf4-f371-46c0-bd2c-c747549de35b\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound is out of scope for adversarial prompt injection attacks, direct LLM jailbreaks, baseline model alignment failures, and hardware-level side-channel data exfiltration, as AgentBound isolates behavior at the action perimeter rather than filtering cognitive model inputs, rendering it incapable of directly intercepting prompt injection, jailbreaks, or internal adversarial model manipulation\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.014690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"88e21077-2e6f-42d8-aa60-8fc54438a2f5\",\n      \"text\": \"OAuth 2.0 token exchange protocol specified by Michael Jones, Anthony Nadalin, Brian Campbell, John Bradley, and Chuck Mortimore in a 2020 technical report\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"e6601d88-b0dc-4e17-8000-8a49013b05ee\",\n      \"text\": \"Two-level standing delegation model empowers persistent periodic agents to operate asynchronously under dynamically refreshed governance policies while preserving immediate user revocability and bounding credential exposure\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.994690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_17\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"b184d623-9e11-40de-bada-82b84d4d726a\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound enforces deterministic compliance at the system runtime boundary rather than optimizing model weights at training time, focusing on verifiable system accountability rather than statistical behavioral shaping, fundamentally diverging from optimization-centric model alignment methods where alignment shapes model cognition beforehand and governance evaluates final behavior before system mutation, analogous to the software engineering boundary between application correctness and localized operational policy, without influencing agent cognition.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.004690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d050441a-f326-43eb-a163-4e668e67863e\",\n      \"text\": \"Internalized governance (embedded in agent reasoning) produces more robust and generalizable compliance than externally enforced governance systems\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.108393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_26\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"a43a2e87-2a9b-412d-90b3-7f7e75897f56\",\n      \"text\": \"Irreversible actions (purchase orders, supplier commits, replenishment triggers) require explicit human confirmation before execution because they cannot be undone if incorrect | Irreversible actions cannot be undone if incorrect\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.078393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_22\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"11d4ee89-01b6-4056-9498-b92aca08cd31\",\n      \"text\": \"During supplier disruption events, all supplier substitution decisions require human review regardless of order value because disruption contexts introduce elevated supply chain risk | Disruption contexts introduce elevated supply chain risk\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.128393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_22\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d71c59c5-e8fc-445b-83bb-992b55ed9459\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound framework mitigates semantic and behavioral threats after traditional authorization concludes, detecting runtime behavioral policy violations and unauthorized execution bypassing approval workflows.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.994690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"704df447-ded6-4142-a2ee-5a9636d3ee2b\",\n      \"text\": \"Crosley proposes runtime constitutions as governance files injected into agent context at execution time with selective loading of relevant rules per task, but remains an engineering pattern rather than formally grounded framework and does not connect agent governance to neurocognitive theory or organizational compliance psychology | Involving: Crosley (author) | Remains engineering pattern rather than formally grounded framework; lacks connection to neurocognitive theory and organizational compliance psychology\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.088393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_29\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"0cdd3053-9292-40c6-86c2-608b98ed3880\",\n      \"text\": \"Procurement orders exceeding $10,000 require human approval before execution because high-value orders carry significant financial risk | High-value orders carry significant financial risk\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.088393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_22\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"5c382421-a18e-45dc-a0fe-39b878c0a920\",\n      \"text\": \"Establishing interoperable governance receipt standards represents a critical path toward unified accountability across heterogeneous multi-agent ecosystems.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.014690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_16\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"2ed71df4-c897-496e-a98a-c0c497131814\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound operates as a deterministic enforcement layer at the system boundary between authorization and execution, governing how physical actions are evaluated justified and recorded without influencing agent cognition\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.004690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_17\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"a13b6643-bbf0-4787-803a-72f7d1c81b0b\",\n      \"text\": \"Documentation/specs/templates/examples: CC BY 4.0\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.854196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_31\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"b483f60c-ba7b-454b-b3dc-7424c0af3151\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound constitutes an administrative governance and behavioral accountability layer rather than a totalizing agent security architecture\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.024690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_5\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"097c480b-5bba-4d8d-816c-b7aef63d21b3\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound framework provides verifiable behavioral oversight for autonomous AI agents by evaluating proposed actions through three independent authorities (delegated authorization, owner-signed behavioral constitutions, and site action contracts) with conservative composition through a formal decision model determining whether actions should be permitted, reviewed, or denied before execution | When: 2026-09-06 | Involving: Anuj Kaul, Qianlong Lan, Pranay Gupta | Addresses gap in agent infrastructure where delegated authorization cannot determine whether authorized actions should execute under current behavioral and operational context\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_0\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"abd6e3c4-c200-49e9-a3a7-fe324332269a\",\n      \"text\": \"Runtime requests latest constitution version from Constitution Service before task materialization; task token encapsulates constitution hash, enabling automatic policy propagation without manual reauthorization.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.984690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"0ca4bd46-b3cd-4b78-a008-09f7f0909110\",\n      \"text\": \"System is explicitly non-diagnostic and must always defer to human judgment for high-risk or ambiguous cases\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.864196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_19\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"72c99091-4148-46fd-8619-6cad5815794f\",\n      \"text\": \"Attack succeeds when RS(α)=Valid AND α∉IO, exploiting cognitive ambiguity, semantic uncertainty, or incomplete governance rule specifications\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.984690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_5\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c05bbc37-af59-4173-b2f7-1bf9f86026f6\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound framework mitigates semantic and behavioral threats after traditional authorization concludes, detecting runtime behavioral policy violations and unauthorized execution bypassing approval workflows\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.994690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_5\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"6e953bb2-4b86-4eff-b1cd-f8ba84bd0eed\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound-Bench quantifies framework efficacy through four core mathematical and system metrics: governance accuracy (correct decisions/total decisions), violation escape rate (violations executed/total violations), receipt verification success rate, and fine-grained governance latency | When: 2026-09-06\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.974690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_12\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"460744ac-83ed-4c88-bd62-0ed9671f99c9\",\n      \"text\": \"Traditional authorization frameworks (Google Zanzibar, Open Policy Agent, Cedar) focus on entitlement validation for technical permissions to access resources, while AgentBound establishes authorization as one governance input among independent arbiters to evaluate contextual invariants beyond resource-level access control | Involving: Google Zanzibar, Open Policy Agent, Cedar, AgentBound\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.024690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_13\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"9f4b9ed0-311d-491e-b0e5-df484fdf0191\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound framework integrates three governance authorities (delegated authorization, owner-signed behavioral constitutions, and site action contracts) into a unified multi-authority decision engine for autonomous systems.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"53796e6b-b18f-433e-8190-551db9236caa\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound builds upon RFC 8693 (OAuth 2.0 Token Exchange) standard for programmatic token transformation and delegation chain security | Provides formal semantic foundations for programmatic token transformation and delegation chain security within distributed environments\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.984690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_14\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"fc44fe51-caf6-4e49-98c6-497bd46b4e49\",\n      \"text\": \"ClinicalTriagePolicyCard formalizes three key obligations: provide only advisory outputs supported by evidence and disclaimers, escalate any red-flag condition to qualified personnel or emergency services, and deny any autonomous diagnosis or prescription\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.814196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_19\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ce770419-1c35-453d-90f5-7152f01d8ee6\",\n      \"text\": \"Agent identifies supply chain risk from unverified supplier not explicitly covered by Rule R4, demonstrating normative generalization through LLM reasoning rather than deterministic rule-matching | Involving: Cletus (agent), Rule R4 | Key innovation: governance embedded in LLM reasoning enables normative generalization beyond explicit rule conditions\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"experience\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.078393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_27\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"f96a6ac4-9239-41cf-a824-ad10cf5d869b\",\n      \"text\": \"Valid to timestamp must be greater than or equal to valid from timestamp, and retention periods must exceed review cadence\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.824196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_9\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"e424c3cc-a088-4727-ab5e-5e4f0106affa\",\n      \"text\": \"PolicyCards act as structured metadata describing both operational policy and its cryptographic verification envelope\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.814196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_25\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"e3d6a13e-b402-4747-aaf5-7ca25f44c03e\",\n      \"text\": \"Autonomous AI agents are transitioning from passive conversational assistants into high-stakes delegated workloads executing consequential tasks on behalf of human principals.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"4d0ba11c-530d-4408-aa01-26fce57e9883\",\n      \"text\": \"Autonomous AI agents are transitioning from passive conversational assistants into high-stakes delegated workloads executing consequential tasks on behalf of human principals.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_16\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c7f73850-8058-4de1-b6d9-311d443326f6\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound is a modular runtime governance and behavioral accountability framework for autonomous agents | Establishes behavioral governance as distinct from identity federation, access control, or training-time model alignment\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_14\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"1a1552cc-5a3a-488c-97be-1ae7df0d6873\",\n      \"text\": \"Adaptive governance research aims to create dynamic constitutions capable of updating enforcement constraints in response to observed agent drift without invalidating cryptographic provenance.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.994690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_16\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"83a18411-f4cf-42ee-bfc3-847b2a9b4aee\",\n      \"text\": \"The framework unifies four principals into a non-bypassable governance pipeline: Owner defines intent profile IO and authorizes delegation, Agent proposes actions, AgentBound Service enforces joint multi-authority policy M, Site Resource Provider hosts target resources; the pipeline sequentially evaluates, logs, and validates agent behaviors before execution, with security guarantees assuming strict operational sequence where governance evaluation occurs non-bypassably prior to execution\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.014690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"0159c929-ee2e-453e-929d-b579bdb8fc24\",\n      \"text\": \"Controls section defines explicit action rules structured as ABAC tuples, each linking directly to evidence fields enumerated in the card: kyc status, risk score, device trust level, beneficiary screening score, escalation id, ensuring every decision is auditable | Involving: Cletus (AI agent), PolicyCard system\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.834196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_16\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"41025ece-357f-4d52-8e42-d167004a09f4\",\n      \"text\": \"Verifying a receipt requires only the artifact payload, corresponding public verification keys, and historical governance artifacts fetched via the receipt's stored references through a validation sequence comprising cryptographic integrity verification, governance reconstruction, and deterministic decision consistency check. | Involving: external verifying entities | Enables asynchronous, untrusted entity validation of policy compliance without requiring real-time agent presence\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.024690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_9\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"caab4851-86fb-43b7-8aac-3dbbfc844b01\",\n      \"text\": \"Pre-Action Governance Reasoning Loop (PA-GRL) proposed as formal mechanism through which agents consult structured governance rule sets before every consequential action, determining whether to proceed, self-correct, or escalate to human oversight, mirroring human deliberative compliance behavior | Involving: agents/researchers | To formalize human-like compliance behavior in AI agent governance\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.088393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_3\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c6c69a12-a267-4249-97d0-f8143486d199\",\n      \"text\": \"The algebraic composition of governance decisions yields four fundamental system properties: authorization preservation, behavioral independence, obligation separation, and replay verifiability. | Represents the guaranteed behavioral guarantees of the AgentBound governance framework.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.984690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_7\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"56b62400-7c29-48b3-a728-ec4b13e97a82\",\n      \"text\": \"Only suppliers present in the verified supplier registry may be contacted because unverified suppliers introduce supply chain and compliance risk | Unverified suppliers introduce supply chain and compliance risk\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.098393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_22\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"b4e51bad-15c5-4172-bef7-e9f2aeb3c8d7\",\n      \"text\": \"Assurance mappings reference NIST (GOVERN-1, MAP-1, MEASURE-1, MANAGE-1, MANAGE-3), ISO42001 (4,8,9,10), and EU AI Act (AnnexIV-3,4,6,9, Art72) for programmatic traceability.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.834196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"7725ee7c-c8d0-4d78-ac9a-a6a6058fd260\",\n      \"text\": \"Framework positions Policy Cards as foundation for autonomous assurance ecosystems where policies are computational, verifiable, and privacy-preserving.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.894196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_26\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"6df9eb59-a12e-484d-8206-21ee84f52653\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound framework integrates three governance authorities (delegated authorization, owner-signed behavioral constitutions, and site action contracts) into a unified multi-authority decision engine for autonomous systems\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_17\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c644676b-1322-439b-8ff4-e09b1dd455e6\",\n      \"text\": \"Traditional identity verification and resource-level access control are insufficient to secure execution perimeters for autonomous agents; a runtime governance layer is needed to determine whether specific actions should occur under given circumstances.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.974690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_16\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"2874a259-3888-463d-9d5e-414e8d41461d\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound introduces standing delegation model that cleanly decouples long-term user authorization from short-lived runtime execution authority for persistent autonomous agents operating without continuous human supervision. | Involving: persistent agents + user authorization | Addresses structural limitation of traditional session-oriented authorization that assumes human presence during transaction initiation\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.994690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_9\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"6ae98d7f-93a9-40cb-86b2-2fce61facff8\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound is implemented as a decoupled, runtime governance layer positioned directly before action execution, serving as a non-bypassable governance checkpoint that every consequential action must pass prior to target system mutation. | Establishes the architectural pattern for out-of-band validation of agent actions.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.994690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_7\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"24515944-a2ee-4e84-a169-c54cebea0f78\",\n      \"text\": \"Formal Runtime Enforcement uses deterministic pipeline to synthesize complementary judgments from independent authorities through conservative decision algebra before action execution\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.984690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_2\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"412755b8-775c-4002-89f0-4f58a9562c18\",\n      \"text\": \"Obligations include user notices (fees/limits), explicit consent recording, escalation protocol enforcement, and audit-trail maintenance | Involving: system | Framework requirements for compliance and traceability\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.824196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_18\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"26737e50-b69b-4fbb-b85f-56cee391b604\",\n      \"text\": \"Both humans and autonomous AI agents interact with their environments through the same mechanism where a reasoning source produces a natural language expression of intent that drives action, analogous to humans formulating instructions directed toward a task and AI agents formulating prompts directed toward an LLM\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.118393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_6\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"087da0a8-6b24-4099-83b9-5f222a324e3e\",\n      \"text\": \"Situational rules are stored as conditional entries with activation predicates; the governance server evaluates these predicates against runtime context signals (such as supplier disruption flag, active audit period, or elevated risk classification) to dynamically include matching rules in retrieval responses.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.088393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_19\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"6140b11f-4488-4a31-aafc-96bb9ad59836\",\n      \"text\": \"The reasoning trace log is queryable through the MCP interface, enabling human operators to inspect governance decisions in real time and supporting post-hoc compliance audit and review.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.108393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_19\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"aae10560-5efd-4918-a840-ba56be792392\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound addresses situations where fully authenticated and legitimately authorized agents execute actions violating principal intent while remaining within delegated access control scope | Demonstrates behavioral governance failures differ from access control breaches\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.994690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_14\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"5b29fff7-d4db-4bce-a7f3-0f6c62489bf6\",\n      \"text\": \"The Policy Card schema is formally specified using JSON Schema 2020-12, defining mandatory fields including required top-level keys, permitted data types, pattern constraints, and enumerations governing how valid cards must be authored and validated, with additionalProperties: false preventing unspecified properties.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.914196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"6adfdf6d-4592-4ade-9534-16646fefb0c0\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound isolates behavior at the action perimeter rather than filtering cognitive model inputs, rendering it incapable of directly intercepting prompt injection, jailbreaks, or internal adversarial model manipulation | When: 2026-09-06 | Involving: AgentBound framework\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.004690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_15\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"0bef11c9-21a3-4b35-852e-408f35185b30\",\n      \"text\": \"In collaborative scenarios (e.g., Clinical Trial Coordinator), agents exchange digital attestations representing partial fulfillment of obligations (e.g., data anonymization, consent verification, statistical integrity), verifiable by peers and aggregable into a composite assurance graph enabling federated compliance | Involving: AI agents in collaborative scenarios | Enables federated compliance where trust emerges from a network of mutually validating agents\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.834196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_24\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c8b164c1-2307-4e8c-a04d-1d684218f37d\",\n      \"text\": \"Governance frameworks must incorporate tamper-resistance mechanisms to protect rule integrity against adversarial inputs | Involving: design requirement\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.118393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_11\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"b90a0113-cf8a-4db5-bf2c-30ca8d64327c\",\n      \"text\": \"The framework achieved 95% compliance decision accuracy (38/40 correct decisions) across 40 evaluation runs, with two errors from edge-case input phrasings producing ambiguous permissibility reasoning | Involving: the framework\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:30:58.088393+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2604.25684v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2604.25684v1.pdf_25\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"8c03b367-8fac-4b70-908b-17a0cbb698d0\",\n      \"text\": \"Validates that every rule in controls uses permitted effect tokens (allow, deny, or require escalation) preventing logically inconsistent or incomplete policy definitions\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.834196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_10\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"09f2e51c-982e-4781-915f-e25f3e58c04d\",\n      \"text\": \"Two-phase countersigning protocol: first, requesting agent signs constructed receipt payload using its private asymmetric key; second, AgentBound enforcement service intercepts and countersigns the entire block covering core receipt payload, agent's signature, and terminal decision vector. | Involving: requesting agent + AgentBound enforcement service | Ensures accountability binding and invalidates verification chain if out-of-band modifications occur to underlying action payload or intermediate governance evaluation\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.974690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_9\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"4a71566e-6bd0-4445-9378-0e1a9bbe3c92\",\n      \"text\": \"The Policy Card framework enables verifiable compliance for autonomous agents through automatic validation, version control, and integration with runtime enforcement or continuous-audit pipelines, forming a foundation for distributed assurance in multi-agent ecosystems | Involving: autonomous agents\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.834196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_0\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"f37c14f6-560c-44e6-bd8a-0fd60f5a3098\",\n      \"text\": \"Receipt generation proceeds via a deterministic four-stage pipeline: evaluation, raw payload construction, two-phase ordered countersigning protocol, and verification architecture enabling asynchronous policy compliance validation by external untrusted entities. | Involving: system architecture | Establishes the complete receipt generation and verification process with five core security invariants\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.964690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_9\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d8849b46-627f-4b04-93df-0900883c23a1\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound enforces deterministic compliance at the system runtime boundary rather than optimizing model weights at training time, focusing on verifiable system accountability rather than statistical behavioral shaping | Involving: AgentBound\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.984690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_13\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"029b038b-467e-4e49-b552-f72e76fb3104\",\n      \"text\": \"Five core security invariants yielded by the verification architecture: integrity, non-repudiation, policy provenance, replay verifiability, and decision transparency. | Involving: system architecture | Defines the security properties guaranteed by the receipt verification system\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.984690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_9\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"7aa44718-fe39-4e17-873e-0b7fab2170fb\",\n      \"text\": \"Validates consistency between sections by cross-checking evidence fields listed in monitoring against those referenced under obligations or controls\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.824196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_10\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"1acc06f1-e5fb-4d88-91c7-7cacb3ae3467\",\n      \"text\": \"Policy Cards are JSON-structured documents with semantic versioning (X.Y.Z) enabling traceable updates and diff-based analysis for auditors to verify what changed between policy revisions.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.814196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_6\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d28afb9c-cac8-4486-ae03-f2fbad8a8192\",\n      \"text\": \"Full schema and validator available in public repository and archived via Zenodo (DOI: 10.5281/zenodo.17464706)\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.844196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_10\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"31e84f05-37b4-44ea-90bc-428e742c36e4\",\n      \"text\": \"Each schema section can be traced to clauses/functions within frameworks, enabling automated validation of compliance claims\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.824196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_4\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"5712001a-8a47-404e-8490-f4d28b9ae781\",\n      \"text\": \"Monitoring defines loggable events, data fields, detectors, and thresholds with minimum retention >=1 day and review cadence >=1 day, linking operational telemetry with audit evidence.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.854196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"f9e87021-301e-4be2-92ca-cbd1e194fa4b\",\n      \"text\": \"Behavioral adversary Abeh manipulates authorized agents into executing actions violating Owner's intent while remaining within delegated permission scope\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.974690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_5\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"1267ec72-9d5c-487b-8b1c-71e29946a8fa\",\n      \"text\": \"Operational rules in Table 3 translate triage obligations into machine-verifiable conditions based on vitals present, risk level, confidence score, red flag status, patient age, and symptom presence (e.g., chest pain)\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T05:31:09.824196+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2510.24383v1.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2510.24383v1.pdf_19\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"6fe42293-0d42-4fa8-9c5f-2f364271cdf1\",\n      \"text\": \"Automatic constitution refresh: runtime requests latest constitution version from Constitution Service before task materialization; task token encapsulates constitution hash, enabling automatic policy propagation without manual reauthorization | Involving: Cletus\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"experience\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.984690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_10\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"f249bcfb-ac2d-4aac-9325-247e6ea3305f\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound evaluates candidate tool invocations non-bypassably before execution, using formal decision algebra to compose intermediate judgments conservatively\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"world\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:42.974690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": \"2606.30970v2.pdf\",\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": \"Cletus_2606.30970v2.pdf_17\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"e7fc775d-ca3a-41c5-9213-52c24ef235bb\",\n      \"text\": \"AgentBound's enforcement layer efficacy depends on the precision and quality of underlying constitutions and site action contracts.\",\n      \"fact_type\": \"observation\",\n      \"entities\": null,\n      \"context\": null,\n      \"occurred_start\": null,\n      \"occurred_end\": null,\n      \"mentioned_at\": \"2026-09-06T04:54:43.014690+00:00\",\n      \"document_id\": null,\n      \"metadata\": {},\n      \"chunk_id\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"source_fact_ids\": null\n    }\n  ],\n  \"trace\": null,\n  \"entities\": null,\n  \"chunks\": null,\n  \"source_facts\": null\n}"
  }
}
